package id.demonpalace.tuntas

/**
 * Question packs taken from practice files Nopal shared (Kompeten TKA paket 100 soal,
 * Pusmendik-style B. Inggris sample, and a B. Inggris worksheet). Generated, edit with care.
 * Each pack sits in its own function so no single method grows past the JVM size limit.
 */
object Bank {

    private fun kompetenBinRaw() = listOf(
        Question("kp1", "Kata serapan dari bahasa asing yang terdapat pada teks tersebut adalah…", listOf("Ekosistem, efisien, reseptor, predator, populasi", "Reseptor, efisien, ekosistem, rantai ma kanan, fokus", "Efisien, sensitif, populasi, serangga, rantai makanan", "Reseptor, sensitif, krustasea, pemangsa, ekosistem", "Populasi, rantai makanan, efisien, krus tasea, focus"), 0, "Kata serapan asing di teks: ekosistem (ecosystem), efisien (efficient), reseptor (receptor), predator, populasi (population). Pilihan lain memuat kata asli Indonesia seperti rantai makanan, serangga, pemangsa.", passage = "Platipus memiliki ciri khas tubuh yang unik. Tubuhnya ditutupi oleh bulu yang lembut dan kedap air, yang melindunginya dari suhu dingin saat berenang di perairan. Paruhnya mirip dengan paruh bebek dan dilengkapi dengan reseptor yang sensitif terhadap peru bahan suhu dan gerakan, membantu platipus dalam mencari makanan di dasar sungai atau danau. Kaki berselaputnya memungkinkan platipus untuk berenang dengan cepat dan efisien. Platipus adalah hewan pemangsa yang makan berbagai jenis makanan, termasuk serangga, cacing, dan krustasea. Mereka mencari ma kan dengan cara meraba-raba dasar perairan menggunakan paruh mereka yang sensitif. Platipus memiliki kemampuan untuk menutup mata, telinga, dan hidungnya saat berada di bawah air, sehingga mereka dapat fokus pada pencarian makanan tanpa gangguan. Platipus memiliki peranan penting dalam ekosistem tempat tinggalnya. Mereka membantu mengontrol populasi serangga dan krustasea, yang dapat memengaruhi keseimbangan ekosistem perairan. Selain itu, platipus juga menjadi bagian dari rantai makanan sebagai mangsa bagi predator seperti ular dan burung pemangsa. Sumber: ruangguru.com"),
        Question("kp2", "Objek utama yang dibicarakan dalam kutipan editorial tersebut adalah…", listOf("Data statistik (jumlah korban, bangunan rusak, titik banjir) sebagai alat evaluasi bencana.", "Tata ruang dan kebijakan publik terkait pembangunan serta mitigasi bencana di Bali.", "Komunikasi pemerintah dan cara publik merespons peringatan dini sebelum banjir.", "Korban jiwa, pengungsi, dan kerugian materil dari banjir Bali 2025.", "Kerusakan infrastruktur dan banyaknya bangunan yang rusak akibat banjir di Bali."), 1, "Judul dan kalimat inti editorial menekankan bahwa banjir adalah persoalan tata ruang dan kebijakan publik/mitigasi; data korban hanya pendukung.", passage = "Banjir Bali 2025: Bias Komunikasi Kebijakan dan Krisis Ekosistem Banjir besar yang melanda Bali pada dini hari hingga siang 10 September 2025 menjadi alarm keras bahwa bencana bukan hanya persoalan curah hujan, tetapi juga persoalan tata ruang, kebijakan publik, dan cara komunikasi pemerintah kepada warganya. Data Badan Penanggulangan Bencana Daerah (BPBD) Bali hingga 12 September mencatat sedikit nya 17 orang meninggal, ada koreksi pencatatan ganda karena sebelumnya 18 orang meninggal. Untuk korban hilang masih ada lima orang lagi dalam pencarian dan ratusan orang mengungsi di Denpasar, Jembrana, dan Badung. Lebih dari 500 bangunan rusak, termasuk Pasar Kumbasari dan kios-kios di Jalan Sulawesi, dengan total kerugian material yang ditaksir mendekati Rp29 miliar. Infrastruktur pun porak-poranda: jembatan putus, tembok pembatas jebol, dan 160 titik banjir ditemukan di seluruh Bali. Hal ini bukan sekadar peristiwa cuaca ekstrem, melainkan peringatan bahwa tata kelola ruang dan kebijakan mitigasi ben cana menghadapi ujian besar."),
        Question("kp3", "Manakah informasi yang sesuai dengan kutipan teks tersebut?", listOf("Peningkatan suhu permukaan laut dapat menurunkan kelembapan udara dan curah hujan esktrem.", "Dampak perubahan iklim hanya berpengaruh pada sektor lingkungan dan tidak memengaruhi kesehatan manusia.", "Banjir dan erosi merupakan salah satu dampak yang dapat muncul akibat perubahan iklim di satu wilayah tertentu.", "BMKG menyarankan adaptasi dengan memperkuat sistem peringatan dini dan memperbaiki sistem drainase.", "Perubahan iklim tidak berhubungan dengan gangguan terhadap infrastruktur."), 3, "Teks menyebut BMKG menyarankan drainase lebih baik dan penguatan sistem peringatan dini. Pilihan A, B, E bertentangan dengan teks.", passage = "Perubahan iklim ditandai dengan perubahan pola suhu permukaan laut dan atmosfer yang menyebabkan peningkatan kelembapan udara serta curah hujan yang ekstrem di beberapa lokasi. BMKG memprediksi bahwa peningkat an uap air akibat suhu laut yang lebih hangat akan meningkatkan frekuensi hujan deras dan potensi cuaca ekstrem di masa depan. Dampaknya akan muncul di beberapa wilayah sebagai banjir, erosi, dan gangguan terhadap infrastruktur, serta peningkatan risiko kesehatan terkait suhu ekstrem dan kelembapan tinggi. Untuk mitigasi, BMKG menyarankan adaptasi melalui pembangunan sistem drainase yang lebih baik, penguatan sistem peringatan dini, serta integrasi kebijakan pengelolaan ling kungan dan tata ruang. Sumber: https://staklim-jatim.bmkg.go.id/"),
        Question("kp4", "Informasi utama dalam teks berita tersebut adalah…", listOf("Restoran Jepang dan India akan mem peroleh subsidi dari pemerintah agar bisa membeli beras impor dengan harga murah.", "Stok beras medium nasional dipastikan aman, namun pemerintah tetap akan melakukan impor untuk masyarakat umum.", "Impor beras 2025 hanya dilakukan untuk restoran tertentu karena jenis beras khusus tidak diproduksi dalam negeri.", "Pemerintah berencana memproduksi beras basmati dan beras Jepang secara massal untuk menggantikan kebutuhan impor restoran.", "Seluruh impor beras pada tahun 2025 dilarang pemerintah untuk menjaga sta bilitas harga gabah petani"), 2, "Inti berita: impor beras 2025 hanya untuk restoran tertentu karena beras khusus (basmati, Jepang) belum diproduksi dalam negeri.", passage = "Wakil Menteri Pertanian (Wamentan) Sudar yono menegaskan bahwa impor beras tahun 2025 hanya ditujukan untuk restoran tertentu, bukan untuk konsumsi masyarakat umum. Restoran Jepang, India, hingga Timur Tengah kerap membutuhkan beras dengan karakter istik khusus, seperti beras basmati dan beras Jepang, yang belum dapat dipenuhi produksi dalam negeri. Ia memastikan stok beras medi um nasional masih aman untuk memenuhi kebutuhan pokok masyarakat. Pemerintah juga menargetkan tidak akan melakukan impor beras medium sepanjang tahun 2025, sekaligus menjaga stabilitas harga gabah petani agar tetap menguntungkan. Sumber: ANTARA News dengan penyesuaian"),
        Question("kp5", "Persamaan kedua teks tersebut adalah…", listOf("Kedua teks membahas bencana alam yang terjadi di daerah perkotaan.", "Kedua teks mengulas dampak ekonomi yang ditimbulkan oleh bencana banjir dan tanah longsor secara mendalam.", "Kedua teks menguraikan bencana alam yang dipengaruhi oleh faktor alam dan tindakan manusia serta upaya pencegah annya.", "Kedua teks memaparkan peristiwa alam tanpa menyebutkan dampak yang ditim bulkan.", "Kedua teks menekankan peran pemerintah sebagai penyebab utama bencana."), 2, "Kedua teks sama-sama membahas bencana (banjir, longsor) yang dipicu faktor alam dan manusia, lalu menyebut upaya pencegahan.", passage = "Teks 1 Banjir merupakan bencana alam yang sering terjadi saat musim hujan akibat curah hujan tinggi dan berlangsung lama. Banjir disebabkan oleh faktor alam, seperti erosi, sedimentasi, dan kapasitas sungai yang terbatas, serta faktor manusia, seperti pembuangan sampah ke sungai, penggundulan hutan, dan perubahan tata guna lahan. Dampak banjir meliputi kerusakan fisik, kerugian ekonomi, dan gangguan kesehatan. Oleh karena itu, diperlukan upaya pencegahan, antara lain menjaga ke bersihan sungai, melindungi hutan, dan tidak membangun di daerah resapan air. Teks 2 Tanah longsor merupakan salah satu bencana alam yang sering terjadi di wilayah perbukitan dan pegunungan, terutama saat musim hujan. Peristiwa ini terjadi ketika massa tanah dan batuan bergerak menuruni lereng akibat hilang nya kestabilan tanah. Curah hujan yang tinggi menjadi faktor utama pemicu tanah longsor karena air yang meresap ke dalam tanah dapat mengurangi daya ikat antarpartikel tanah. Selain faktor alam, aktivitas manusia juga ber peran besar dalam terjadinya tanah longsor. Penebangan hutan secara liar menyebabkan akar pohon yang seharusnya mengikat tanah menjadi berkurang. Akibatnya, struktur tanah menjadi rapuh dan mudah bergerak saat di guyur hujan. Pembangunan permukiman di lereng curam tanpa perencanaan yang tepat juga meningkatkan risiko terjadinya longsor. Tanah longsor menimbulkan berbagai dam pak negatif, seperti rusaknya permukiman, terputusnya akses jalan, serta korban jiwa. Aktivitas ekonomi dan sosial masyarakat pun terganggu akibat bencana ini. Oleh karena itu, diperlukan upaya pencegahan, seperti reboisasi, pengaturan tata ruang wilayah, serta peningkatan kesadaran masyarakat untuk menjaga lingkungan. Dengan langkah-langkah tersebut, risiko terjadinya tanah longsor dapat dikurangi."),
        Question("kp6", "Pernyataan manakah yang paling tepat mengenai persamaan dan perbedaan gagasan inti kedua teks?", listOf("Kedua teks mengajak masyarakat ikut beradaptasi; perbedaannya teks 1 menekankan prakiraan cuaca pada musim kemarau, teks 2 lebih kepada penyesuaian infrastuktur dan sistem peringatan dini.", "Kedua teks menggambarkan kelembapan udara sebagai penyebab utama; teks 1 fokus pada jagung, kacang-kedelai, teks 2 fokus pada wilayah pesisir dan perkotaan.", "Kedua teks menekankan perlunya mitigasi drainase; perbedaannya, teks 1 menyarankan pemantauan cuaca rutin, teks 2 menyebut peringatan dini dan kebijakan tata ruang.", "Keduanya menjelaskan dampak terhadap sektor pertanian; teks 1 menyebut hama dan gagal panen, teks 2 menyebut erosi dan infrastruktur rusak.", "Kedua teks membahas pengaruh perubahan iklim terhadap pola curah hujan; perbedaannya teks 1 fokus pada kemarau basah selama musim kemarau, teks 2 berfokus pada hujan ekstrem dan panas udara akibat suhu laut tinggi."), 4, "Topik bersama: pengaruh iklim pada pola hujan. Teks 1 fokus kemarau basah, teks 2 fokus hujan ekstrem akibat suhu laut yang menghangat.", passage = "Kutipan 1 Musim kemarau basah adalah fenomena ke tika hujan masih turun secara berkala meski sudah memasuki musim kemarau. BMKG menyebut bahwa kondisi ini dipicu oleh dinamika atmosfer regional dan global, seperti suhu muka laut yang hangat, angin monsun aktif, serta pengaruh La Nina dan Indian Ocean Dipole yang negatif. Dampak kemarau basah terasa di sektor pertanian karena lahan menjadi lembap, yang kadang menyebabkan gagal panen pada komoditas jagung, kacang- kacang an, dan kedelai. Selain itu, penyakit dan hama lebih mudah berkembang dalam kondisi lembap, dan aktivitas pertanian menjadi sulit direncanakan. Untuk mengantisipasi fenomena ini, BMKG menyarankan pemantauan rutin cuaca dan iklim, memperbaiki drainase, serta menyampaikan informasi prakiraan cuaca yang akurat kepada masyarakat. Sumber: https://gaw-bariri.bmkg.go.id Kutipan 2 Perubahan iklim ditandai dengan perubahan pola suhu permukaan laut dan atmosfer yang menyebabkan peningkatan kelembapan udara serta curah hujan yang ekstrem di beberapa lokasi. BMKG memprediksi bahwa peningkat an uap air akibat suhu laut yang lebih hangat akan meningkatkan frekuensi hujan deras dan potensi cuaca ekstrem di masa depan. Dampaknya akan muncul di beberapa wilayah sebagai banjir, erosi, dan gangguan terhadap infrastruktur, serta peningkatan risiko kesehatan terkait suhu ekstrem dan kelembapan tinggi. Untuk mitigasi, BMKG menyarankan adaptasi melalui pembangunan sistem drainase yang lebih baik, penguatan sistem peringatan dini, serta integrasi kebijakan pengelolaan lingkungan dan tata ruang. Sumber: https://staklim-jatim.bmkg.go.id/"),
        Question("kp7", "Jika kebijakan dalam teks berjalan dengan baik, kondisi yang mungkin terjadi pada sektor pendidikan adalah…", listOf("Peningkatan kompetensi tenaga pendidik melalui program pelatihan yang didanai negara.", "Peningkatan kompetensi tenaga pendidik yang terhambat akibat pengurangan anggaran pendidikan.", "Perluasan akses pendidikan di salah satu jenjang melalui pemanfaatan anggaran yang optimal.", "Perluasan akses pendidikan yang terbatas karena prioritas anggaran dialihkan ke sektor lain.", "Menurunnya kualitas sarana dan prasarana pendidikan untuk menunjang pembelajaran."), 0, "Anggaran pendidikan besar untuk SDM unggul paling mungkin berdampak pada program peningkatan kompetensi tenaga pendidik.", passage = "Pemerintah melalui Kementerian Keuangan telah menetapkan Rancangan Anggaran Pendapatan dan Belanja Negara (RAPBN) Tahun Anggaran 2025 dengan fokus utama pada pembangunan Sumber Daya Manusia (SDM) unggul. Dalam RAPBN 2025, anggaran pen didikan dialokasikan sebesar Rp722,6 triliun, yang sebagian besar akan digunakan untuk program-program pendidikan dasar hingga perguruan tinggi. Selain itu, pemerintah juga mengalokasikan dana untuk peningkatan kualitas kesehatan, infrastruktur, dan program-program sosial lainnya. Fokus utama ini bertujuan untuk menciptakan SDM yang berkualitas, produktif, dan memiliki daya saing tinggi di tingkat global. Pemerintah berharap dengan alokasi anggaran yang tepat, pemba ngunan SDM unggul dapat tercapai dan men dukung pertumbuhan ekonomi yang inklusif dan berkelanjutan."),
        Question("kp8", "Berdasarkan teks tersebut, apa dampak yang mungkin terjadi pada seseorang yang ingin menjadi penulis?", listOf("Penulis pemula akan bersemangat menulis karena pasti menjadi orang yang sukses.", "Orang tidak akan ragu untuk memulai menulis karena ada fakta bahwa penulis tidak harus berpendidikan sastra.", "Orang miskin yang punya keinginan menulis akan mulai menulis karena penulis harus berasal dari keluarga kaya.", "Orang tidak bisa menekuni hobi menulis jika bekerja di bidang lain, karena menjadi penulis tidak bisa dilakukan bersamaan dengan profesi utama.", "Orang akan ragu untuk menulis karena ternyata untuk menjadi penulis membutuhkan waktu berproses yang lama."), 1, "Tere Liye kuliah akuntansi tetapi menjadi penulis, jadi orang tak perlu ragu menulis meski bukan lulusan sastra.", passage = "Darwis atau yang lebih kita kenal sebagai ‘Tere Liye’ dilahirkan di sebuah kota kecil di Provinsi Sumatra Selatan, tepatnya, yaitu Kota Lahat pada tanggal 21 Mei 1979. Darwis bukanlah seorang anak yang lahir dari sebuah keluarga kaya raya. Orang tuanya sehari-hari memiliki mata pencaharian sebagai petani dengan di karuniai banyak anak. Dia diketahui merupa kan anak keenam dari tujuh bersaudara. Meskipun begitu, orang tua Tere Liye mendidik dan membesarkan anaknya sehingga tumbuh sebagai pribadi yang pintar dan cerdas. Tere Liye banyak menghabiskan masa kecilnya di kampung halamannya. Semasa menginjak usia masuk sekolah, Tere Liye mengenyam pendidikan dasar di Sekolah Dasar Negeri 2 Kikim Timur, Kecamatan Kikim Timur. Kemudian, Tere Liye melanjutkan ke jenjang pendidikan tingkat menengah di SMP Negeri 2 Kikim yang juga terletak di wilayah Kabupaten Lahat. Setelah mulai menginjak usia Sekolah Menengah Atas, Tere Liye mulai keluar dari kampung halamannya untuk meneruskan pendidikannya di SMA Negeri 9 Bandar Lampung, Provinsi Lampung. Kehidupannya di Bandar Lampung telah membuat sosok Tere Liye menjadi seorang yang haus akan ilmu. Selanjutnya, Tere Liye memutuskan untuk melanjutkan pendidikan ke jenjang lebih tinggi lagi. Dia ingin mengenyam pendidikan tinggi terbaik yang di Indonesia. Maksud dari keinginannya tersebut adalah kuliah di Universitas Indonesia atau disingkat UI. Pada akhirnya, Tere Liye berhasil mewujudkan mimpinya tersebut. Tere Liye secara resmi di terima sebagai mahasiswa baru di Universitas Indonesia (UI). Sebagai seorang penulis novel yang erat kaitannya dengan program studi sastra, ternyata banyak orang yang tidak mengetahui bahwa Tere Liye merupakan mahasiswa dari Jurusan Akuntansi di Fakultas Ekonomi UI. Setelah menyelesaikan kuliahnya, Tere Liye ternyata tidak bekerja di sebuah perusahaan yang memiliki keterkaitan dengan dunia sastra atau kepenulisan. Tere Liye awalnya bekerja sebagai seorang akuntan di sebuah perusaha an. Hal ini pun sesuai dengan latar belakang pendidikannya, yaitu akuntansi. Sumber: gramedia.com"),
        Question("kp9", "Berdasarkan kutipan biografi Pramoedya Ananta Toer tersebut, manakah dampak peristiwa dalam hidup Pramoedya terhadap kehidupan manusia yang tepat?", listOf("Penahanan politik yang dialami Pramoedya menginspirasi masyarakat untuk menghargai pentingnya kebebasan berekspresi.", "Pembatasan kebebasan membuat karya Pramoedya menjadi tidak dikenal oleh masyarakat luas.", "Karya Pramoedya yang mengangkat keadilan sosial kurang memotivasi aktivis dalam memperjuangkan perubahan masyarakat.", "Kritik Pramoedya terhadap pemerintah menyebabkan karya-karyanya hanya relevan di masa lalu saja.", "Pramoedya menjadi suara kelompok kalangan atas dan memberi inspirasi perjuangan sosial sampai sekarang."), 0, "Penahanan dan keteguhan Pramoedya membuat karyanya menginspirasi orang untuk menghargai kebebasan berekspresi. Pilihan E salah karena ia suara kelompok terpinggirkan, bukan kalangan atas.", passage = "Pramoedya Ananta Toer (1925–2006) adalah sastrawan Indonesia yang sangat berpengaruh, dikenal lewat karya-karyanya yang menyoroti tema kemanusiaan, keadilan sosial, dan perjuangan bangsa. Ia mengalami masa penahanan politik selama rezim Orde Baru akibat kritiknya terhadap pemerintah yang dianggap kontroversial. Meskipun berada di bawah tekanan dan pembatasan kebebasan, karya-karya Pramoedya tetap diterbitkan dan dikenal luas oleh masyarakat. Hal ini menunjukkan keteguhan dan semangatnya untuk terus berkarya meski menghadapi rintangan besar. Karya-karya Pramoedya memberikan inspirasi yang kuat bagi banyak aktivis sosial dan pembaca yang peduli pada hak asasi ma nusia dan kebebasan berekspresi. Ia dianggap sebagai suara bagi kelompok- kelompok yang terpinggirkan dan terus memberi pengaruh positif dalam perjuangan sosial sampai saat ini. Melalui tulisan- tulisannya, Pramoedya memotivasi banyak orang untuk memperju angkan keadilan dan kebebasan, meskipun menghadapi tantangan politik dan sosial yang kompleks. Pengaruh karya dan perjuangannya tetap relevan bagi kehidupan masyarakat modern di Indonesia. (Sumber: disarikan dari berbagai sumber dengan penyesuaian)"),
        Question("kp10", "Kalimat yang tidak berkaitan dengan gagasan utama paragraf tersebut adalah…", listOf("(2)", "(3)", "(4)", "(5)", "(7)"), 3, "Gagasan utama: literasi digital ASN. Kalimat (5) tentang kegiatan olahraga tidak berkaitan.", passage = "Kemendikbudristek terus berupaya mening katkan literasi digital di kalangan Aparatur Sipil Negara (ASN) melalui berbagai program pelatihan. (2) Salah satu inisiatif utama adalah penyelenggaraan Webinar Literasi Digital yang diikuti oleh lebih dari 80.000 ASN dari berbagai unit kerja. (3) Pelatihan ini bertujuan untuk membekali ASN dengan empat dimensi literasi digital, di antaranya keterampilan digital, etika digital, budaya digital, dan keamanan digital. (4) Dengan pemahaman yang mendalam tentang dimensi-dimensi ini, diharapkan ASN dapat mengoptimalkan penggunaan teknologi dalam pelayanan publik. (5) Kemendikbudristek juga mengadakan berbagai kegiatan olahraga untuk meningkatkan kebugar an ASN. (6) Melalui platform e-Learning, ASN dapat mengakses materi pelatihan kapan saja dan di mana saja. (7) Inisiatif ini sejalan dengan komitmen Kemendikbudristek untuk menciptakan lingkungan kerja yang adaptif terhadap perkembangan teknologi."),
        Question("kp12", "Penggunaan diksi konotatif dari puisi tersebut adalah…", listOf("Kalau sampai waktuku", "Aku mau tak seorang kan merayu", "Aku ini binatang jalang", "Luka dan bisa kubawa berlari", "Aku mau hidup seribu tahun lagi"), 2, "Diksi konotatif = makna kias. \"Binatang jalang\" bukan binatang sungguhan, tetapi kiasan untuk pribadi yang bebas dan tak mau diatur.", passage = "Aku — Chairil Anwar\n\nKalau sampai waktuku\nAku mau tak seorang kan merayu\nTidak juga kau\nTak perlu sedu sedan itu\nAku ini binatang jalang\nDari kumpulannya terbuang\nBiar peluru menembus kulitku\nAku tetap meradang menerjang\nLuka dan bisa kubawa berlari\nBerlari\nHingga hilang pedih peri\nDan aku akan lebih tidak peduli\nAku mau hidup seribu tahun lagi"),
        Question("kp13", "Dari teks tersebut, kosakata dan kalimat manakah yang paling tepat menggambarkan karakter Aku sebagai sosok yang berhati-hati dalam mengambil keputusan?", listOf("“Aku terdiam selama beberapa saat, ber upaya memahami arti di balik pertanyaan Rudi yang sebenarnya.”", "“Pikiranku melayang ke segala janji yang terdengar seperti lagu lama.”", "“Kami bertemu secara tidak sengaja, teta pi percakapan yang kemudian mengalir terasa seperti disengaja.”", "“Tatapannya tak pernah teralihkan dari cangkir kopi.”", "“Kami duduk dalam keheningan sesaat.”"), 0, "Terdiam sambil berupaya memahami arti pertanyaan menunjukkan Aku berhati-hati sebelum memutuskan.", passage = "Berjarak setengah meter dari keberadaanku, Rudi, rekan kerja sekaligus tetanggaku, duduk ditemani secangkir kopi hitam berwarna pekat. Wajahnya bersemangat, ada semacam gairah yang berkecambah dan tumbuh tanpa suara. Kami bertemu secara tidak sengaja, tetapi percakapan yang kemudian mengalir terasa seperti disengaja. “Jadi, kamu mau milih siapa? Nomor satu, dua, atau tiga?” tanya Rudi kepadaku, tanpa menoleh, tatapannya lekat pada cangkir kopi yang baru saja diangkat dan disesapnya penuh nikmat. “Jangan bilang bahwa semua pilihan sama saja, kecuali kamu memang tidak punya cukup informasi sampai akhirnya berkata demikian.” Aku terdiam selama beberapa saat, berupaya memahami arti di balik pertanyaan Rudi yang sebenarnya. Pikiranku melayang ke segala janji yang terdengar seperti lagu lama, kata- kata yang dilemparkan ke udara tanpa pernah benar-benar mengakar. Rudi menghela napas, lalu berkata, “Mungkin kamu memang sudah terlalu lelah untuk berharap banyak dari politik. Tapi, jangan pernah berhenti mencoba memahami, setidaknya untuk diri sendiri.” Tatapannya tak pernah teralihkan dari cangkir kopi, tetapi aku merasakan ada sesuatu yang lebih dari sekadar kopi yang ia nikmati, sebuah keyakinan yang dalam, walau tak banyak ter ucap. Kami duduk dalam keheningan sesaat, lalu aku mulai merasakan sesuatu yang sebelumnya tidak pernah kusadari: bahwa pertemuan ini bukan hanya soal pilihan politik, melainkan juga tentang keberanian memilih dan berpendirian."),
        Question("kp14", "Isi kutipan cerpen di atas adalah…", listOf("Indo sudah sangat letih merawat Ambe", "Yang dimiliki Aku dan Indo hanyalah tongkonan", "Ambe punya harta untuk perayaan kematiannya", "Sebenarnya Ambe dulu kaya, tetapi anak- anaknya serakah", "Aku ingin segera mendapatkan uang untuk membiayai upacara kematian Indo"), 1, "Teks menyebut \"Cuma tongkonan ini yang kami punya\". Pilihan E salah karena upacara kematian itu untuk Ambe, bukan Indo.", passage = "Sering kulihat rona wajahnya tak ada duka meski ia sudah lama berkabung. Mungkin karena itu hatinya tak lagi berkabut. Menjalani hari dengan bahagia walau keadaan seperti ini. Ia mengantar kepergianku sampai depan pintu. Aku tahu, ia selalu menaruh harap agar aku cepat dapat uang untuk upacara kematian Ambe. Letihkah Indo merawat Ambe?. Cuma tongkonan ini yang kami punya atau yang tersisa. Indo hanya istri kedua Ambe. Katanya, dulu banyak kerabat tidak setuju ketika mereka menikah dan kakak-kakak tiriku menerima dengan syarat menuntut pembagian harta sebagai ahli waris mendiang ibu mereka. Sekarang, Ambe tak memiliki harta peninggalan, bahkan buat perayaan kemati annya sendiri. Anak-anaknya terdahulu pun seperti tak peduli. Tinggallah aku dan Indo yang menanggung beban. Berat, entah sampai kapan kami mampu menahan. (Ambe Masih Sakit, Emil Amir)"),
        Question("kp15", "Tema utama dari puisi tersebut adalah…", listOf("Semangat belajar dan usaha meraih cita cita di masa depan.", "Tekad kuat seorang pelajar dalam menghadapi hari-hari sekolah.", "Harapan dan optimisme untuk membangun masa depan yang lebih baik.", "Perjuangan menuntut ilmu sebagai bekal kehidupan kelak.", "Kedisiplinan siswa dalam menjalani rutinitas pendidikan."), 0, "Puisi berisi semangat bangun pagi, belajar, dan menuntut ilmu sebagai jembatan menuju cita-cita.", passage = "Aku dan Masa Depanku — Ulil Albab Af-Farizi\n\nKetika sang mentari menampakkan sinarnya\nDiiringi kicauan burung yang menyapa\nDetik demi detik yang berbunyi\nMembangunkanku untuk menggapai cita\nBuku-buku yang memandangku\nSeolah tak rela menenggelamkan dalam angan\nKutatap mentari dan berkata\nAku siap demi masa depanku\nSemangat yang membara\nMembangkitkan jiwa dan raga\nLonceng sekolah yang memanggil\nAdalah awal mengumpulkan ilmu\nMenuntut ilmu\nIalah candu bagiku\nMenambah kecerdasan\nDan menjadi jembatan\nAkan cita-citaku"),
        Question("kp16", "Berdasarkan dialog tersebut, dapat disimpul kan bahwa watak Dito adalah…", listOf("Rajin dan displin", "Kurang bertanggung jawab terhadap tugas", "Pemalu dan pendiam", "Sabar dan rendah hati", "Penurut dan patuh"), 1, "Dito santai, lupa, dan belum menyelesaikan tugas yang sudah diingatkan sejak minggu lalu → kurang bertanggung jawab.", passage = "Rani: “Ssst…Bu Maya datang!”\nBu Maya: (Para siswa segera duduk rapi) “Selamat pagi, Anak-anak.”\nAnak-anak: “Selamat pagi, Bu!”\nBu Maya: “Hari ini Ibu akan mengumpulkan tugas ringkasan bacaan. Semua sudah siap?”\nAnak-anak: “Sudah, Bu.”\nBu Maya: “Dito, mana tugasmu?”\nDito: (santai) “Ada, Bu… tapi belum selesai.”\nBu Maya: “Kenapa belum selesai?”\nDito: “Saya kira bisa dikumpulkan besok, Bu.”\nSalsa: “Bu, tugasnya dikumpulkan hari ini.”\nBu Maya: “Dito, Ibu sudah mengingatkan sejak minggu lalu.”\nDito: (mengangkat bahu) “Saya lupa, Bu.”\nBu Maya: “Melalaikan tugas adalah bentuk kurang tanggung jawab.”\nDito: (menunduk) “Maaf, Bu. Saya salah.”\nBu Maya: “Ibu beri kamu kesempatan mengerjakan ulang, tapi ini jadi pelajaran.”\nDito: “Iya, Bu. Saya akan lebih bertang gung jawab.”"),
        Question("kp17", "Konsekuensi yang harus ditanggung oleh tokoh Rizky adalah…", listOf("Mendapat sanksi tilang dari masyarakat.", "Diperbolehkan melanjutkan perjalanan setelah berjanji tidak mengulangi pelang garan.", "Dibiarkan saja.", "Tetap diperbolehkan melanjutkan perja lanan tanpa helm.", "Risiko mengalami cedera fatal jika terjadi kecelakaan di jalan."), 4, "Tidak memakai helm membuat Rizky berisiko cedera fatal bila terjadi kecelakaan; itulah konsekuensi yang ditekankan polisi.", passage = "Pagi itu, dua orang remaja putra bernama Rizky dan Bagas hendak berangkat ke sekolah menggunakan sepeda motor.\nBagas: “Riz, kita cepetan berangkat, nanti ke buru bel masuk.”\nRizky: “Iya, tenang aja, masih sempat kok.”\nBagas: (Mereka berangkat terburu-buru. Rizky membawa motor, tetapi tidak memakai helm) “Riz, helm kamu mana?”\nRizky: “Ah, jaraknya dekat. Lagian ribet pakai helm.”\nPolisi: (Saat di pertigaan jalan, mereka diberhentikan oleh polisi lalu lintas) “Selamat pagi, kalian kenapa tidak me makai helm?”\nRizky: (gugup) “Maaf, Pak. Tadi terburu-buru jadi lupa.”\nBagas: “Saya pakai helm, Pak, tapi Rizky tidak.”\nPolisi: “Helm wajib digunakan demi keselamatan. Aturan ini tidak boleh dilanggar.”"),
        Question("kp18", "Berdasarkan kutipan cerpen tersebut, bagai mana reaksi tokoh yang paling mungkin muncul terhadap konflik yang sedang terjadi?", listOf("Pedagang pasar berusaha menghindar dari konfrontasi dengan Satpol PP dengan tidak membawa dagangan ke pasar sementara waktu.", "Yasiron memilih melawan preman dan Satpol PP secara terbuka demi membela hak para pedagang.", "Para pedagang merasa takut dan pasrah, lalu memilih menyerahkan uang keamanan kepada Mad Darsan agar dagangan mereka aman.", "Mad Darsan memanfaatkan situasi untuk memperkuat posisinya dengan membiarkan pedagang tidak membayar uang keamanan.", "Yasiron tidak menemukan cara agar tetap bisa berdagang tanpa terlibat konflik dengan Satpol PP maupun preman pasar."), 2, "Para pedagang digambarkan tertekan dan terjebak, jadi reaksi paling mungkin adalah takut lalu membayar uang keamanan.", passage = "Pasar Wage adalah pusat aktivitas pedagang kecil yang berjualan di pinggir jalan dengan berbagai barang dagangan, mulai dari sayur- mayur hingga buku. Meski begitu, para pedagang ini kerap menghadapi kesulitan besar karena adanya pemalakan yang dila kukan oleh preman-preman yang menguasai beberapa titik strategis di pasar. Tidak hanya preman, juru parkir liar juga ikut menambah beban para pedagang dengan meminta uang parkir yang kadang tidak jelas penggunaan nya. Konflik ini telah berlangsung lama dan membuat suasana pasar jadi tegang. Bahkan, beberapa kali ada upaya penertiban dari pe tugas Satpol PP, tetapi informasi tentang ren cana penertiban ini sering bocor ke pedagang sehingga mereka bisa mengemasi barang dagangannya sebelum petugas datang, mem buat operasi penertiban menjadi tidak efektif. Salah satu sosok yang paling berpengaruh di pasar Wage adalah Mad Darsan, preman yang menguasai area parkir di sekitar masjid dan toko sepeda Bah Bengwi. Dia memiliki pengaruh besar dan sering meminta uang “keamanan” kepada para pedagang yang berjualan di sekitarnya. Yasiron, salah satu pelapak yang berdagang buku dan alat tulis di dekat masjid, sering merasa tertekan dengan keberadaan Mad Darsan. Yasiron sendiri dagangannya tidak selalu laku, tapi ia memilih bertahan kare na ia ingin terus mengamati dan mencari tahu siapa yang membocorkan rencana penertiban kepada para pedagang. Ia sadar bahwa informasi bocor itu berperan penting agar mereka bisa menyelamatkan dagangannya dari pener tiban yang kerap dilakukan. Menjelang datangnya operasi penertiban dari Satpol PP, suasana di pasar Wage semakin tegang dan cemas. Para pedagang mulai bersiap-siap dengan mengemasi dagangan mereka agar tidak ikut disita atau dibongkar oleh petugas. Yasiron mendapat kabar dari pelapak lain bahwa penertiban akan dilakukan esok hari, sehingga mereka harus segera me ngosongkan lapak. Meski takut dengan kon sekuensi yang akan terjadi, para pelapak tetap berusaha bertahan dan mempertahankan usaha mereka. Mereka menghadapi tekanan bu kan hanya dari petugas penertiban, tapi juga dari para preman seperti Mad Darsan yang mengancam jika mereka tidak mau membayar uang keamanan. Keadaan ini membuat para pedagang merasa terjebak dan harus mencari cara agar tetap bisa bertahan hidup di tengah situasi sulit tersebut. (Sumber: Dikutip dari Majalah Elipsis dengan penyesuaian)"),
        Question("kp19", "Perbandingan majas kedua puisi tersebut adalah…", listOf("Puisi 1 banyak menggunakan majas metafora dan personifikasi, sedangkan puisi 2 dominan menggunakan majas metafora dan simbolik.", "Puisi 1 didominasi majas hiperbola, sedangkan puisi 2 menggunakan majas ironi.", "Puisi 1 menggunakan majas sinekdoke, sedangkan puisi 2 menggunakan majas asosiasi.", "Puisi 1 lebih menonjolkan majas ironi, sedangkan puisi 2 menampilkan majas personifikasi.", "Puisi 1 menggunakan majas litotes, sedangkan puisi 2 menggunakan majas eufemisme."), 0, "Puisi 1 penuh metafora dan personifikasi (\"sepi menyanyi\"); puisi 2 memakai metafora dan simbol perubahan diri.", passage = "Sajak Putih — Chairil Anwar\n\nBersandar pada tari warna pelangi\nKau depanku bertudung sutra senja\nDi hitam matamu kembang mawar dan melati\nHarum rambutmu mengalun bergelut senda\nSepi menyanyi\nMalam dalam mendoa tiba\nMeriak muka air kolam jiwa\nDan dalam dadaku memerdu jiwa\nDan dalam dadaku memerdu lagu\nMenarik menari seluruh aku\nHidup dari hidupku, pintu terbuka\nSelama matamu bagiku menengadah\nSelama kau darah mengalir dari luka\nAntara kita mati datang tidak membelah \nMetamorfosis — Sapardi Djoko Damono\n\nAda yang sedang menanggalkan\nKata-kata yang satu demi satu\nMendudukkanmu di depan cermin\nDan membuatmu bertanya\nTubuh siapakah gerangan\nYang kukenakan ini\nAda yang sedang diam-diam\nMenulis riwayat hidupmu\nMenimbang-nimbang hari lahirmu\nMereka-reka sebab-sebab kematianmu\nAda yang sedang diam-diam\nBerubah menjadi dirimu"),
        Question("kp20", "Konflik tokoh Sahasika yang sering terjadi dalam kehidupan sehari-hari adalah…", listOf("Orang akan melampiaskan kekecewaan dengan melakukan perlawanan secara terbuka.", "Orang berusaha memperoleh kedudukan tinggi untuk mendapatkan pengakuan.", "Orang mudah menyalahkan pihak lain atas kegagalan yang dialaminya.", "Orang cenderung merasa nyaman saat menerima pujian yang tidak sesuai dengan kenyataan.", "Orang sering meragukan kemampuan dirinya sendiri ketika menghadapi kegagalan."), 4, "Sahasika merasa bukan orang hebat karena gagal mencegah dua peristiwa → meragukan kemampuan diri saat gagal.", passage = "“Paman, bagi saya, pujian yang datangnya bisa dari siapa saja bukan ukuran kalau saya benar- benar memiliki kehebatan seperti yang disangkakan orang lain. Mereka bisa salah memperkirakan seberapa tinggi kemampuan saya. Saya mengatakan ini berdasarkan bukti nyata Paman.” “Apa bukti nyata yang kamu maksudkan, Sahasika?” “Kegagalan saya mencegah terjadinya perang antara Wilwatikta dan Tuban merupakan bukti nyata bahwa saya bukan orang hebat. Kemudian terjadinya pembunuhan terhadap kesatria utama Mahesa Sora yang tidak bisa saya cegah juga. Dari kedua peristiwa itu saja menunjukkan bahwa saya tidak mempunyai kemampuan apa-apa. Makanya saya paling merasa malu kalau dipuji-puji sebagai kesatria hebat.” “Pernyataanmu bukan bukti nyata kalau kamu gagal mencegah dua peristiwa besar yang membuat rakyat Wilwatikta makin lemah. Kamu hanya rakyat jelata. Kamu bukan raja, bukan punggawa, bukan senopati, dan bukan prajurit Wilwatikta. Apa dayamu sebagai rak yat jelata untuk mencegah peristiwa yang pasti tidak bisa dicegah oleh siapa saja, termasuk Sinuwun Prabu waktu itu. Sebentar..., tiba-tiba aku ingat kata seorang sahabat yang tinggal di Wilwatikta dan mengenal dekat mendiang Adipati Ranggalawe.” “Apa kata sahabat Paman itu?” “Begini.... Kata sahabatku itu, dulu Dyah Wija ya pernah menjanjikan kedudukan mahapatih kepada Ranggalawe kalau pendirian Wilwa tikta selesai. Namun kenyataannya, saat Wi watikta berdiri dan Dyah Wijaya menobatkan dirinya sebagai raja, yang diangkat sebagai mahapatih adalah Nambi. Rasa kecewa Adi pati Tuban itu dilampiaskan dengan sikap me nentang keputusan Dyah Wijaya secara keras. Waktu itu Adipati Ranggalawe tidak akan ber gabung dengan Wilwatikta kalau Mahapatih Hamengkubumi Nambi tidak diganti.” (Mahapatih Nambi, Gesta Bayuadhy)"),
        Question("kp21", "Sikap tokoh Sahasika yang dapat dijadikan teladan adalah ...", listOf("Sahasika bersikap rendah hati karena mengakui kehebatan Halayuda.", "Sahasika merasa takut dan menganggap dirinya lemah daripada Halayuda.", "Sahasika bersikap mudah percaya terhadap kabar yang beredar tentang Halayuda.", "Sahasika sombong dan meremehkan kemampuan Halayuda di hadapan orang lain.", "Sahasika menerima semua pendapat pamannya tanpa memberikan bantahan."), 0, "Sahasika mengakui kehebatan Halayuda dan tidak menyombongkan diri → rendah hati.", passage = "“Mengapa Halayuda bisa memengaruhi segala kebijakan, Sinuwun Prabu?” tanya Pundak Rajung. “Karena dia pandai mengambil hati Sinuwun Prabu. Setiap pemikirannya bisa dengan leluasa dia tanamkan ke benak siapa saja. Itu memang kehebatan Halayuda. Saya sudah cukup mengenal watak aslinya. Dia sangat hebat dengan memainkan lidahnya. Dia pandai bersilat lidah. Entah itu secara halus ataupun secara kasar.” “Apakah hanya itu kemampuannya?” “Tentu saja tidak, Paman. Halayuda juga memi liki kesaktian tingkat tinggi yang tidak mudah dikalahkan siapa pun. Saya yang dianggap paling hebat di Paguron Candhini, belum tentu bisa menandingi Halayuda. Bahkan kalau su atu saat saya bertarung melawan Halayuda, bisa saja saya kalah dan mati di tangannya.” “Kamu boleh berendah hati dan berendah diri seperti itu, Sahasika. Hanya saja, menurut kabar yang beredar, Halayuda juga keder dan ciut nyali setiap mendengar namamu. Tidak heran dia mau membunuhmu dengan berba gai cara. Kamu hampir saja mati di jurang saat pulang dari Tuban. Untung saja kamu masih terselamatkan.” “Dari mana Paman tahu kalau Halayuda min der sama Sahasika? Jangan-jangan Paman se dang mimpi sekarang! Kalau yang berbicara Munding Bayong, jangan langsung dipercaya Paman! Munding Bayong itu kadang-kadang terlalu membesar-besarkan kehebatan orang lain.” “Selain Munding Bayong, ada beberapa te manku yang sering bertandang ke ibu kota Wilwatikta. Katanya, nama Sahasika tidak bisa dianggap enteng di kalangan para punggawa, senopati, prajurit, dan kalangan rakyat pada umumnya. Bahkan semasa mendiang Sinu wun Prabu Dyah Wijaya, beberapa kali beliau memuji kehebatanmu dalam beberapa per tempuran agung di istana Wilwatikta. (Mahapatih Nambi, Gesta Bayuadhy)"),
        Question("kp22", "Berdasarkan teks tersebut, dapat disimpulkan bahwa…", listOf("Masa remaja merupakan masa yang penuh dengan pengaruh negatif dari lingkungan sekitar.", "Pendidikan karakter diperlukan untuk membentuk remaja yang berkarakter kuat, berprestasi, dan berakhlak baik.", "Remaja yang tidak mendapatkan pendidikan karakter akan sulit bersaing secara internasional.", "Nilai religius menjadi satu-satunya faktor pembentuk kepribadian remaja.", "Peran orang tua lebih penting daripada pendidikan karakter dalam membentuk remaja."), 1, "Simpulan teks: pendidikan karakter membentuk remaja yang berkarakter kuat, berprestasi, dan berbudi pekerti baik.", passage = "Masa remaja merupakan masa sulit karena butuh pengendalian diri yang lebih daripada saat masa anak-anak. Dalam masa ini remaja butuh orang dewasa untuk mengarahkan ke perilaku positif agar tidak terpengaruh ke perbuatan negatif. Jika pengendaliannya baik, remaja bisa menjadi anak yang membanggakan orang tuanya. Pendidikan karakter ini dapat membentuk remaja menjadi berprestasi. Di dalam pendidikan karakter mereka juga di ajarkan nilai religius yang dapat menguraikan kebaikan agar remaja tumbuh sebagai manusia yang peka pada lingkungan sosial. Di samping itu mereka juga diajarkan nilai toleransi dan cinta damai atau nilai-nilai kemanusiaan agar membentuk remaja yang mempunyai sifat pengasih. Dengan demikian, nilai-nilai positif dalam pendidikan karakter itu dapat membentuk remaja yang unggul. Mereka juga dapat bersaing dengan baik di tingkat nasional maupun internasional. Dengan begitu, remaja yang memiliki karakter kuat. Nilai positif dalam pendidikan karakter juga dapat membuat kegiatan remaja terarah dan akan mempunyai budi pekerti yang baik."),
        Question("kp52", "Kata serapan dari bahasa asing yang terdapat dalam kutipan teks di atas adalah ….", listOf("bioteknologi, inovasi, vektor, modifikasi", "signifikan, medis, penyakit, presisi", "metode, ilmuwan, materi, potensi", "etika, moral, batasan, regulasi", "genetik, sel, kajian, target"), 0, "Bioteknologi (biotechnology), inovasi (innovation), vektor (vector), modifikasi (modification) adalah kata serapan asing. Pilihan lain memuat kata asli seperti penyakit, ilmuwan, batasan, kajian.", passage = "Perkembangan bioteknologi modern telah membawa dampak signifikan dalam dunia medis, khususnya dalam penanganan pe nyakit genetik. Salah satu inovasi terbarunya adalah metode penyuntingan gen yang me mungkinkan ilmuwan untuk memperbaiki mutasi DNA dengan presisi tinggi. Proses ini sering melibatkan penggunaan vektor khu sus untuk menghantarkan materi genetik ke dalam sel target. Meskipun menawarkan potensi kesembuhan yang besar, penerapan teknologi ini tetap memerlukan kajian etika yang mendalam agar tidak melanggar batasan moral kemanusiaan. Selain itu, regulasi ketat diperlukan untuk mencegah penyalahgunaan modifikasi biologis di masa depan."),
        Question("kp53", "Opini penulis yang menjadi gagasan utama dalam kutipan editorial tersebut adalah ….", listOf("Transformasi digital di sekolah hanya menjadi pilihan bagi institusi yang memiliki anggaran besar.", "Ketimpangan akses teknologi harus diatasi dengan pemerataan infrastruktur dan kompetensi guru, bukan sekadar pembagian gawai.", "Siswa di daerah terpencil memiliki skor literasi digital yang lebih rendah karena kurangnya minat belajar.", "Pemerintah telah berhasil melakukan pemerataan jaringan internet di seluruh wilayah pendidikan nasional.", "Evaluasi pendidikan nasional menunjukkan bahwa gawai adalah solusi tunggal untuk meningkatkan kualitas siswa."), 1, "Opini utama: ketimpangan akses harus diatasi dengan pemerataan jaringan dan pelatihan guru, bukan sekadar membagi gawai.", passage = "Transformasi digital di sektor pendidikan bu kan lagi sekadar pilihan, melainkan keharusan yang mendesak. Ketimpangan akses teknologi antara sekolah di kota besar dan daerah terpencil menjadi sorotan utama dalam evaluasi pendidikan nasional tahun ini. Data menun jukkan bahwa siswa dengan akses internet stabil memiliki skor literasi digital 40% lebih tinggi dibandingkan mereka yang terkenda la infrastruktur. Pemerintah tidak bisa hanya berfokus pada pembagian gawai, tetapi juga harus memastikan pemerataan jaringan dan pelatihan kompetensi guru. Jika infrastruktur digital tidak segera dibenahi, jurang kualitas pendidikan akan semakin melebar, menciptakan ketidakadilan struktural bagi generasi mendatang."),
        Question("kp54", "Manakah informasi yang sesuai dengan kutipan teks tersebut?", listOf("Hingga saat ini, wayang kulit belum termasuk warisan budaya yang diakui oleh UNESCO.", "Peran sentral dalam pertunjukan wayang kulit dipegang oleh sinden yang memimpin iringan musik gamelan.", "Regenerasi pelaku seni dan penikmat wayang kulit di kalangan generasi muda menjadi bukan menjadi tantangan saat ini.", "Pertunjukan wayang kulit harus mempertahankan durasi aslinya dan menolak segala bentuk adaptasi digital.", "Inovasi digital dan pemadatan durasi dilakukan untuk menjaga relevansi wayang kulit bagi generasi Z"), 4, "Teks menyebut inovasi digital dan pemadatan durasi dilakukan agar wayang tetap relevan bagi generasi Z.", passage = "Wayang kulit telah diakui oleh UNESCO seba gai Karya Agung Warisan Budaya Lisan dan Nonbendawi Manusia ( and Intangible Heritage of Humanity tahun 2003. Pertunjukan ini bukan sekadar tontonan hiburan, melainkan media refleksi yang sarat akan nilai filosofis, moral, dan spiritual masya rakat Jawa. Seorang dalang memegang peran sentral sebagai narator, penggerak tokoh, sekaligus pemimpin iringan musik gamelan. Namun, seiring perkembangan zaman, seni tradisi ini menghadapi tantangan regenerasi, baik dari sisi pelaku seni maupun penikmat nya di kalangan generasi muda. Oleh karena itu, inovasi melalui platform digital dan pemadatan durasi pertunjukan mulai dilakukan agar wayang kulit tetap relevan dan diminati oleh generasi Z tanpa menghilangkan esensi pakemnya."),
        Question("kp55", "Informasi utama dalam teks berita tersebut adalah ….", listOf("Tantangan utama ekosistem EV adalah ketersediaan SPKLU yang belum merata di seluruh wilayah Indonesia.", "Subsidi pembelian kendaraan listrik hanya diberikan kepada konsumen yang memiliki daya listrik rendah di rumah.", "Investor asing diwajibkan membangun pabrik baterai di dalam negeri sebelum tahun 2026 agar mendapat insentif.", "Pemerintah mempercepat ekosistem kendaraan listrik melalui target produksi dan pemberian insentif fiskal.", "Produksi dua juta unit motor listrik telah tercapai berkat adanya potongan pajak pertambahan nilai bagi produsen."), 3, "Inti berita: pemerintah mempercepat ekosistem EV lewat target produksi dan insentif pajak/subsidi.", passage = "Pemerintah Indonesia terus mempercepat pembangunan ekosistem kendaraan listrik (EV) guna menekan emisi karbon dan keter gantungan pada bahan bakar fosil. Kemen terian Perindustrian menargetkan produksi dua juta unit motor listrik pada tahun 2026. Untuk mencapai target tersebut, pemerintah memberikan insentif berupa potongan pajak pertambahan nilai (PPN) bagi produsen dan subsidi pembelian bagi konsumen. Langkah ini diharapkan mampu menarik minat investor asing untuk membangun pabrik baterai di dalam negeri. Namun, tantangan ketersediaan stasiun pengisian kendaraan listrik umum (SPKLU) yang belum merata masih menjadi pekerjaan rumah yang harus diselesaikan."),
        Question("kp56", "Pernyataan yang paling tepat mengenai persamaan dan perbedaan gagasan inti kedua teks adalah ….", listOf("Kedua teks membahas dampak AI dalam pendidikan. Perbedaannya, Teks 1 fokus pada manfaat personalisasi pembelajaran, sedangkan Teks 2 menyoroti risiko penurunan berpikir kritis. Keduanya menjelaskan cara kerja sistem adaptif.", "Perbedaannya, Teks 1 menyebut kan analisis kecepatan belajar, sedangkan Teks 2 menjelaskan tentang chatbot ja waban instan.", "Kedua teks menekankan perlunya peran guru. Perbedaannya, Teks 1 menyaran kan penggunaan AI untuk motivasi, Teks 2 menolak penggunaan AI di sekolah.", "Kedua teks menggambarkan AI sebagai pengganti manusia. Perbedaannya, Teks 1 fokus pada penggantian peran penga jar, sedangkan Teks 2 fokus pada peng gantian proses evaluasi.", "Kedua teks mengajak sekolah untuk melarang AI. Perbedaannya, Teks 1 karena alasan biaya, sedangkan Teks 2 karena alasan etika akademik."), 0, "Kedua teks membahas AI di pendidikan; teks 1 menyoroti manfaat personalisasi, teks 2 risiko menurunnya berpikir kritis.", passage = "Kutipan 1 Kecerdasan Buatan (AI) telah merevolusi cara siswa belajar dengan menghadirkan penga laman personalisasi yang mendalam. Sistem adaptif mampu menganalisis kecepatan belajar siswa dan menyediakan materi yang sesuai dengan kebutuhan individu. Hal ini memung kinkan setiap siswa berkembang sesuai poten sinya tanpa merasa tertinggal atau bosan di kelas. Dengan demikian, AI menjadi alat bantu yang efektif untuk meningkatkan motivasi dan hasil belajar. Kutipan 2 Integrasi Kecerdasan Buatan (AI) di sekolah memunculkan kekhawatiran baru terkait integritas akademik dan ketergantungan siswa. Kemudahan mendapatkan jawaban instan melalui chatbot dapat mengikis kemampuan berpikir kritis serta analitis siswa. Guru kini menghadapi tantangan besar untuk merancang metode evaluasi yang memastikan orisinalitas pemikiran siswa, bukan sekadar hasil olahan mesin."),
        Question("kp57", "Hubungan sebab-akibat yang logis dari kedua teks tersebut adalah ….", listOf("Prestasi akademik nasional stagnan, sehingga siswa beralih menggunakan gawai dan media sosial untuk belajar materi kompleks.", "Materi pelajaran sains dan matematika sangat sulit, akibatnya siswa menjadi malas membaca dan lebih memilih bermain di perpustakaan.", "Kurangnya akses buku dan dominasi gawai menyebabkan minat baca rendah, yang berdampak pada sulitnya pema haman materi dan stagnannya prestasi akademik.", "Perpustakaan sekolah kekurangan buku berkualitas karena siswa gagal mengidentifikasi informasi penting dalam teks panjang.", "Daya saing lulusan sulit meningkat, oleh karena itu sekolah melarang penggunaan gawai agar siswa fokus membaca buku pelajaran."), 2, "Teks 1 = sebab (akses buku kurang, gawai mendominasi → minat baca rendah). Teks 2 = akibat (sulit memahami materi, prestasi stagnan).", passage = "Kutipan 1 Minat baca siswa di Indonesia masih tergolong rendah dibandingkan negara-negara tetangga. Kurangnya akses terhadap buku bacaan yang berkualitas dan menarik di perpustakaan sekolah menjadi salah satu faktor penyebab utamanya. Selain itu, penggunaan gawai dan media sosial yang berlebihan sering kali lebih mendominasi waktu luang siswa daripada ke giatan membaca buku. Kutipan 2 Kemampuan literasi yang rendah berdampak pada sulitnya siswa memahami materi pelajaran yang kompleks, seperti sains dan matematika. Banyak siswa yang gagal mengidentifikasi informasi penting dalam soal cerita atau teks panjang. Akibatnya, prestasi akademik secara nasional cenderung stagnan dan daya saing lulusan sulit meningkat di tingkat global."),
        Question("kp58", "Berdasarkan informasi dalam artikel tersebut, dampak yang kemungkinan besar akan terjadi selanjutnya pada sektor ekonomi dan ketena gakerjaan adalah ….", listOf("Permintaan terhadap tenaga kerja dengan keahlian khusus di bidang teknologi energi terbarukan akan menurun drastis.", "Pemerintah akan membuka kembali izin operasional PLTU batu bara baru untuk menampung tenaga kerja tambang.", "Tenaga kerja di sektor pertambangan batu bara menghadapi risiko kehilangan pekerjaan sehingga memerlukan program pelatihan ulang (reskilling).", "Arus investasi asing di Indonesia akan mengalami penurunan drastis karena penutupan pembangkit listrik konvensional.", "Berkurangnya peluang bisnis dan lapangan kerja baru yang berkaitan dengan infrastruktur ekonomi hijau."), 2, "Teks menyebut sektor tambang batu bara berpotensi kehilangan tenaga kerja, sehingga perlu pelatihan ulang ke sektor energi baru.", passage = "Pemerintah Indonesia berkomitmen untuk mempercepat transisi energi menuju Net Zero Emission pada tahun 2060. Salah satu langkah strategisnya adalah pensiun dini Pembangkit Listrik Tenaga Uap (PLTU) batu bara dan meng gantinya dengan energi terbarukan, seperti tenaga surya dan panas bumi. Transformasi ini diprediksi akan mengubah peta ketenaga kerjaan nasional secara signifikan. Sektor pertambangan batu bara berpotensi mengalami pengurangan tenaga kerja, sementara sektor nisi baru yang terampil. Selain itu, investasi asing diproyeksikan akan mengalir deras ke proyek- proyek keberlanjutan, mendorong pertumbuhan ekonomi hijau yang lebih inklusif."),
        Question("kp59", "Prediksi yang paling mungkin terjadi terkait penerapan sistem kesehatan digital tersebut di masa depan adalah ….", listOf("Rumah sakit akan sepenuhnya menghen tikan pelayanan tatap muka dan beralih total ke telemedisin karena dianggap lebih efisien.", "Pasien akan kesulitan dalam melakukan akses terhadap rekam medis pribadi mereka.", "Pemerintah dan penyedia layanan kesehatan akan mengurangi investasi pada infrastruktur keamanan siber untuk melindungi data pasien.", "Tenaga medis akan kesulitan mengambil keputusan klinis karena data digital dinilai kurang akurat dibandingkan berkas fisik.", "Regulasi mengenai privasi data dan standardisasi format digital akan diperketat untuk menjamin keamanan informasi pengguna."), 4, "Teks menutup dengan standardisasi data dan perlindungan privasi sebagai fokus regulasi mendatang.", passage = "Pemerintah sedang gencar mengintegrasikan data kesehatan nasional melalui satu platform digital terpusat. Langkah ini bertujuan untuk memudahkan pasien dalam mengakses riwa yat medis mereka di mana saja tanpa harus membawa berkas fisik. Selain itu, tenaga me dis dapat mengambil keputusan klinis yang lebih akurat dan cepat berdasarkan data yang komprehensif. Namun, digitalisasi data kese hatan skala besar ini membawa risiko keboco an data pribadi yang serius jika tidak dibarengi dengan sistem keamanan siber yang kuat. Oleh karena itu, standardisasi format data dan perlindungan privasi menjadi fokus utama regulasi mendatang."),
        Question("kp60", "Keterkaitan semangat tokoh dalam kutipan tersebut dengan kehidupan sehari-hari adalah….", listOf("Seseorang harus mengabaikan kesehatan diri sendiri demi mendapatkan pujian dari orang lain.", "Keterbatasan fisik dan rintangan yang berat tidak boleh menjadi alasan untuk menyerah dalam mencapai tujuan mulia.", "Pemimpin yang baik adalah pemimpin yang selalu meminta bantuan bawahannya untuk menyelesaikan tugas pribadi.", "Kita harus menolak saran medis dari dokter agar terlihat kuat dan berwibawa di hadapan bawahan.", "Perjuangan membela negara hanya dapat dilakukan dengan cara mengangkat senjata dan masuk ke dalam hutan."), 1, "Soedirman tetap memimpin gerilya meski sakit → keterbatasan fisik bukan alasan menyerah.", passage = "Jenderal Soedirman dikenal sebagai Panglima Besar pertama Tentara Nasional Indonesia yang memiliki dedikasi luar biasa. Meski menderita sakit paru-paru parah hingga harus menjalani operasi, Jendral Soedirman menolak untuk beristirahat total saat Agresi Militer Belanda II terjadi pada tahun 1948. Dengan kondisi fisik yang sangat lemah dan harus ditandu, Soedirman tetap memimpin pasukannya bergerilya masuk keluar hutan serta naikturun gunung selama berbulan-bulan. Jendral Soedirman membuktikan bahwa keterbatasan fisik bukanlah penghalang untuk mempertahankan kedaulatan bangsa. Sikapnya yang lebih mementingkan kepentingan negara di atas kepentingan pribadi dan kesehatannya sendiri menjadikannya sosok pemimpin yang sangat dihormati oleh kawan maupun lawan."),
        Question("kp61", "Berdasarkan kutipan biografi tersebut, dampak perjuangan Butet Manurung terhadap kehidupan masyarakat adat adalah ….", listOf("Pendidikan antropologis yang diterapkan menyebabkan konflik berkepanjangan antara anak-anak dan tetua adat.", "Anak-anak Rimba meninggalkan hutan dan tradisi leluhur untuk hidup modern di kota besar berkat kemampuan baca tulis.", "Kemampuan literasi digunakan oleh masyarakat adat sebagai alat untuk mempertahankan hak dan wilayah hutan mereka dari ancaman luar.", "Masyarakat adat masih kesulitan mendapat akses pendidikan literasi yang relevan.", "Terciptanya kesadaran bahwa pendidikan tidak dapat berjalan beriringan dengan pelestarian kearifan local"), 2, "Literasi dipakai anak-anak Rimba untuk melindungi hutan adat dari penyerobotan lahan.", passage = "Saur Marlina Manurung, atau yang lebih dikenal sebagai Butet Manurung, mendedikasikan hidupnya untuk memberikan pendidikan bagi masyarakat adat di pedalaman hutan Indone sia melalui “Sokola Rimba”. Ia mengembang kan metode pembelajaran antropologis yang unik: mengajarkan baca- tulis-hitung dengan menyesuaikan pola hidup dan adat istiadat setempat, bukan mengubahnya. Awalnya, ia menghadapi penolakan keras karena diang gap membawa pengaruh buruk atau melanggar tabu leluhur. Namun, berkat kegigihannya, anak-anak Rimba kini memiliki kemampuan literasi yang mereka gunakan untuk melin dungi hutan adat mereka dari penyerobotan lahan oleh pihak luar. Pendekatan Butet membuktikan bahwa pendidikan tidak harus mencabut seseorang dari akar budayanya, melainkan justru menjadi senjata untuk mempertahankan hak hidup mereka."),
        Question("kp62", "Kalimat yang tidak padu atau tidak berkaitan langsung dengan gagasan utama paragraf tersebut ditandai dengan nomor ….", listOf("(1)", "(2)", "(3)", "(4)", "(5)"), 3, "Gagasan utama: pentingnya kecerdasan emosional. Kalimat (4) tentang tes IQ di masa lalu tidak padu dengan gagasan itu.", passage = "(1) Kecerdasan emosional (emotional intelligence) memiliki peran yang sama pentingnya dengan kecerdasan intelektual dalam kesuksesan karier seseorang. (2) Kemampuan mengelola emosi diri dan memahami perasaan orang lain sangat dibutuhkan dalam kerja tim. (3) Individu dengan kecerdasan emosional tinggi cenderung lebih tahan terhadap tekanan dan mampu menyelesaikan konflik dengan kepala dingin. (4) Tes IQ sering kali menjadi satu- satunya tolak ukur dalam proses rekrutmen pegawai di perusahaan-perusahaan besar pada masa lalu. (5) Oleh karena itu, banyak perusahaan modern kini mulai memasukkan tes psikologi kepribadian sebagai bagian dari seleksi karyawan baru."),
        Question("kp63", "Kalimat yang tidak efektif dalam paragraf ter sebut ditandai dengan nomor ….", listOf("(1)", "(2)", "(3)", "(4)", "(5)"), 3, "Kalimat (4) tidak efektif karena kata depan \"Bagi\" membuat kalimat tidak bersubjek. Seharusnya \"Para nelayan sangat menggantungkan hidupnya…\".", passage = "(1) Hutan mangrove memiliki fungsi ekologis yang sangat vital bagi kawasan pesisir. (2) Akar-akar bakau yang kuat mampu mena han laju abrasi air laut yang dapat mengikis daratan secara perlahan. (3) Selain itu, hutan ini menjadi habitat alami bagi berbagai biota laut seperti kepiting, udang, dan ikan-ikan kecil untuk berkembang biak. (4) Bagi para nelayan sangat menggantungkan hidupnya pada kelestarian ekosistem ini untuk menda patkan hasil tangkapan yang melimpah. (5) Oleh karena itu, upaya konservasi mangrove harus terus digalakkan demi keberlangsungan hidup masyarakat pesisir."),
        Question("kp64", "Kutipan baris berikut ini yang merupakan penggunaan diksi konotatif dalam puisi di atas adalah ….", listOf("Matahari membakar kulit ari", "Peluh bercucuran membasahi diri", "Walau duri dan kerikil menyapa kaki", "Di ujung jalan yang berdebu ini", "Aku menitipkan sisa-sisa mimpi"), 2, "\"Duri dan kerikil menyapa kaki\" adalah kiasan untuk rintangan hidup, jadi bermakna konotatif.", passage = "Jalan Berdebu\n\nDi ujung jalan yang berdebu ini\nAku menitipkan sisa-sisa mimpi\nMatahari membakar kulit ari\nPeluh bercucuran membasahi diri\nNamun, langkah tak boleh terhenti\nWalau duri dan kerikil menyapa kaki\nAku harus terus mendaki\nHingga kutemukan mata air abadi"),
        Question("kp65", "Watak tokoh Wulan yang tergambar dalam kutipan cerpen tersebut adalah ….", listOf("Keras kepala dan sulit menerima nasihat orang tua.", "Mandiri dan memiliki tekad kuat untuk berusaha.", "Pemalu dan merasa rendah diri dengan keadaannya.", "Sombong karena merasa mampu mencari uang sendiri.", "Pasrah menerima nasib tanpa mau mela kukan perubahan."), 1, "Wulan menolak keringanan dan memilih berjualan kue untuk membayar SPP → mandiri dan bertekad kuat.", passage = "“Kau tidak perlu memaksakan diri, Lan. Kalau memang tidak ada uang, biar Ibu yang bicara sama pihak sekolah,” ujar Bu Mirna lembut sambil mengelus pundak anak sulungnya itu. Wulan menggeleng kuat. Matanya berkaca- kaca, namun ada kilat tekad di sana. “Tidak, Bu. Wulan malu kalau harus minta ke ringanan terus. Wulan akan coba jualan kue sepulang sekolah. Teman-teman banyak yang suka kue buatan Ibu. Hasilnya lumayan buat nambah bayar SPP.” Bu Mirna terdiam. Hatinya perih melihat anak seusia Wulan harus memikirkan beban eko nomi keluarga, namun di sisi lain, ia bangga melihat semangat pantang menyerah yang tumbuh di jiwa putrinya itu."),
        Question("kp66", "Berdasarkan kutipan cerpen di atas, pernyataan yang sesuai dengan isi cerita adalah ….", listOf("Pak Mamat tetap membuat layang-layang semata-mata karena butuh uang untuk memperbaiki rumahnya yang lapuk.", "Anak-anak di lingkungan sekitar rumah Pak Mamat saat ini lebih tertarik bermain layang-layang daripada bermain gawai.", "Sarti mendukung penuh usaha suaminyadan menyemangatinya untuk terus memproduksi layang-layang tanpa henti.", "Pak Mamat memandang aktivitas membuat layang-layang sebagai upaya melestarikan tradisi di tengah perubahan zaman.", "Cucu Pak Mamat merasa biasa saja ketika layang-layang tradisional buatan kakeknya mampu terbang tinggi di angkasa."), 3, "Bagi Pak Mamat, membuat layang-layang adalah cara menjaga napas tradisi agar tidak mati.", passage = "Pak Mamat masih setia meraut bambu di beranda rumahnya yang mulai lapuk. Di seberang jalan, anak-anak lebih asyik menunduk menatap layar ponsel daripada berlarian mengejar layang-layang putus. “Zaman sudah berubah, Pak. Sudahlah, istirahat saja,” kata Sarti, istrinya, sambil menyodorkan teh hangat. Namun, bagi Pak Mamat, membuat layang-layang bukan sekadar mencari uang receh. Itu adalah cara dia menjaga napas tradisi agar tidak mati tergilas sunyi. Ia ingat betul binar mata cucunya minggu lalu saat la yang-layang buatan kakeknya berhasil menari di angkasa, mengalahkan drone canggih milik tetangga sebelah. Kebanggaan itu tak bisa dibeli dengan pulsa data."),
        Question("kp67", "Tema utama dari puisi tersebut adalah ….", listOf("Keindahan hutan yang masih alami dan belum terjamah manusia.", "Perjuangan burung-burung mempertahankan sarangnya di atas pohon.", "Kerusakan alam dan lingkungan akibat keserakahan pembangunan manusia.", "Pentingnya menanam pohon kembali untuk masa depan bumi.", "Kekaguman penyair terhadap gedung- gedung tinggi yang modern."), 2, "Puisi menggambarkan pohon ditebang demi gedung, tanah memerah, sungai keruh → kerusakan alam akibat pembangunan.", passage = "Nyanyian Pohon Tumbang\n\nDulu, kami adalah payung raksasa\nMenyimpan sejuk di sela-sela daun\nTempat burung-burung merajut kisah\nDan angin berbisik tentang embun\nKini, deru mesin mengganti kicauan\nGergaji tajam memutus harapan\nTubuh kami roboh mencium tanah\nDemi gedung-gedung yang menjulang gagah\nTanah menjadi merah, sungai menjadi keruh\nManusia lupa, napas mereka pun dari peluh kami"),
        Question("kp68", "Berdasarkan dialog di atas, watak tokoh Raka dapat disimpulkan sebagai ….", listOf("Keras kepala dan tidak memiliki rasa empati terhadap kesulitan teman.", "Tegas berpegang pada prinsip kejujuran namun tetap solutif.", "Penakut dan tidak berani mengambil risiko demi menolong orang lain.", "Sombong karena merasa memiliki jabatan tinggi di organisasi.", "Mudah dipengaruhi dan ragu-ragu dalam mengambil keputusan penting."), 1, "Raka menolak memakai kas tanpa prosedur (tegas, jujur) tetapi menawarkan galang dana (solutif).", passage = "Suasana di ruang OSIS sepulang sekolah.\nRaka: “Kita tidak bisa membiarkan dana pensi ini dipakai untuk keperluan pribadi, Don. Itu uang siswa, amanah yang harus dijaga.”\nDoni: (Merenung sejenak, lalu menatap Raka tajam) “Tapi ini darurat, Rak. Ibuku sakit keras, butuh bia ya operasi segera. Aku janji akan menggantinya bulan depan setelah panen sawah Bapak di kampung.”\nRaka: (Menghela napas panjang, suara nya melunak namun tegas) “Aku turut prihatin dengan ibumu, Don. Sungguh. Kita bisa galang dana bantuan atau iuran sukarela dari teman-teman. Tapi kalau menyentuh kas OSIS tanpa prosedur, itu korupsi namanya. Aku tidak bisa membiarkanmu menghancurkan masa depanmu sendiri dengan cara yang salah.”\nDoni: “Jadi, kau lebih peduli aturan daripada nyawa ibuku?”\nRaka: “Bukan begitu. Justru karena aku peduli padamu, aku tidak mau kau terjerumus. Ayo, kita cari solusi lain yang halal.”"),
        Question("kp69", "Berdasarkan dialog tersebut, pernyataan yang tepat mengenai konflik yang terjadi adalah ….", listOf("Konflik terjadi antara keinginan anak untuk mengejar passion seni dan keinginan orangtua akan kemapanan finansial anaknya.", "Ibu melarang keras Bayu melukis karena menganggap seni adalah pekerjaan yang hina dan tidak bermartabat.", "Bayu mengalami konflik batin antara mempertahankan idealismenya atau berbakti dan menambah beban orangtua.", "Ibu merasa Bayu bijak karena bergantung secara finansial pada uang pensiun ayahnya meskipun sudah dewasa.", "Bayu setuju untuk langsung berhenti melukis saat itu juga demi membahagiakan ibunya."), 0, "Konflik: Bayu ingin mengejar seni, ibu ingin anaknya mapan secara finansial.", passage = "Ibu: (Menahan suara agar tidak meninggi) “Ibu tidak melarang kamu menjadi seniman, Bayu. Tapi lihat realitas! Lukisanmu belum bisa memberimu makan. Tawaran kerja di perusahaan om-mu itu kesempatan emas. Gaji tetap, asuransi, masa depan terjamin.”\nBayu: (Tetap memandang kanvas, ti dak menoleh) “Masalahnya bukan soal uang, Bu. Ini soal jiwa. Kalau aku ambil pekerjaan itu, aku mati pelan- pelan. Aku jadi robot. Apa Ibu mau punya anak yang kaya tapi kosong?”\nIbu: “Kamu ini egois! Kamu pikir si apa yang membiayai cat dan kanvasmu selama ini? Itu uang pensiunan Bapakmu! Ibu hanya ingin kamu mandiri sebelum Ibu tiada.”\nBayu: (Terdiam, kuas di tangannya gemetar) “Beri aku waktu satu tahun lagi, Bu. Hanya satu tahun. Kalau pameran tunggalku bulan depan gagal, aku akan turuti semua mau Ibu.”"),
        Question("kp70", "Pernyataan yang tepat terkait pendeskripsian watak tokoh Ardi dalam kutipan tersebut adalah ….", listOf("Kalimat (1) dan (2) menunjukkan bahwa Ardi adalah mahasiswa yang mudah putus asa saat menghadapi kritik tajam.", "Kalimat (1) dan (4) menggambarkan Ardi sebagai sosok yang memiliki prioritas tinggi dan bertanggung jawab terhadap tugas akhirnya.", "Kalimat (4) membuktikan bahwa Ardi adalah tipe orang yang antisosial karena menolak ajakan teman-temannya.", "Kalimat (4) menunjukkan kegigihan dan kerja keras Ardi dalam memperjuangkan tujuannya meskipun dalam kondisi fisik yang lelah.", "Pengarang menggambarkan watak tokoh Ardi secara dramatik melalui dialog dan perilaku tokoh, bukan melalui penjelasan langsung."), 4, "Watak Ardi digambarkan lewat dialog dan perilakunya (dramatik), bukan dijelaskan langsung oleh pengarang.", passage = "(1) Ardi menatap nanar tumpukan skripsi yang baru saja dicoret-coret oleh dosen pembimbingnya. (2) “Revisi total bagian bab empat. Datanya tidak valid,” kata-kata dosen itu masih terngiang, menyengat telinga. (3) Teman-teman sekosnya mengajak pergi ke pantai untuk menyegarkan pikiran, namun Ardi menolak halus. (4) “Kalian duluan saja. Aku harus menyelesaikan perbaikan data ini malam ini juga supaya bisa mengejar sidang bulan depan,” ucapnya sambil kembali membuka laptop. (5) Meskipun matanya sudah merah karena kurang tidur, jari-jemarinya tetap lincah menari di atas papan ketik, mencari referensi jurnal terbaru untuk memperkuat argumennya."),
        Question("kp71", "Pandangan penulis yang tergambar dalam kutipan artikel tersebut adalah ….", listOf("Penulis menolak keras sistem kerja dari rumah karena dianggap mematikan ino vasi dan budaya perusahaan.", "Penulis menilai bahwa bekerja dari kantor sepenuhnya adalah satu-satunya cara untuk meningkatkan produktivitas karyawan.", "Penulis mendukung penerapan model kerja hibrida sebagai solusi yang menye imbangkan fleksibilitas dan kolaborasi.", "Penulis berpendapat bahwa interaksi virtual jauh lebih efektif dan efisien diban dingkan pertemuan tatap muka.", "Penulis bersikap netral dan menyerahkan keputusan sepenuhnya kepada masing- masing karyawan tanpa memberi kan solusi."), 2, "Penulis menyimpulkan model hibrida sebagai jalan tengah yang paling rasional.", passage = "Debat mengenai sistem kerja jarak jauh (remote working) versus kembali ke kantor (work from office) terus bergulir pascapandemi. Meskipun bekerja dari rumah menawarkan fleksibilitas dan penghematan waktu perjalanan, banyak pemimpin perusahaan meyakini bahwa kolaborasi tatap muka tak tergantikan untuk memantik inovasi. Interaksi spontan di koridor kantor sering kali melahirkan ide-ide brilian yang sulit muncul dalam ruang rapat virtual yang kaku. Selain itu, budaya perusaha an sulit dibangun jika karyawan hanya berin teraksi lewat layar. Oleh sebab itu, model kerja hibrida tampaknya menjadi jalan tengah yang paling rasional, mengakomodasi kebutuhan akan fleksibilitas individu sekaligus menjaga kohesi tim."),
        Question("kp72", "Berdasarkan artikel tersebut, fakta yang sesuai mengenai dampak industri adalah….", listOf("Industri karbon global yang lebih rendah dibandingkan dengan sektor transportasi laut dan udara.", "Pencemaran air tawar di berbagai belahan dunia turut diperparah oleh limbah pewarna dari industri tekstil.", "Pakaian berbahan serat sintetis di TPA dapat terurai dengan cepat sehingga aman bagi kesuburan tanah.", "Siklus pergantian model yang lambat dan harga murah memicu penumpukan sampah pakaian di tempat pembuangan akhir.", "Mikroplastik yang mencemari lingkungan hanya berasal dari penguraian serat sintetis pakaian bekas."), 1, "Teks menyebut proses pewarnaan tekstil sebagai salah satu penyebab utama pencemaran air tawar.", passage = "Industri mode cepat ( pakaian trendi dengan harga terjangkau dan siklus pergantian model yang sangat singkat. Namun, kemudahan ini harus dibayar mahal oleh lingkungan. Data menunjukkan bahwa industri ini menyumbang sekitar 10% dari total emisi karbon global, angka yang lebih besar daripada gabungan emisi penerbangan internasional dan pelayaran maritim. Selain itu, proses pewarnaan tekstil menjadi salah satu penyebab utama pencemaran air tawar di dunia. Masalah semakin pelik ketika jutaan ton pakaian bekas yang tidak terjual berakhir di Tempat Pembuangan Akhir (TPA). Sebagian besar pakaian tersebut berbahan serat sintetis seperti poliester yang membutuhkan waktu ratusan tahun untuk terurai, sekaligus melepaskan mikroplastik ke tanah dan perairan."),
        Question("kp73", "Nilai yang paling dominan dalam kutipan hikayat tersebut adalah …", listOf("Nilai sosial, yaitu kewajiban seorang raja untuk menjamu rakyatnya dan orang orang besar di istana.", "Nilai pendidikan, yaitu kewajiban menuntut ilmu agama dan ilmu bela diri sebagai bekal kehidupan dan kepemimpinan.", "Nilai estetika, yaitu keindahan bahasa yang digunakan dalam menggambarkan pertumbuhan anak raja.", "Nilai budaya, yaitu tradisi mengadakan pesta besar-besaran setiap kali seorang anak menamatkan pengajian.", "Nilai moral, yaitu sikap rendah hati seorang anak raja yang mau belajar kepada rakyat biasa."), 1, "Anak raja dididik mengaji lalu belajar ilmu prajurit sebagai bekal memerintah → nilai pendidikan.", passage = "Maka tiada berapa lama, anak raja itu pun besarlah. Maka oleh baginda diserahkan anaknya itu mengaji kepada seorang mualim. Hatta be berapa lamanya, anak raja itu pun tamatlah mengaji dan khatam Al-Qur’an. Maka baginda pun terlalu sukacita hatinya, lalu memberi sedekah kepada fakir miskin dan menjamu sega la orang besar-besar. Kemudian, anak raja itu diserahkan pula kepada seorang pendekar untuk belajar ilmu hulu balang dan ilmu prajurit, supaya tahu ia akan kelak memerintah negeri dan menjaga rakyatnya dari musuh."),
    )

    private fun kompetenBigRaw() = listOf(
        Question("kp33", "Based on the text, all of the following are rea sons why the Camel helped the Zebra during the tough situation, EXCEPT...", listOf("The Camel possessed a hump that functioned as a water storage.", "The Camel had a strong sense of smell to locate an oasis.", "The Camel and the Zebra shared a long- standing friendship.", "The Camel’s thick skin and eyelashes provided protection from storms.", "The Donkey persuaded the Camel to share his resources with the Zebra."), 4, "Kisah menyebut punuk, penciuman tajam, kulit dan bulu mata unta, serta persahabatan mereka. Keledai justru enggan berbagi air, jadi E bukan alasan.", passage = "The Camel and Zebra There was once a jungle where two animals were great friends – a camel and a zebra. Although these two animals were very different from each other, they were known to be best friends. However, the zebra thought of itself as very glamorous with its black and white coat, and it thought of the camel as an ugly creature with humps, weird feet, ugly eyelashes, and so on. One day, the camel asked the zebra to come and play with him in the mud, to which the zebra replied with a no. He said that his beautiful black and white coat will get dirty. The camel was sad at this and he played in the mud alone and sat there thinking why the zebra was ignoring him. In a few days, there came a sudden drought. All the water in the forest started drying up. The tortoises complained about the water shortage in the lakes too, from which all animals would drink everyday. This made the zebra very worried. He saw a donkey carrying water buckets on his back and asked him if he could give him some water. The donkey was hesitant because he needed the water for himself. The zebra was feeling lost and went to his best friend, the camel. The camel said that he could take him to an oasis since camels have a strong sense of smell, which they can use to smell out oases. The zebra was surprised at the calmness of the camel in such a tough situation. This is when the camel revealed that the ugly thing that the zebra didn’t like on the camel’s back was his hump, which was a store of water. He said that he could use this water to survive for weeks, even a month. He also mentioned the hooves that allow him to walk through the hot sand in the desert. The zebra was upset that he did not have such hooves to give him comfort while walking in the scorching heat. The camel’s skin was thick and protected him from sandstorms and heat, and his eyelashes also helped him keep his eyes protected during such storms. The camel did not hesitate to help his friend and keep the zebra covered under him during the sand storms. The zebra was very thankful to his friend, the camel, for his help, and he realized that not all ugly things are useless. They again started playing together happily after the drought was over. (The Camel and the Zebra available at Vedantu.com and Funcolouring.com)"),
        Question("kp34", "Based on the description of in the last paragraph, what could the zebra have done to protect himself while traveling with the camel during the sandstorm?", listOf("Walking away from the Camel.", "Asking the Camel to share his eyelashes with him.", "Staying under the Camel’s body to block the wind and sand.", "Trying to find a Donkey to carry him through the storm.", "Observing how the Camel uses his thick skin to withstand the heat."), 2, "Paragraf terakhir: unta melindungi zebra dengan menutupinya di bawah tubuhnya saat badai pasir.", passage = "The Camel and Zebra There was once a jungle where two animals were great friends – a camel and a zebra. Although these two animals were very different from each other, they were known to be best friends. However, the zebra thought of itself as very glamorous with its black and white coat, and it thought of the camel as an ugly creature with humps, weird feet, ugly eyelashes, and so on. One day, the camel asked the zebra to come and play with him in the mud, to which the zebra replied with a no. He said that his beautiful black and white coat will get dirty. The camel was sad at this and he played in the mud alone and sat there thinking why the zebra was ignoring him. In a few days, there came a sudden drought. All the water in the forest started drying up. The tortoises complained about the water shortage in the lakes too, from which all animals would drink everyday. This made the zebra very worried. He saw a donkey carrying water buckets on his back and asked him if he could give him some water. The donkey was hesitant because he needed the water for himself. The zebra was feeling lost and went to his best friend, the camel. The camel said that he could take him to an oasis since camels have a strong sense of smell, which they can use to smell out oases. The zebra was surprised at the calmness of the camel in such a tough situation. This is when the camel revealed that the ugly thing that the zebra didn’t like on the camel’s back was his hump, which was a store of water. He said that he could use this water to survive for weeks, even a month. He also mentioned the hooves that allow him to walk through the hot sand in the desert. The zebra was upset that he did not have such hooves to give him comfort while walking in the scorching heat. The camel’s skin was thick and protected him from sandstorms and heat, and his eyelashes also helped him keep his eyes protected during such storms. The camel did not hesitate to help his friend and keep the zebra covered under him during the sand storms. The zebra was very thankful to his friend, the camel, for his help, and he realized that not all ugly things are useless. They again started playing together happily after the drought was over. (The Camel and the Zebra available at Vedantu.com and Funcolouring.com)"),
        Question("kp35", "What is the main moral lesson the Zebra learned from his experience with the Camel?", listOf("Friendship is only tested during difficult times.", "Physical appearance does not determine an individual’s worth.", "Survival in the desert requires specific physical adaptations.", "One should always prepare for a sudden natural disaster.", "Seeking help from a best friend is better than asking a stranger."), 1, "Zebra sadar bahwa hal yang tampak jelek tidak berarti tak berguna → penampilan fisik tidak menentukan nilai seseorang.", passage = "The Camel and Zebra There was once a jungle where two animals were great friends – a camel and a zebra. Although these two animals were very different from each other, they were known to be best friends. However, the zebra thought of itself as very glamorous with its black and white coat, and it thought of the camel as an ugly creature with humps, weird feet, ugly eyelashes, and so on. One day, the camel asked the zebra to come and play with him in the mud, to which the zebra replied with a no. He said that his beautiful black and white coat will get dirty. The camel was sad at this and he played in the mud alone and sat there thinking why the zebra was ignoring him. In a few days, there came a sudden drought. All the water in the forest started drying up. The tortoises complained about the water shortage in the lakes too, from which all animals would drink everyday. This made the zebra very worried. He saw a donkey carrying water buckets on his back and asked him if he could give him some water. The donkey was hesitant because he needed the water for himself. The zebra was feeling lost and went to his best friend, the camel. The camel said that he could take him to an oasis since camels have a strong sense of smell, which they can use to smell out oases. The zebra was surprised at the calmness of the camel in such a tough situation. This is when the camel revealed that the ugly thing that the zebra didn’t like on the camel’s back was his hump, which was a store of water. He said that he could use this water to survive for weeks, even a month. He also mentioned the hooves that allow him to walk through the hot sand in the desert. The zebra was upset that he did not have such hooves to give him comfort while walking in the scorching heat. The camel’s skin was thick and protected him from sandstorms and heat, and his eyelashes also helped him keep his eyes protected during such storms. The camel did not hesitate to help his friend and keep the zebra covered under him during the sand storms. The zebra was very thankful to his friend, the camel, for his help, and he realized that not all ugly things are useless. They again started playing together happily after the drought was over. (The Camel and the Zebra available at Vedantu.com and Funcolouring.com)"),
        Question("kp36", "Which of the following can be inferred from the first paragraph?", listOf("The museum was initially private and only recently became public.", "The museum’s location in London’s centre makes it inaccessible to locals.", "The museum’s accessibility is enhanced by its non-existent entry fee.", "Only people with high budgets were allowed to visit before 1759.", "The museum is the only free attraction located in central London."), 2, "Paragraf pertama menyebut museum gratis, sehingga bisa dinikmati siapa saja tanpa memandang anggaran.", passage = "The British Museum The British Museum is one of the most famous and important museums in the world. It is located in the centre of London, England. The museum first opened to the public in 1759 and has been welcoming visitors ever since. One of the best things about the British Museum is that it is free to enter. This means people from all over the world can enjoy it, no matter their budget. The museum holds a very large and impressive collection of over eight million objects from many different countries and cultures. These objects help us understand human history, art, science, religion, and daily life in different parts of the world. Some of the most popular and interesting items include the Rosetta Stone, Egyptian mummies, and the Parthenon sculptures from ancient Greece. The Rosetta Stone is especially famous because it helped experts learn how to read ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs. This was a big moment in the study of history. The Egyptian galleries also attract many visitors who want to see real mummies and learn about ancient beliefs about life and death. The museum building itself is also beautiful and historic. It has tall Greek-style columns at the front and a famous Reading Room inside. In the year 2000, the museum opened the Great Court, which is a huge covered area with a beautiful glass roof. It is now the largest covered public square in Europe. In recent years, the British Museum has also taken steps to promote environmental awareness. It is working to reduce its carbon footprint through energy-saving measures and sustainable practices. The museum encourages visitors to consider how ancient cultures interacted with nature and how we can learn from them to protect our environment today. Overall, the British Museum is an amazing place to learn about the past. It is a museum for everyone-students, families, tourists, and history lovers. If you are ever in London, don’t miss the chance to visit this wonderful and inspiring place. (Adapted from https://www.britishmuseum.org/about-us/ british-museum-story/history)"),
        Question("kp37", "“The Rosetta Stone is especially famous because it helped experts learn how to read ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs. This was a big moment in the study of history.” This sentence implies that...", listOf("Egyptian hieroglyphs were a mystery to modern scholars before the stone was found.", "The Rosetta Stone is the only artifact in the museum that experts can fully read.", "Ancient Egyptians wrote the stone specifically to help future historians.", "Studying history was not considered important before the discovery of the stone.", "Experts had already mastered hieroglyphs before the Rosetta Stone arrived at the museum."), 0, "Batu Rosetta membantu ahli membaca hieroglif, berarti sebelumnya hieroglif belum bisa dibaca para ahli.", passage = "The British Museum The British Museum is one of the most famous and important museums in the world. It is located in the centre of London, England. The museum first opened to the public in 1759 and has been welcoming visitors ever since. One of the best things about the British Museum is that it is free to enter. This means people from all over the world can enjoy it, no matter their budget. The museum holds a very large and impressive collection of over eight million objects from many different countries and cultures. These objects help us understand human history, art, science, religion, and daily life in different parts of the world. Some of the most popular and interesting items include the Rosetta Stone, Egyptian mummies, and the Parthenon sculptures from ancient Greece. The Rosetta Stone is especially famous because it helped experts learn how to read ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs. This was a big moment in the study of history. The Egyptian galleries also attract many visitors who want to see real mummies and learn about ancient beliefs about life and death. The museum building itself is also beautiful and historic. It has tall Greek-style columns at the front and a famous Reading Room inside. In the year 2000, the museum opened the Great Court, which is a huge covered area with a beautiful glass roof. It is now the largest covered public square in Europe. In recent years, the British Museum has also taken steps to promote environmental awareness. It is working to reduce its carbon footprint through energy-saving measures and sustainable practices. The museum encourages visitors to consider how ancient cultures interacted with nature and how we can learn from them to protect our environment today. Overall, the British Museum is an amazing place to learn about the past. It is a museum for everyone-students, families, tourists, and history lovers. If you are ever in London, don’t miss the chance to visit this wonderful and inspiring place. (Adapted from https://www.britishmuseum.org/about-us/ british-museum-story/history)"),
        Question("kp38", "Based on the text, what are the potential actions or outcomes for students if they learn about climate change at an early age?", listOf("They will be able to make more informed and better choices as future leaders.", "They might not choose to commute to school using eco-friendly transportation like bicycles.", "They will likely stop studying traditional subjects like Science and Geography.", "They can’t contribute to significant environmental changes through small daily actions.", "They will be required to plant trees as their only way to pass English classes."), 0, "Paragraf kedua: belajar sejak dini membuat siswa, para pemimpin masa depan, bisa mengambil keputusan yang lebih baik.", passage = "Why Schools Should Teach More About Climate Change Climate change is one of the biggest problems in the world today. It affects people, animals, and the environment. Because of this, schools should teach more about climate change. Students need to understand what is happening and how they can help. First, students are the future leaders of the world. If they learn about climate change early, they can make better choices. For example, they can save energy, use less plastic, or plant trees. These actions may seem small, but if many people do them, they can make a big difference. Second, learning about climate change helps students become more responsible. They understand how their actions affect the planet. This can make them more careful in their daily lives. For example, they might walk or bike to school instead of using a car, or they might turn off lights when not in use. Third, teaching about climate change can help students with their studies. Climate topics are useful in science, geography, and even English classes. Stu dents can learn to write essays, read graphs, and discuss global issues. Based on the arguments above we can conclude that teaching students about climate change is very important. It helps them understand the world, become responsible, and improve their academic skills. Schools should include climate education in every level so young people can help protect the planet for the future."),
        Question("kp39", "What did Wangari Maathai primarily do to add ress environmental and social issues in Kenya?", listOf("She focused solely on providing education for women in urban areas.", "She founded an organization to plant trees while simultaneously empowering women and their rights.", "She worked for the government to create laws that stop people from cutting down trees.", "She traveled across Africa to study various species of trees and forest conservation.", "She organized protests to demand that the government give more money to rural families."), 1, "Maathai mendirikan Green Belt Movement: menanam pohon sambil memberdayakan perempuan.", passage = "Wangari Maathai: A Voice for the Environment and Women Wangari Maathai was a Kenyan environmentalist, political activist, and the first African woman to receive the Nobel Peace Prize. She was born on April 1, 1940, in Nyeri, a rural area in central Kenya. From a young age, Wangari showed a strong interest in learning and the environment. She studied in the United States and later earned a PhD from the University of Nairobi, becoming the first woman in East and Central Africa to achieve this. Her passion for education, the environment, and women’s rights led her to create the Green Belt Movement in 1977. This organization encouraged women to plant trees to fight deforestation, provide firewood, and create income for families. Wangari believed that taking care of the environment was closely linked to peace, democracy, and human rights. Through tree planting, she helped communities. Understand their power to change the future. Over the years, her movement led to the planting of more than 50 million trees across Kenya and beyond. She faced many challenges, including opposition from the government and even arrest. However, she remained strong and continued to speak out. In 2004, she was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize for her efforts to protect the environment and promote social justice. Wangari Maathai passed away in 2011, but her legacy lives on. She inspired people around the world to care for the earth and to stand up for what they believe is right. Her life showed that one person’s actions can truly make a difference. (Adapted from: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/pea ce/2004/maathai/biographical/)"),
        Question("kp40", "Which of the following statements about Maathai is true according to the text?", listOf("She was the first woman in East and Central Africa to receive a PhD.", "Her movement focused on planting trees only in rural parts of the United States.", "She gave up her environmental movement after being arrested by the government.", "The Nobel Peace Prize she received was mainly for her work in the field of tourism.", "She believed that environmental protection has no connection to human rights."), 0, "Teks menyebut ia perempuan pertama di Afrika Timur dan Tengah yang meraih gelar PhD.", passage = "Wangari Maathai: A Voice for the Environment and Women Wangari Maathai was a Kenyan environmentalist, political activist, and the first African woman to receive the Nobel Peace Prize. She was born on April 1, 1940, in Nyeri, a rural area in central Kenya. From a young age, Wangari showed a strong interest in learning and the environment. She studied in the United States and later earned a PhD from the University of Nairobi, becoming the first woman in East and Central Africa to achieve this. Her passion for education, the environment, and women’s rights led her to create the Green Belt Movement in 1977. This organization encouraged women to plant trees to fight deforestation, provide firewood, and create income for families. Wangari believed that taking care of the environment was closely linked to peace, democracy, and human rights. Through tree planting, she helped communities. Understand their power to change the future. Over the years, her movement led to the planting of more than 50 million trees across Kenya and beyond. She faced many challenges, including opposition from the government and even arrest. However, she remained strong and continued to speak out. In 2004, she was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize for her efforts to protect the environment and promote social justice. Wangari Maathai passed away in 2011, but her legacy lives on. She inspired people around the world to care for the earth and to stand up for what they believe is right. Her life showed that one person’s actions can truly make a difference. (Adapted from: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/pea ce/2004/maathai/biographical/)"),
        Question("kp41", "In which step does the user receive a unique number to monitor the status of their money movement?", listOf("Step 1: Create and Verify Your Account", "Step 2: Enter Transfer Details", "Step 3: Choose Payment Method", "Step 4: Send and Track the Transfer", "Step 5: Notify the Receiver"), 3, "Step 4: setelah konfirmasi, pengguna mendapat nomor konfirmasi/tracking untuk memantau transfer.", passage = "How to Transfer Money Internationally with Wise Wise (formerly known as TransferWise) is a global financial technology company that specializes in international money transfers. It was founded in 2011 and is headquartered in London, UK. Transferring money abroad with Wise is fast, cheap, and secure. If you want to send money from one country to another, follow these steps carefully to do it correctly. Step 1: Create and Verify Your Account First, go to Wise’s website or download the app. Register by entering your email address, name, and other details. You may need to verify your identity. This keeps the service safe for everyone. Wise uses two-factor authentication and monitors transactions to protect you. Step 2: Enter Transfer Details Next, choose the amount you want to send and the currency your recipient will receive. Decide who will receive the money and how (bank account, mobile wallet, etc.). Wise shows you the fees and current exchange rate before you confirm. This helps avoid surprises. Step 3: Choose Payment Method Choose how to pay for the transfer. You can use your bank account, a debit or credit card, or other supported payment methods. Each method has different fees and speed. Wise often offers lower fees when paying via bank transfer. Step 4: Send and Track the Transfer After entering all necessary details and payment, confirm the transfer. You will get a confirmation or tracking number. You can use this to check progress and see when the recipient will get the money. Step 5: Notify the Receiver Once the transfer is on its way, tell the recipient that the money is coming. Share the expected arrival time and any reference or tracking number so they can watch for the funds. (Adapted from: https://wise.com/gb/send-money/)"),
        Question("kp42", "Based on the transition in Neola’s behavior, which of the following statements correctly describe her financial transformation?", listOf("She shifted from impulsive spending to a disciplined, categorized budgeting system.", "She realized that earning a salary didn’t guarantee financial independence even with proper management.", "She decided to rely solely on digital applications because the physical envelope system was too difficult to maintain.", "She didn’t integrate both traditional and modern tools to monitor her cash flow and ensure she stays within her limits.", "She successfully increased her monthly income by taking advice from her older brother on how to get a promotion."), 0, "Neola berubah dari belanja impulsif menjadi disiplin dengan sistem amplop per kategori.", passage = "Big Lessons from a Small Paycheck Last year, Neola started her first job as a cashier at a small supermarket. She was excited to earn her own salary and finally feel independent. At first, she enjoyed the freedom. “I can finally buy whatever I want,” she told her friend on her first payday. Neola spent money on new clothes, ate out almost every day, and even bought a new phone with monthly payments. But after two months, Neola noticed a problem. By the end of each month, her bank account was almost empty, One day, she didn’t have enough money for the bus and almost missed her shift. “I don’t understand where all my money goes,” she said sadly to her coworker. That evening, she spoke with her older brother, who was good at managing money. After listening to her, he said, “You need a plan. Why don’t you try the envelope system?” “The envelope system?” Neola asked. “Yes,” he explained. “You divide your salary into envelopes for rent, food, transport, savings, and fun. When an envelope is empty, you stop spending in that category.” Neola agreed to try it. At first, it was hard to say no to eating out or shopping. But she followed the plan. “It’s not easy, but I like seeing money still in my account,” she said after a few weeks. Now, Neola uses both real envelopes and a budgeting app to track her spending. She no longer borrows money or worries at the end of the month. “I feel so much more in control,” she told her brother. Her experience taught her that learning how to manage money is just as important as earning it especially when starting a new job."),
        Question("kp43", "According to the text, which of the following statements are true regarding money management and budgeting strategies?", listOf("Cutting down on “wants” such as sub scriptions or eating out is the second step when running out of money.", "The Pay-Yourself-First method suggests that you should spend all your money before putting some into savings.", "Saving for an emergency fund or buying a new phone is considered a long-term financial goal.", "In the Envelope Method, you must stop spending in a specific category once the allocated money is finished.", "A budget plan should never be changed once it is created to ensure the user stays consistent."), 3, "Envelope Method: berhenti belanja di kategori yang amplopnya sudah kosong.", passage = "Easy Guide to Making a Budget Budgeting helps you manage money wisely so you don’t run out and can save for things you want. Follow these steps: Step 1: Know Your Real Income Find out how much money you actually get (your allowance, part-time job pay, or pocket money). This is what you can spend not the “bigger number” before deductions. Step 2: Track Your Spending Write down everything you buy for a few weeks: snacks, transport, phone credit, clothes, etc. Put them into two groups: a. b. Fixed expenses: things you always pay (like internet bills or school transport). Variable expenses: things that change (food, hangouts, movies). Variable expenses are usually where you can save. Step 3: Set Your Goals Decide what you’re saving for. Short-term goals (1-3 years) could be buying a new phone or building an emergency fund. Long-term goals might be saving for college or even your first motorbike. Step 4: Make a Plan Compare your income and spending. Create limits for each category (needs, wants, and savings). Ad just until you can cover your essentials and still save a little. Step 5: Pick a Method Choose a style that works for you: a) b) c) d) 50/30/20 Rule: 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings. Envelope Method: Use envelopes or e- wallets for each category. When one is empty, stop spending in that category. Zero-Based Budget: Assign every rupiah a job nothing left unplanned. Pay-Yourself-First: Save first, then spend what’s left. Step 6: Adjust Your Spending If you run out of money, cut “wants” first (like online games, subscriptions, or cating out). Even small changes, like making coffee at home, can save a lot. Step 7: Review Regularly Check your budget every month. If your allowance, job, or goals change, update your plan. This keeps you on track. With a budget, you’ll always know where your money goes and you’ll be closer to reaching your goals. (Adapted from: https://bettermoneyhabits.bankofamericcom/en/saving- budgeting/creating-a-budget)"),
        Question("kp44", "What can be inferred about the narrator’s initial reaction to the virus warnings on the laptop?", listOf("The narrator immediately recognized the severity of the situation and sought expert help.", "The narrator was indifferent because they had already backed up all their important files.", "The narrator underestimated the threat, assuming it was a minor issue that could be easily closed.", "The narrator suspected that their friend who studied computer science was responsible for the pop-ups.", "The narrator intentionally downloaded the malware to test the laptop’s security system."), 2, "Awalnya narator tidak panik dan hanya menutup pop-up → meremehkan ancaman.", passage = "I never really thought about digital security until one night last month. I was doing my homework on my laptop, when suddenly my screen was filled with strange pop-ups and warning messages about viruses. At first I didn’t panic and just tried to close it, but more and more pop-ups appeared, and my laptop started to feel slow. A few moments later, I realized something was wrong. Some important files on my desktop, including the draft of the assignment I was working on, just disappeared. I tried searching in various folders, but there are none. Then, I received a notification saying that one of my social media accounts had been hacked. Panic finally appeared. I feel scared and confused, don’t know what to do. In that despair, I contacted a friend who studied computer science. He calmly guided me. First, he told me to disconnect the internet immediately. Then, he explained that I may have downloaded malware from an unsafe site. It helped me scan the laptop with trusted antivirus software, and slowly, we managed to clean the system. We also immediately changed all my passwords, especially for email and bank accounts, to stronger passwords. That bad experience becomes a valuable lesson. I realized how vulnerable our digital data is. Since then, I have become more careful when browsing the internet. I no longer click links or download files from unknown sources. I also started using a pas sword manager and enabled two-factor authentication for all important accounts. That moment of panic has turned me into an individual who is more aware of the importance of digital security."),
        Question("kp45", "What is the primary purpose of the writer in sharing this personal experience?", listOf("To criticize the quality of current antivirus software available on the market.", "To provide a technical tutorial on how to hack social media accounts safely.", "To entertain readers with a fictional story about a student’s struggle with home work.", "To raise awareness among internet users about the importance of proactive digital security.", "To discourage people from using the internet for doing academic assignments at night."), 3, "Pengalaman ini dibagikan untuk menyadarkan pembaca tentang pentingnya keamanan digital.", passage = "I never really thought about digital security until one night last month. I was doing my homework on my laptop, when suddenly my screen was filled with strange pop-ups and warning messages about viruses. At first I didn’t panic and just tried to close it, but more and more pop-ups appeared, and my laptop started to feel slow. A few moments later, I realized something was wrong. Some important files on my desktop, including the draft of the assignment I was working on, just disappeared. I tried searching in various folders, but there are none. Then, I received a notification saying that one of my social media accounts had been hacked. Panic finally appeared. I feel scared and confused, don’t know what to do. In that despair, I contacted a friend who studied computer science. He calmly guided me. First, he told me to disconnect the internet immediately. Then, he explained that I may have downloaded malware from an unsafe site. It helped me scan the laptop with trusted antivirus software, and slowly, we managed to clean the system. We also immediately changed all my passwords, especially for email and bank accounts, to stronger passwords. That bad experience becomes a valuable lesson. I realized how vulnerable our digital data is. Since then, I have become more careful when browsing the internet. I no longer click links or download files from unknown sources. I also started using a pas sword manager and enabled two-factor authentication for all important accounts. That moment of panic has turned me into an individual who is more aware of the importance of digital security."),
        Question("kp46", "What might have happened if the narrator had not immediately disconnected the internet and changed their passwords after the attack?", listOf("The malware would have physically over heated the laptop and caused a permanent fire.", "The hacker could have gained further access to sensitive personal data, such as bank accounts.", "The lost assignment drafts would have automatically reappeared in the original folders.", "The friend who studied computer science would not have been able to help with the antivirus scan.", "The strange pop-ups would have eventually disappeared on their own after the laptop was turned off."), 1, "Tanpa memutus internet dan mengganti kata sandi, peretas bisa mengakses data penting seperti rekening bank.", passage = "I never really thought about digital security until one night last month. I was doing my homework on my laptop, when suddenly my screen was filled with strange pop-ups and warning messages about viruses. At first I didn’t panic and just tried to close it, but more and more pop-ups appeared, and my laptop started to feel slow. A few moments later, I realized something was wrong. Some important files on my desktop, including the draft of the assignment I was working on, just disappeared. I tried searching in various folders, but there are none. Then, I received a notification saying that one of my social media accounts had been hacked. Panic finally appeared. I feel scared and confused, don’t know what to do. In that despair, I contacted a friend who studied computer science. He calmly guided me. First, he told me to disconnect the internet immediately. Then, he explained that I may have downloaded malware from an unsafe site. It helped me scan the laptop with trusted antivirus software, and slowly, we managed to clean the system. We also immediately changed all my passwords, especially for email and bank accounts, to stronger passwords. That bad experience becomes a valuable lesson. I realized how vulnerable our digital data is. Since then, I have become more careful when browsing the internet. I no longer click links or download files from unknown sources. I also started using a pas sword manager and enabled two-factor authentication for all important accounts. That moment of panic has turned me into an individual who is more aware of the importance of digital security."),
        Question("kp47", "According to the third paragraph, what specific opportunity is provided to hospitality workers by the location of the eco-lodges?", listOf("The chance to build their own solar energy panels and organic farms.", "Direct collaboration with international researchers and local communities.", "A guaranteed career path as a researcher in protected national parks.", "The opportunity to manage global conservation funds for the government.", "Exclusive access to live inside the protected national parks permanently."), 1, "Paragraf ketiga: lokasi dekat taman nasional memungkinkan pekerja berinteraksi dengan konservasionis, peneliti, dan masyarakat lokal.", passage = "Lodges in Costa Rica: Hospitality Training in Nature Costa Rica is a leader in sustainable tourism, offering eco-lodges that provide hospitality training and career opportunities. These lodges are surrounded by lush rainforests, flowing rivers, and diverse wildlife, creating a unique learning environment for those interested in eco-friendly hospitality. The surroundings of these lodges are breathtaking. Towering trees stretch toward the sky, providing shade and shelter for colorful birds and playful monkeys. The air is fresh, filled with the scent of wildflowers and damp earth. Nearby rivers flow gently, offering a peaceful atmosphere for both guests and workers. Many lodges are located near protected national parks, where hospitality workers can interact with conservationists, researchers, and local communities. This allows them to gain hands-on experience in both tourism and environmental protection. Eco-lodges in Costa Rica teach guest services, housekeeping, eco- tour guiding, and sustainable hotel management. Many lodges use solar energy, rainwater collection, and organic farming, ensuring that trainees learn environmentally responsible practices. Eco-lodges provide job opportunities in areas such as front desk management, food service, and tour guiding. Employees also learn about sustainability, including energy conservation and eco-friendly business practices. Working in an eco-lodge allows individuals to develop hospitality skills while supporting conservation efforts. Employees gain experience in guest relations, sustainable tourism, and nature- based hospitality, making it a rewarding career path. Costa Rica’s eco-lodges offer a unique blend of tourism, education, and sustainability, making them excellent places for hospitality training and career development. These lodges foster a deep connection between people and nature, allowing workers to experience the beauty of Costa Rica’s landscapes while contributing to their preservation. Choosing a career in an eco-lodge means embracing a lifestyle that supports sustainability, cultural appreciation, and a greener future for travel. (Source https://global-studies.sherthanastories.com/eco tourism-in costa rica/index.html https//www.nikonilifestyles.com/blog/costa-ricas-innova tive- tourism-embraces-sustainability https://ticotimes.net/2025/06/20/costa-rica-green-hotels lead- global-suistainable-tourism https://enchanting-costarica.com/where-to-stay/top tripadvisor-greenleader-award-given-to-costa-rica-eco lodge/)"),
        Question("kp48", "What can be inferred about the training program provided by eco-lodges in Costa Rica?", listOf("It focuses entirely on environmental science rather than traditional hotel services.", "It is designed to prepare students for careers in high-tech urban hotel management.", "It integrates professional hospitality skills with environmentally responsible ethics.", "It requires trainees to have a background in organic farming before they can join.", "It is primarily intended for tourists who want to learn how to guide themselves."), 2, "Pelatihan menggabungkan keterampilan hospitality dengan praktik ramah lingkungan (tenaga surya, air hujan, pertanian organik).", passage = "Lodges in Costa Rica: Hospitality Training in Nature Costa Rica is a leader in sustainable tourism, offering eco-lodges that provide hospitality training and career opportunities. These lodges are surrounded by lush rainforests, flowing rivers, and diverse wildlife, creating a unique learning environment for those interested in eco-friendly hospitality. The surroundings of these lodges are breathtaking. Towering trees stretch toward the sky, providing shade and shelter for colorful birds and playful monkeys. The air is fresh, filled with the scent of wildflowers and damp earth. Nearby rivers flow gently, offering a peaceful atmosphere for both guests and workers. Many lodges are located near protected national parks, where hospitality workers can interact with conservationists, researchers, and local communities. This allows them to gain hands-on experience in both tourism and environmental protection. Eco-lodges in Costa Rica teach guest services, housekeeping, eco- tour guiding, and sustainable hotel management. Many lodges use solar energy, rainwater collection, and organic farming, ensuring that trainees learn environmentally responsible practices. Eco-lodges provide job opportunities in areas such as front desk management, food service, and tour guiding. Employees also learn about sustainability, including energy conservation and eco-friendly business practices. Working in an eco-lodge allows individuals to develop hospitality skills while supporting conservation efforts. Employees gain experience in guest relations, sustainable tourism, and nature- based hospitality, making it a rewarding career path. Costa Rica’s eco-lodges offer a unique blend of tourism, education, and sustainability, making them excellent places for hospitality training and career development. These lodges foster a deep connection between people and nature, allowing workers to experience the beauty of Costa Rica’s landscapes while contributing to their preservation. Choosing a career in an eco-lodge means embracing a lifestyle that supports sustainability, cultural appreciation, and a greener future for travel. (Source https://global-studies.sherthanastories.com/eco tourism-in costa rica/index.html https//www.nikonilifestyles.com/blog/costa-ricas-innova tive- tourism-embraces-sustainability https://ticotimes.net/2025/06/20/costa-rica-green-hotels lead- global-suistainable-tourism https://enchanting-costarica.com/where-to-stay/top tripadvisor-greenleader-award-given-to-costa-rica-eco lodge/)"),
        Question("kp49", "What is the author’s primary goal in describing the environment and practices of Costa Rica’s eco-lodges?", listOf("To persuade readers to spend their next vacation at an expensive luxury lodge.", "To criticize the lack of technology used in modern hotel management in Costa Rica.", "To explain how nature-based tourism can be a platform for career development and sustainability.", "To provide a scientific report on the diver se wildlife found in lush rainforests.", "To warn employees about the difficulties of working in remote areas like flowing rivers."), 2, "Penulis menjelaskan bagaimana eco-lodge menjadi tempat pengembangan karier sekaligus mendukung keberlanjutan.", passage = "Lodges in Costa Rica: Hospitality Training in Nature Costa Rica is a leader in sustainable tourism, offering eco-lodges that provide hospitality training and career opportunities. These lodges are surrounded by lush rainforests, flowing rivers, and diverse wildlife, creating a unique learning environment for those interested in eco-friendly hospitality. The surroundings of these lodges are breathtaking. Towering trees stretch toward the sky, providing shade and shelter for colorful birds and playful monkeys. The air is fresh, filled with the scent of wildflowers and damp earth. Nearby rivers flow gently, offering a peaceful atmosphere for both guests and workers. Many lodges are located near protected national parks, where hospitality workers can interact with conservationists, researchers, and local communities. This allows them to gain hands-on experience in both tourism and environmental protection. Eco-lodges in Costa Rica teach guest services, housekeeping, eco- tour guiding, and sustainable hotel management. Many lodges use solar energy, rainwater collection, and organic farming, ensuring that trainees learn environmentally responsible practices. Eco-lodges provide job opportunities in areas such as front desk management, food service, and tour guiding. Employees also learn about sustainability, including energy conservation and eco-friendly business practices. Working in an eco-lodge allows individuals to develop hospitality skills while supporting conservation efforts. Employees gain experience in guest relations, sustainable tourism, and nature- based hospitality, making it a rewarding career path. Costa Rica’s eco-lodges offer a unique blend of tourism, education, and sustainability, making them excellent places for hospitality training and career development. These lodges foster a deep connection between people and nature, allowing workers to experience the beauty of Costa Rica’s landscapes while contributing to their preservation. Choosing a career in an eco-lodge means embracing a lifestyle that supports sustainability, cultural appreciation, and a greener future for travel. (Source https://global-studies.sherthanastories.com/eco tourism-in costa rica/index.html https//www.nikonilifestyles.com/blog/costa-ricas-innova tive- tourism-embraces-sustainability https://ticotimes.net/2025/06/20/costa-rica-green-hotels lead- global-suistainable-tourism https://enchanting-costarica.com/where-to-stay/top tripadvisor-greenleader-award-given-to-costa-rica-eco lodge/)"),
        Question("kp50", "According to the text, what are the primary environmental threats currently endangering Egypt’s agricultural sector?", listOf("The expansion of the Sahara Desert into the city of Cairo.", "Rising sea levels from the Mediterranean Sea flooding the Nile Delta.", "Soil damage isn’t caused by the intrusion of saltwater into fertile land.", "Regular rainfall patterns making farming more difficult for the people.", "The complete disappearance of the Nile River due to extreme heat."), 1, "Teks menyebut naiknya permukaan Laut Mediterania membanjiri Delta Nil, wilayah paling subur.", passage = "Egypt: A Land of Wonders and Climate Challenges Egypt is a country in northeastern Africa that is famous for its pyramids, the Nile River, and wide deserts. It is a land where ancient history meets modern life, making it one of the most fascinating countries in the world. Egypt’s landscape is dominated by the Sahara Desert and the Nile River, which has been the lifeline of the country for thousands of years. The Nile makes farming possible in an otherwise dry land. Cities like Cairo are busy and modern, while the deserts and ancient monuments reflect Egypt’s rich cultural heritage. However, Egypt also faces serious challenges from climate change. The weather is becoming hotter, and rainfall is no longer regular. This situation makes farming more difficult and worsens water scarcity. In the north, rising sea levels from the Mediterranean Sea are flooding parts of the Nile Delta, which is the most fertile area of the country. Saltwater also damages the soil, reducing food production. These problems have a strong impact on people’s lives. Farmers lose their farmland, families face poverty and hunger, and some communities may have to move. At the same time, the government needs to spend more money on adaptation, such as protecting the coast and saving water. This situation creates economic difficulties and social pressures, especially for vulnerable groups. Even so, Egypt still has hope. The Nile River remains its greatest strength. With better water management, sustainable farming, and stronger climate policies, Egypt can protect its people and secure its future. (Adapted from: https://carnegieendowment.org/ research/2023/10/climate-change-in-)"),
        Question("kp51", "Which of the following social and economic impacts are mentioned as results of the climate crisis in Egypt?", listOf("Decreased government spending on coastal protection and water saving.", "Communities being forced to relocate or move due to environmental issues.", "Families don’t face economic struggles.", "A significant increase in tourism revenue due to warmer weather.", "Farmers becoming wealthier by selling salt collected from the flooded land."), 1, "Teks menyebut sebagian komunitas mungkin harus pindah (relokasi).", passage = "Egypt: A Land of Wonders and Climate Challenges Egypt is a country in northeastern Africa that is famous for its pyramids, the Nile River, and wide deserts. It is a land where ancient history meets modern life, making it one of the most fascinating countries in the world. Egypt’s landscape is dominated by the Sahara Desert and the Nile River, which has been the lifeline of the country for thousands of years. The Nile makes farming possible in an otherwise dry land. Cities like Cairo are busy and modern, while the deserts and ancient monuments reflect Egypt’s rich cultural heritage. However, Egypt also faces serious challenges from climate change. The weather is becoming hotter, and rainfall is no longer regular. This situation makes farming more difficult and worsens water scarcity. In the north, rising sea levels from the Mediterranean Sea are flooding parts of the Nile Delta, which is the most fertile area of the country. Saltwater also damages the soil, reducing food production. These problems have a strong impact on people’s lives. Farmers lose their farmland, families face poverty and hunger, and some communities may have to move. At the same time, the government needs to spend more money on adaptation, such as protecting the coast and saving water. This situation creates economic difficulties and social pressures, especially for vulnerable groups. Even so, Egypt still has hope. The Nile River remains its greatest strength. With better water management, sustainable farming, and stronger climate policies, Egypt can protect its people and secure its future. (Adapted from: https://carnegieendowment.org/ research/2023/10/climate-change-in-)"),
        Question("kp91", "Based on the text, all of the following are des criptions of Lampuuk Beach, EXCEPT....", listOf("It has soft white sand and clear blue water.", "Palm trees provide shade along the shore.", "The waves roll gently toward the beach in the afternoon.", "The beach is surrounded by tall pine trees and hiking trails.", "The sunset creates warm golden colors in the sky."), 3, "Lampuuk digambarkan berpasir putih, berair biru, berpohon kelapa, dengan senja keemasan. Pohon pinus dan jalur pendakian bukan ciri Lampuuk.", passage = "Exploring Aceh’s Natural Wonders Aceh, a province located at the northern tip of Sumatra, Indonesia, is well known for its strong culture and warm hospitality. However, beyond its traditions and history, Aceh also offers natural attractions that impress visitors from many parts of the world. From cool highlands to beautiful beaches, Aceh presents a unique combination of peaceful scenery and rich biodiversity. In the central highlands, travelers can visit Lake Laut Tawar, a large freshwater lake surrounded by green hills and fresh mountain air. The lake looks calm and wide, reflecting the blue sky on its surface. Early in the morning, thin mist rises gently above the water, creating a quiet and magical at mosphere. Local fishermen often row small boats across the lake, while birds fly low above the water. The cool temperature and natural beauty make this area a perfect place to relax and enjoy the peaceful side of Aceh. Not far from the lake, visitors may explore the Bur Ni Telong mountain area, which is famous for its forests and scenic views. Tall pine trees cover the hills, and the air feels clean and refreshing. Along the hiking trails, small streams flow between rocks, and wildflowers grow naturally on the roadside. From the higher points, travelers can see wide valleys and distant mountains. The calm environment and natural sounds of the forest create an unforgettable experience for nature lovers. Heading toward the western coast, tourists can also enjoy the beauty of Lampuuk Beach, one of Aceh’s most popular coastal destinations. The beach has soft white sand and clear blue water. Palm trees stand along the shore, providing shade for visitors who want to rest. In the afternoon, the waves roll gently toward the beach, and the sunlight turns golden as the sun begins to set. The peaceful so und of the ocean and the warm colors of the sky make Lampuuk Beach a perfect place to end a day of travel. These natural wonders show Aceh’s richness in both landscape and wildlife. By visiting and appreciating these places, tourists not only enjoy beautiful scenery but also help support local communities and encourage conservation efforts. In this way, Aceh’s natural treasures can continue to be protected and enjoyed by future generations."),
        Question("kp92", "Which statement is NOT supported by the text?", listOf("Lake Laut Tawar is located in the highlands", "Bur Ni Telong offers hiking trails", "Lampuuk Beach has coral reefs and mangrove swamps", "The air in Bur Ni Telong feels clean", "Aceh combines coastal and highland scenery"), 2, "Teks tidak menyebut terumbu karang dan rawa bakau di Pantai Lampuuk.", passage = "Exploring Aceh’s Natural Wonders Aceh, a province located at the northern tip of Sumatra, Indonesia, is well known for its strong culture and warm hospitality. However, beyond its traditions and history, Aceh also offers natural attractions that impress visitors from many parts of the world. From cool highlands to beautiful beaches, Aceh presents a unique combination of peaceful scenery and rich biodiversity. In the central highlands, travelers can visit Lake Laut Tawar, a large freshwater lake surrounded by green hills and fresh mountain air. The lake looks calm and wide, reflecting the blue sky on its surface. Early in the morning, thin mist rises gently above the water, creating a quiet and magical at mosphere. Local fishermen often row small boats across the lake, while birds fly low above the water. The cool temperature and natural beauty make this area a perfect place to relax and enjoy the peaceful side of Aceh. Not far from the lake, visitors may explore the Bur Ni Telong mountain area, which is famous for its forests and scenic views. Tall pine trees cover the hills, and the air feels clean and refreshing. Along the hiking trails, small streams flow between rocks, and wildflowers grow naturally on the roadside. From the higher points, travelers can see wide valleys and distant mountains. The calm environment and natural sounds of the forest create an unforgettable experience for nature lovers. Heading toward the western coast, tourists can also enjoy the beauty of Lampuuk Beach, one of Aceh’s most popular coastal destinations. The beach has soft white sand and clear blue water. Palm trees stand along the shore, providing shade for visitors who want to rest. In the afternoon, the waves roll gently toward the beach, and the sunlight turns golden as the sun begins to set. The peaceful so und of the ocean and the warm colors of the sky make Lampuuk Beach a perfect place to end a day of travel. These natural wonders show Aceh’s richness in both landscape and wildlife. By visiting and appreciating these places, tourists not only enjoy beautiful scenery but also help support local communities and encourage conservation efforts. In this way, Aceh’s natural treasures can continue to be protected and enjoyed by future generations."),
        Question("kp93", "Which of the following can be inferred from the text about Borobudur Temple?", listOf("Borobudur was built mainly to attract international tourists.", "The relief panels only serve as decoration and have no educational purpose.", "Protecting Borobudur requires rules because tourism can cause damage.", "Visitors are free to climb to the top without any restrictions.", "Borobudur is no longer considered important for Indonesian culture."), 2, "Teks menekankan aturan pengunjung karena pariwisata bisa merusak candi.", passage = "Borobudur Temple Borobudur Temple is one of the most remarkable historical sites in Indonesia and a world-famous cultural landmark. It is located in Magelang, Central Java, and attracts visitors from many countries every year. Built in the 9th century during the Sailendra dynasty, Borobudur is the largest Buddhist temple in the world. Today, it is not only a place of worship, but also an important symbol of Indonesian heritage. The temple is designed in the form of a giant mandala, which represents the Buddhist view of the universe. Borobudur consists of nine levels, including six square platforms and three circular ones at the top. On the upper levels, visitors can see dozens of bell-shaped stupas, each containing a statue of Buddha inside. The temple walls are also covered with more than 2,600 relief panels that tell stories about moral values, daily life, and spiritual journeys. One of the most interesting aspects of Borobudur is how it combines art, architecture, and education. The relief panels do not only serve as decoration, but also act as a “stone book” that teaches lessons about kindness, patience, and self-control. This shows that ancient people did not build monuments only for beauty, but also for learning and reflection. However, Borobudur also faces modern challenges. As tourism increases, the temple becomes more vulnerable to damage caused by overcrowding and pollution. For this reason, the government and cultural organizations have introduced rules to protect the site, such as limiting the number of visitors who can climb to the top. These efforts show that preserving history requires responsibility, not just admiration. In recent years, Borobudur has also been connected to environmental awareness. The surrounding area is being developed with more eco-friendly tourism, including waste management and sustainable transportation. This helps visitors understand that protecting cultural heritage is closely related to protecting nature, since both are valuable for future generations. Overall, Borobudur Temple is an extraordinary place that offers more than just a beautiful view. It teaches us about history, spirituality, and human creativity. If people visit it with respect and care, Borobudur will continue to inspire the world for many years to come."),
        Question("kp94", "“As tourism increases, the temple becomes more vulnerable to damage caused by overcrowding and pollution.” This sentence implies that...", listOf("Tourism always improves the condition of historical sites.", "Borobudur can be damaged if too many visitors come without control.", "Overcrowding only affects the area outside the temple, not the temple itself.", "Pollution is not a serious problem for ancient buildings.", "The temple is already fully protected and cannot be harmed anymore."), 1, "Kalimat itu berarti candi bisa rusak bila pengunjung terlalu banyak tanpa pengendalian.", passage = "Borobudur Temple Borobudur Temple is one of the most remarkable historical sites in Indonesia and a world-famous cultural landmark. It is located in Magelang, Central Java, and attracts visitors from many countries every year. Built in the 9th century during the Sailendra dynasty, Borobudur is the largest Buddhist temple in the world. Today, it is not only a place of worship, but also an important symbol of Indonesian heritage. The temple is designed in the form of a giant mandala, which represents the Buddhist view of the universe. Borobudur consists of nine levels, including six square platforms and three circular ones at the top. On the upper levels, visitors can see dozens of bell-shaped stupas, each containing a statue of Buddha inside. The temple walls are also covered with more than 2,600 relief panels that tell stories about moral values, daily life, and spiritual journeys. One of the most interesting aspects of Borobudur is how it combines art, architecture, and education. The relief panels do not only serve as decoration, but also act as a “stone book” that teaches lessons about kindness, patience, and self-control. This shows that ancient people did not build monuments only for beauty, but also for learning and reflection. However, Borobudur also faces modern challenges. As tourism increases, the temple becomes more vulnerable to damage caused by overcrowding and pollution. For this reason, the government and cultural organizations have introduced rules to protect the site, such as limiting the number of visitors who can climb to the top. These efforts show that preserving history requires responsibility, not just admiration. In recent years, Borobudur has also been connected to environmental awareness. The surrounding area is being developed with more eco-friendly tourism, including waste management and sustainable transportation. This helps visitors understand that protecting cultural heritage is closely related to protecting nature, since both are valuable for future generations. Overall, Borobudur Temple is an extraordinary place that offers more than just a beautiful view. It teaches us about history, spirituality, and human creativity. If people visit it with respect and care, Borobudur will continue to inspire the world for many years to come."),
        Question("kp95", "What might have happened if the writer had not suggested another similar book to the student?", listOf("The student would have learned the catalog system by himself immediately.", "The student might have left the library without any useful source for the assignment.", "The missing book would have suddenly appeared on the shelf.", "The writer would have received the certificate earlier.", "The student would have gone to the librarian to complain about the writer’s poor service."), 1, "Tanpa saran buku lain, siswa itu kemungkinan pulang tanpa sumber untuk tugasnya.", passage = "My Experience as a Volunteer at a School Library Last semester, I had the chance to become a volunteer at my school library. It was my first time joining an official school program outside of class, and I felt both excited and nervous. The program lasted for three months, and during that time, I learned many valuable lessons about responsibility, teamwork, and patience. On my first week, the librarian introduced me to the daily tasks. I had to arrange books on the shelves, record borrowed books, and help students find the titles they needed. At first, everything felt confusing because the library used a catalog system that I had never used before. I often worried about placing books in the wrong section. However, the librarian was very supportive and taught me how to read the codes and organize the books correctly. In the second month, I faced a situation that tested my communication skills. One day, a student came to the library looking upset because he could not find a book needed for an assignment. I listened carefully and asked for the book’s title and the author’s name. After checking the catalog, I realized the book had been borrowed by another student and was not yet returned. Instead of leaving the student disappointed, I suggested another similar book and helped him take notes from it. The stu dent thanked me, and I felt happy because I had been able to help calmly. At the end of the program, the librarian held a short evaluation session for all volunteers. She told me that I had improved in organizing, problem-solving, and communicating with others. She also gave me a small certificate as a token of appreciation. I felt proud of myself because the experience taught me how to work responsibly and serve others. This volunteering program became one of the most meaningful experiences I have had at school."),
        Question("kp96", "What is the primary purpose of the writer in sharing this personal experience?", listOf("To provide a detailed guide on how to complete all school assignments perfectly.", "To entertain readers with a fictional story about a student’s busy week.", "To raise awareness about the importance of maintaining mental health and mana ging stress.", "To criticize teachers for giving too many assignments and activities.", "To encourage students to avoid participating in school clubs and activities."), 2, "Penulis ingin menyadarkan pembaca tentang pentingnya menjaga kesehatan mental dan mengelola stres.", passage = "I never really thought much about mental health until one stressful week last semester. I was trying to keep up with homework, club activities, and exam preparations, when suddenly I felt completely overwhelmed. At first, I just tried to push through, telling myself I could handle it, but the anxiety kept growing, and I found it difficult to concentrate on anything. A few days later, I realized something was seriously wrong. I was constantly exhausted, losing sleep, and even small mistakes in my assignments made me feel like a failure. I began avoiding friends and skipping meals because I felt too stressed to socialize or take care of myself. Then, during a class, I felt a sudden panic attack and could barely breathe. Fear and confusion hit me hard, I didn’t know how to calm myself down. In that moment of despair, I reached out to the school counselor. She listened patiently and explained that I was experiencing burnout and that it was okay to ask for help. She taught me some breathing exercises and time management techniques to handle stress better. Together, we created a plan to balance schoolwork and rest, and she encouraged me to talk to my teachers about manageable deadlines. That difficult experience became an important les son. I realized how fragile our mental health can be if we ignore it. Since then, I have started setting aside time for relaxation, exercising, and talking to friends when I feel stressed. I also learned to prioritize tasks and accept that I cannot do everything perfectly. That moment of panic turned me into a person who is more aware of my mental health and committed to taking care of myself."),
        Question("kp97", "What was one immediate effect of the writer’s stress?", listOf("Improved concentration on schoolwork.", "Constant exhaustion and panic attacks.", "Stronger relationships with classmates.", "Increased interest in joining more school activities.", "Better time management skills."), 1, "Dampak langsung stres yang diceritakan: kelelahan terus-menerus dan serangan panik.", passage = "I never really thought much about mental health until one stressful week last semester. I was trying to keep up with homework, club activities, and exam preparations, when suddenly I felt completely overwhelmed. At first, I just tried to push through, telling myself I could handle it, but the anxiety kept growing, and I found it difficult to concentrate on anything. A few days later, I realized something was seriously wrong. I was constantly exhausted, losing sleep, and even small mistakes in my assignments made me feel like a failure. I began avoiding friends and skipping meals because I felt too stressed to socialize or take care of myself. Then, during a class, I felt a sudden panic attack and could barely breathe. Fear and confusion hit me hard, I didn’t know how to calm myself down. In that moment of despair, I reached out to the school counselor. She listened patiently and explained that I was experiencing burnout and that it was okay to ask for help. She taught me some breathing exercises and time management techniques to handle stress better. Together, we created a plan to balance schoolwork and rest, and she encouraged me to talk to my teachers about manageable deadlines. That difficult experience became an important les son. I realized how fragile our mental health can be if we ignore it. Since then, I have started setting aside time for relaxation, exercising, and talking to friends when I feel stressed. I also learned to prioritize tasks and accept that I cannot do everything perfectly. That moment of panic turned me into a person who is more aware of my mental health and committed to taking care of myself."),
        Question("kp98", "Why is it important to provide air holes or turn the compost pile periodically?", listOf("To prevent insects from eating the com post.", "To ensure decomposing bacteria get enough oxygen.", "To keep vegetable scraps from turning brown.", "To prevent the compost from becoming too dry.", "To make the compost bin look neater in the yard."), 1, "Membalik tumpukan memberi oksigen agar bakteri pengurai bekerja lebih efektif.", passage = "Simple Guide to Home Composting Turning organic waste into compost at home is an excellent way to reduce landfill waste and create free nutrients for your plants. Follow these steps to get started: 1. 2. 3. 4. 5. Choose the Right Bin Use a dedicated compost bin or dig a hole in your backyard. Ensure the container has air holes to allow oxygen to enter, which speeds up the decomposition process. Balance “Green” and “Brown” Materials For healthy compost, you need a balance of two types of materials: Green Materials (Nitrogen): Vegetable scraps, fruit peels, and fresh grass clippings. Brown Materials (Carbon): Dry leaves, small twigs, shredded cardboard, and sawdust. Avoid Harmful Items Do not put meat, dairy products, oils, or pet waste into your compost. These items can cause unpleasant odors and attract pests like rodents. Maintain Moisture and Air The compost pile should feel damp, like a wrung-out sponge. Turn the pile every one or two weeks to provide air (oxygen), which helps decomposing bacteria work more efficiently. Use the Result After several months, the compost will turn into dark, rich soil. Use this to enrich your pot ted plants or garden to reduce your reliance on chemical fertilizers."),
        Question("kp99", "Which of the following best describes the les son Daniel learned from his cooking experience?", listOf("Talent alone is enough to succeed in cooking.", "Learning and practice are essential to achieve results.", "Recipes are unnecessary if you are creative.", "Cooking is impossible without professional training.", "Mistakes should be avoided by skipping difficult steps."), 1, "Daniel berhasil setelah belajar dan berlatih dengan sabar.", passage = "Big Lessons from a Small Kitchen Experiment Last summer, Daniel decided to learn how to cook at home. He was excited to try new recipes and feel independent. At first, he thought cooking would be easy. “I can just follow a recipe,” he told his friend on the first day. He tried making pasta and scram bled eggs, but often forgot ingredients or used too much salt. After a week, he noticed a problem. His meals didn’t taste very good, and sometimes he burned the food. One evening, he almost ruined dinner for his family. “I don’t understand why cooking is so hard,” he said disappointedly. That night, he spoke with his older sister, who loved cooking. After listening, she said, “You need a plan. Start simple and learn the basics first.” “Start simple?” Daniel asked. “Yes,” she explained. “Focus on one recipe at a time. Measure ingredients carefully, follow instructions step by step, and taste as you go. Take notes on what works and what doesn’t. Over time, you’ll improve.” Daniel agreed to try it. At first, it was challenging to follow every step carefully. But he practiced consistently. “It’s not easy, but I enjoy seeing my meals turn out better each time,” he said after a few weeks. Now, Daniel keeps a small cooking journal and watches tutorial videos to improve his skills. He can prepare breakfast, pasta dishes, and simple desserts without mistakes. He even cooks for his family on weekends. “I feel proud that I can make food that everyone enjoys,” he told his sister. His experience taught him that learning how to cook properly is just as important as trying new recipes, especially when starting small and practicing patiently."),
        Question("kp100", "What could happen if schools do not include digital literacy education for students?", listOf("Students might struggle to make responsible choices online.", "Students will automatically develop digital skills without guidance.", "Students will be completely safe online without instruction.", "Students will excel academically without technology knowledge.", "Students will ignore traditional subjects entirely."), 0, "Tanpa pendidikan literasi digital, siswa bisa kesulitan membuat keputusan yang bertanggung jawab di dunia maya.", passage = "Why Schools Should Teach More About Digital Literacy Digital literacy is one of the most important skills for students today. It affects how they learn, communicate, and stay safe online. Because of this, schools should teach more about digital literacy. Students need to understand how to use techno logy effectively and responsibly. First, students are the future workers and leaders in a technology-driven world. If they learn digital skills early, they can make better decisions online and offline. For example, they can identify fake news, use online tools efficiently, and manage their digital footprint. These actions may seem small, but if many students practice them, it can create a safer and smarter online community. Second, learning digital literacy helps students become more responsible citizens. They understand how their online behavior affects themselves and others. This can make them more careful when posting on social media, sharing information, or interacting with others online. For example, they might think before posting personal information or avoid cyberbullying. Third, teaching digital literacy can improve academic performance. Digital skills are useful in research, writing, and collaboration. Students can learn to search for reliable sources, create presentations, and communicate effectively in online platforms. These skills also help them in subjects like English, science, and social studies. Based on the arguments above, we can conclude that teaching students about digital literacy is very important. It helps them navigate the digital world safely, become responsible online, and enhance their academic skills. Schools should include digital literacy education at every level so students are prepared for the challenges of a digital future."),
    )

    private fun kompetenMatRaw() = listOf(
        Question("kp23", "Kecepatan reaksi kimia dengan suhu tertentu dapat dimodelkan secara linear dengan persamaan: v = 0,8 T + 5 dengan T adalah besar suhu (dalam °C) dan v adalah kecepatan reaksi (dalam satuan mmol/ detik). Jika kecepatan reaksi terstruktur sebesar 45 mmol/detik, berapakah suhu T pada saat itu?", listOf("42 °C", "47 °C", "48 °C", "50 °C", "55 °C"), 3, "0,8T + 5 = 45 → 0,8T = 40 → T = 50 °C."),
        Question("kp24", "Berapakah jumlah halaman yang dibaca siswa tersebut pada hari ke-6?", listOf("32 halaman", "33 halaman", "35 halaman", "36 halaman", "37 halaman"), 4, "Barisan aritmetika a = 12, b = 5. U₆ = 12 + 5 × 5 = 37 halaman.", passage = "Seorang siswa memantau jumlah halaman yang berhasil ia baca dari sebuah buku setiap harinya. Pada hari ke-1, ia berhasil membaca 12 halaman. Pada hari ke-2, jumlah halaman yang dibaca meningkat menjadi 17 halaman, dan pada hari ke-3 menjadi 22 halaman. Setiap hari jumlah halaman yang ia baca bertambah dengan pola yang sama selama beberapa hari berikutnya."),
        Question("kp25", "Pada pukul berapa populasi berada dalam kondisi stabil, tetapi belum perlu dipindahkan ke media baru?", listOf("10.00", "12.00", "14.00", "15.00", "18.00"), 2, "Tiap 2 jam dikali 1,3: 08.00 = 650, 10.00 = 845, 12.00 ≈ 1.099, 14.00 ≈ 1.428 (sudah > 1.200 dan < 2.000), 16.00 ≈ 1.856. Pilihan yang memenuhi: 14.00.", passage = "Sebuah kultur mikroorganisme memiliki 500 sel pada pukul 06.00. Jumlah sel tersebut bertambah 30% setiap 2 jam karena proses reproduksi. Diketahui bahwa: • • Populasi mikroorganisme dianggap stabil jika jumlah sel lebih dari 1.200. Populasi dianggap terlalu padat jika jum lah sel melebihi 2.000, sehingga kultur perlu segera dipindahkan ke media baru."),
        Question("kp28", "Putuskan apakah pernyataan (1) dan (2) cukup untuk menjawab pertanyaan tersebut.", listOf("Pernyataan (1) SAJA cukup untuk men jawab pertanyaan, tetapi pernyataan (2) SAJA tidak cukup.", "Pernyataan (2) SAJA cukup untuk menjawab pertanyaan, tetapi pernyataan (1) SAJA tidak cukup.", "Pernyataan (1) dan (2) cukup untuk men jawab pertanyaan, tetapi salah satu dari keduanya tidak cukup", "Pernyataan (1) ataupun pernyataan (2) SAJA sudah cukup untuk menjawab pertanyaan.", "Pernyataan (1) dan pernyataan (2) tidak cukup untuk menjawab pertanyaan."), 0, "Luas 10 = ½(a + b) × 4 → a + b = 5. Dengan (1), a = 2 dan b = 3; kaki = √(4² + 0,5²) ≈ 4,03 sehingga keliling ≈ 13,1 < 17, jadi terjawab. Dengan (2), a + b = 5 dan b = a + 4 memberi a = 0,5 (bukan bilangan asli), jadi tidak bisa dipakai. Jawaban A.", passage = "Suatu trapesium sama kaki dengan tinggi 4 cm dan luas 10 cm² memiliki panjang sisi sejajar (dalam cm) berupa bilangan asli a dan b dengan a < b. Apakah keliling trapesium tersebut kurang dari 17 cm?\n(1) b = a + 1\n(2) b = a + 4"),
        Question("kp32", "Berapa peluang tamu yang terpilih menggunakan pakaian berwarna putih?", listOf("35%", "40%", "45%", "55%", "60%"), 3, "Putih: laki-laki 15, perempuan 60 − 20 = 40. Total 55 dari 100 → 55%.", passage = "Dalam sebuah acara perayaan ulang tahun, para undangan diminta untuk menggunakan dresscode berupa pakaian berwarna biru atau putih. Terdapat 100 orang tamu undangan yang hadir pada perayaan ulang tahun tersebut. Panitia menghitung bahwa dari 40 orang tamu laki-laki, terdapat 15 orang laki-laki yang menggunakan pakaian berwarna putih dan sisanya berwarna biru. Sementara itu, untuk tamu perempuan 20 orang menggunakan pakaian berwarna biru dan sisanya putih. Untuk memeriahkan acara tersebut, pihak penyelenggara akan membagikan satu hadiah utama kepada salah satu peserta yang hadir. Panitia akan memilih satu orang tamu undangan secara acak untuk menerima hadiah tersebut."),
        Question("kp75", "Bentuk sederhana dari (27^(2/3) × a⁵ × b²) / (3⁴ × a² × b⁵) adalah ....", listOf("a³ / (3² b³)", "a³ / (3⁶ b³)", "a⁷ / (3² b⁷)", "3² a³ b³", "1 / (3² a³ b³)"), 0, "27^(2/3) = (∛27)² = 3² = 9. Jadi 3² × a⁵ × b² / (3⁴ × a² × b⁵) = a⁵⁻² / (3⁴⁻² × b⁵⁻²) = a³ / (3² b³)."),
        Question("kp76", "Jika seorang kurir menerima total gaji sebesar Rp187.500,00 dalam satu hari, jumlah paket yang berhasil diantarkan oleh kurir tersebut adalah….", listOf("45 paket", "50 paket", "55 paket", "60 paket", "65 paket"), 2, "2.500x + 50.000 = 187.500 → 2.500x = 137.500 → x = 55 paket.", passage = "Sebuah perusahaan ekspedisi menetapkan total gaji harian seorang kurir berdasarkan jumlah paket yang berhasil diantarkan. Hubungan tersebut dimodelkan dengan persamaan: y = 2.500x + 50.000 Keterangan: - - - - x adalah jumlah paket yang diantarkan. y adalah total gaji harian yang diterima (dalam Rupiah). 50.000 merupakan uang makan tetap per hari. 2.500 adalah komisi per paket."),
        Question("kp77", "Jika peneliti tersebut ingin mempre diksi ukuran daun pada hari ke-15, berapakah panjang daun tanaman tersebut?", listOf("37,5 cm", "40,0 cm", "42,5 cm", "45,0 cm", "47,5 cm"), 2, "Dari hari ke-4 ke ke-9 bertambah 12,5 cm dalam 5 hari → 2,5 cm/hari. Hari ke-15 = 27,5 + 6 × 2,5 = 42,5 cm.", passage = "Seorang peneliti botani sedang memantau pertumbuhan panjang daun sebuah tanaman langka. Berdasarkan hasil pengamatan: - - Pada hari ke-4, panjang daun tercatat 15 cm. Pada hari ke-9, panjang daun tercatat 27,5 cm. Tanaman tersebut diketahui memiliki pola pertumbuhan panjang yang konstan setiap harinya."),
        Question("kp78", "Berdasarkan data di atas, pada pukul berapa populasi berada dalam kondisi optimal namun belum mendesak untuk dipindahkan ke media baru (jumlah sel 4.000)?", listOf("14.00", "17.00", "20.00", "22.00", "02.00 (hari berikutnya)"), 4, "Tiap 3 jam dikali 1,25: 11.00 = 1.000, 14.00 = 1.250, 17.00 ≈ 1.563, 20.00 ≈ 1.953, 23.00 ≈ 2.441, 02.00 ≈ 3.052 (optimal dan < 4.000). Di antara pilihan, hanya 02.00 yang memenuhi.", passage = "Sebuah laboratorium bioteknologi sedang mengamati pertumbuhan bakteri X-200. Pada pukul 08.00, terdapat 800 sel dalam media nutrisi. Bakteri ini memiliki karakteristik reproduksi yang unik: jumlah selnya meningkat sebesar 25% setiap 3 jam. Namun, diketahui kondisi lingkungan memengaruhi efektivitas kultur sebagai berikut. - - - Kondisi Optimal: Populasi dianggap produktif jika jumlah sel berada di rentang 2.000 hingga 4.500 sel. Risiko Toksisitas: Jika populasi melebihi 4.500 sel, limbah metabolik menjadi racun sehingga 20% dari total populasi akan mati seketika pada jam tersebut sebelum melanjutkan pertumbuhan ber ikutnya. Media Baru: Kultur harus segera dipindahkan ke tangki besar jika jumlah sel sudah melampaui 4.000 sel untuk menjaga kualitas."),
        Question("kp79", "Berdasarkan ketentuan di atas, manakah bidang di bawah ini yang mungkin menjadi posisi atau jalur pemasangan sekat kaca tersebut?", listOf("Bidang PSWT (Sisi atas)", "Bidang SRVW (Sisi belakang)", "Bidang yang memotong tengah akuarium dan sejajar dengan bidang QRVU", "Bidang TUVW (Sisi atas/tutup)", "Bidang diagonal PRVT"), 2, "Sekat harus tegak di alas, sejajar QRVU, dan tegak lurus PQUT. Itu dipenuhi bidang tegak di tengah akuarium yang sejajar QRVU.", passage = "Seorang desainer interior sedang merancang sebuah akuarium besar berbentuk balok PQRS.TUVW untuk lobi sebuah hotel. Di dalam akuarium tersebut, akan dipasang sebuah sekat kaca vertikal untuk memisahkan ikan predator dengan ikan kecil. Ketentuan pemasangan sekat kaca: - - - Sekat kaca harus dipasang tegak lurus terhadap sisi alas akuarium (PQRS). Sekat kaca tersebut harus dipasang sejajar dengan sisi samping kanan akuarium (QRVU). Sekat kaca harus tegak lurus dengan sisi depan akuarium (PQUT)."),
        Question("kp80", "Seorang arsitek merancang fasad gedung berbentuk trapesium sama kaki ABCD (CD = 6 m, AB = 12 m). Di dalamnya ada panel kaca EFGH berbentuk trapesium sama kaki yang sebangun dengan ABCD. Jarak tegak lurus CD ke AB adalah 8 m dan tinggi panel EFGH 4 m. Panjang sisi miring gedung (AD) dan luas panel kaca EFGH adalah…", listOf("10 m dan 9 m²", "√73 m dan 18 m²", "10 m dan 12 m²", "√73 m dan 9 m²", "10 m dan 13,5 m²"), 1, "Selisih alas (12 − 6)/2 = 3, jadi AD = √(8² + 3²) = √73 m. Tinggi EFGH 4 = ½ dari 8, jadi sisi sejajarnya 3 m dan 6 m. Luas = ½ × (3 + 6) × 4 = 18 m².", image = "soal/kp80_trapesium.jpg"),
        Question("kp81", "Titik P(2, −4) mengalami transformasi berurutan: (1) rotasi 180° dengan pusat (0, 0), (2) pencerminan terhadap garis y = x, (3) translasi oleh vektor (3, −2). Koordinat bayangan akhir P‴ adalah…", listOf("(4, −2)", "(1, 2)", "(−1, 6)", "(7, 4)", "(7, −4)"), 4, "Rotasi 180°: (−2, 4). Cermin y = x: (4, −2). Translasi (3, −2): (4 + 3, −2 − 2) = (7, −4). (Di berkas asli pilihannya berupa grafik; di sini ditulis sebagai koordinat.)"),
        Question("kp82", "Pak Andi ingin memasang lampu gantung di ruang tamu berukuran 6 m × 4 m × 3 m. Ia menarik kabel lurus dari salah satu pojok atas ruangan (titik A) ke pengait lampu (titik P) yang berada tepat di tengah langit-langit. Berapa panjang kabel minimal yang dibutuhkan?", listOf("250 cm", "√13 m", "√52 m", "500 cm", "13 m"), 1, "A dan P sama-sama di langit-langit. P di tengah, jadi AP = ½ × diagonal langit-langit = ½ × √(6² + 4²) = ½ × √52 = √13 m."),
        Question("kp84", "Putuskan apakah pernyataan (1) dan (2) cukup untuk menjawab pertanyaan tersebut.", listOf("Pernyataan (1) SAJA cukup untuk men jawab pertanyaan, tetapi pernyataan (2) SAJA tidak cukup.", "Pernyataan (2) SAJA cukup untuk men jawab pertanyaan, tetapi pernyataan (1) SAJA tidak cukup.", "Dua pernyataan BERSAMA-SAMA cukup untuk menjawab pertanyaan, tetapi satu pernyataan SAJA tidak cukup.", "Pernyataan (1) SAJA cukup DAN pernyataan (2) SAJA cukup.", "Pernyataan (1) dan pernyataan (2) tidak cukup untuk menjawab pertanyaan."), 3, "Luas 80 = ½(x + y) × 8 → x + y = 20. (1): x = 4, y = 16, kaki = √(8² + 6²) = 10, keliling 40 m → biaya Rp5.000.000 (tidak lebih), terjawab. (2): x = 2, y = 18, kaki = √(8² + 8²) ≈ 11,3, keliling ≈ 42,6 m → biaya ≈ Rp5,33 juta, terjawab. Masing-masing cukup.", passage = "Sebuah taman berbentuk trapesium sama kaki dengan tinggi 8 meter dan luas 80 m². Panjang sisi sejajarnya x dan y (meter), bilangan asli dengan x < y. Apakah biaya memasang pagar di sekeliling taman lebih dari Rp5.000.000,00 jika harga pagar Rp125.000,00 per meter?\n(1) Selisih panjang kedua sisi sejajar adalah 12 meter.\n(2) Perbandingan x dan y adalah 1 : 9."),
        Question("kp88", "Seorang kolektor punya 6 mobil antik berwarna berbeda (merah, hitam, kuning, hijau, biru, dan satu warna lain) yang akan diparkir sejajar. Aturannya: (1) mobil merah dan hitam di kedua ujung barisan, (2) mobil kuning dan hijau harus berdampingan, (3) mobil biru tidak boleh tepat di samping mobil kuning. Berapa banyak susunan yang mungkin?", listOf("4 cara", "8 cara", "12 cara", "16 cara", "24 cara"), 3, "Ujung: merah-hitam atau hitam-merah = 2 cara. Tengah (4 tempat): blok kuning-hijau (2 urutan) + biru + mobil lain = 3! × 2 = 12 susunan, dikurangi 4 susunan saat biru menempel di sisi kuning = 8. Total 2 × 8 = 16. (Kunci berkas asli menulis A, tetapi hitungan lengkap memberi 16.)"),
        Question("kp89", "Berapa peluang bahwa peserta yang terpilih adalah peserta yang mengikuti lomba Matematika?", listOf("45%", "55%", "62,5%", "65%", "70%"), 2, "Matematika: SMA 75, SMP 80 − 30 = 50. Total 125 dari 200 → 62,5%.", passage = "Di sebuah kompetisi sains tingkat kota, terdapat 200 peserta yang terbagi menjadi kelompok pelajar SMP dan SMA. Setiap peserta wajib mengikuti satu bidang lomba: Matematika atau Fisika. Berikut adalah rincian datanya: - - - Dari total peserta, terdapat 120 peserta SMA dan sisanya adalah peserta SMP. Pada kelompok peserta SMA, terdapat 75 orang yang mengikuti lomba Matematika. Pada kelompok peserta SMP, terdapat 30 orang yang mengikuti lomba Fisika. Panitia akan memilih satu orang pemenang doorprize secara acak dari seluruh peserta yang hadir."),
    )

    private fun resmiBigRaw() = listOf(
        Question("rb1", "Which option best summarizes the story?", listOf("Beginning: A lion was walking through the jungle. Problem: The mouse got lost and couldn't find food. Solution: The lion gave food to the mouse. Lesson: Always be generous to those in need.", "Beginning: A mouse accidentally disturbed a sleeping lion. Problem: The lion was caught in a hunter's net. Solution: The mouse chewed through the net and set the lion free. Lesson: Even the smallest creature can be a great help.", "Beginning: The lion and mouse were best friends. Problem: The lion got hurt in a fight. Solution: The mouse helped him find water. Lesson: Friendship is built on adventure.", "Beginning: A mouse was building a home near a tree. Problem: A storm destroyed the tree and trapped the lion. Solution: The mouse called for help from the jungle. Lesson: Teamwork solves big problems.", "Beginning: A lion was hungry and searching for food. Problem: He couldn't catch any prey. Solution: The mouse helped him find food. Lesson: Hunger teaches humility."), 1, "Hanya pilihan B yang cocok dengan alur: tikus mengganggu singa tidur → singa terjerat jaring → tikus menggigit jaring → pesan: makhluk kecil pun bisa sangat membantu.", passage = "The Lion and the Mouse\n\nOnce upon a time, in a thick jungle in Africa, there lived a strong and fierce lion. Every afternoon, the lion would rest under the cool shade of a big tree after walking through the forest.\nOne day, while he was sleeping, a playful little mouse passed by. The mouse saw the lion's thick mane and was curious. He climbed up and began to jump around on the lion's head, playing in his mane.\nThe lion woke up suddenly and was not happy at all. He quickly caught the mouse in his big paw and roared, \"Who dares to wake me up?\" He was very angry and almost killed the mouse.\nScared and shaking, the mouse begged the lion, \"Please don't kill me! I didn't mean to bother you. If you let me go, I promise I'll help you one day.\"\nThe lion laughed loudly. \"You? Help me? That's funny.\" But the lion was feeling kind, so he let the mouse go free.\nA few days later, the lion was walking through the jungle again when he fell into a trap. A net set by hunters caught him, and he couldn't escape. He tried to bite and tear the ropes, but they were too strong. The lion roared loudly, hoping someone would come.\nThe mouse heard the roar and ran to help. He saw the lion trapped and quickly started to chew the ropes with his sharp teeth. After some time, the net broke, and the lion was free.\nThe lion looked at the mouse with surprise and said, \"Thank you! You really saved my life.\"\nThe mouse smiled and said, \"I told you I would help you one day.\"\nFrom that moment on, the lion and the mouse became close friends. The lion learned that even small creatures can do great things, and we all need help sometimes.\n(Source: vedanta.com/stories/the-lion-and-the-mouse)"),
        Question("rb2", "Which of the following statements best conveys the message of the story? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("We should never wake up a sleeping animal", "Even the small and weak can help the strong", "It's always good to ask for help when we need it", "Lions are dangerous animals and should be avoided", "Never trust anyone who plays with your hair"), 1, "Kalimat penutup cerita: even small creatures can do great things (B), and we all need help sometimes (C).", passage = "The Lion and the Mouse\n\nOnce upon a time, in a thick jungle in Africa, there lived a strong and fierce lion. Every afternoon, the lion would rest under the cool shade of a big tree after walking through the forest.\nOne day, while he was sleeping, a playful little mouse passed by. The mouse saw the lion's thick mane and was curious. He climbed up and began to jump around on the lion's head, playing in his mane.\nThe lion woke up suddenly and was not happy at all. He quickly caught the mouse in his big paw and roared, \"Who dares to wake me up?\" He was very angry and almost killed the mouse.\nScared and shaking, the mouse begged the lion, \"Please don't kill me! I didn't mean to bother you. If you let me go, I promise I'll help you one day.\"\nThe lion laughed loudly. \"You? Help me? That's funny.\" But the lion was feeling kind, so he let the mouse go free.\nA few days later, the lion was walking through the jungle again when he fell into a trap. A net set by hunters caught him, and he couldn't escape. He tried to bite and tear the ropes, but they were too strong. The lion roared loudly, hoping someone would come.\nThe mouse heard the roar and ran to help. He saw the lion trapped and quickly started to chew the ropes with his sharp teeth. After some time, the net broke, and the lion was free.\nThe lion looked at the mouse with surprise and said, \"Thank you! You really saved my life.\"\nThe mouse smiled and said, \"I told you I would help you one day.\"\nFrom that moment on, the lion and the mouse became close friends. The lion learned that even small creatures can do great things, and we all need help sometimes.\n(Source: vedanta.com/stories/the-lion-and-the-mouse)", multi = setOf(1, 2)),
        Question("rb3", "Why did the lion trust the mouse and decide to let him go instead of eating him?", listOf("The lion was too tired to eat the mouse", "The mouse told the lion he might help him one day", "The lion was felling happy to see the mouse", "The lion heard someone coming and got scared", "The mouse promised to bring food for the lion"), 1, "Tikus memohon dan berjanji akan menolong singa suatu hari; singa yang sedang baik hati pun melepaskannya.", passage = "The Lion and the Mouse\n\nOnce upon a time, in a thick jungle in Africa, there lived a strong and fierce lion. Every afternoon, the lion would rest under the cool shade of a big tree after walking through the forest.\nOne day, while he was sleeping, a playful little mouse passed by. The mouse saw the lion's thick mane and was curious. He climbed up and began to jump around on the lion's head, playing in his mane.\nThe lion woke up suddenly and was not happy at all. He quickly caught the mouse in his big paw and roared, \"Who dares to wake me up?\" He was very angry and almost killed the mouse.\nScared and shaking, the mouse begged the lion, \"Please don't kill me! I didn't mean to bother you. If you let me go, I promise I'll help you one day.\"\nThe lion laughed loudly. \"You? Help me? That's funny.\" But the lion was feeling kind, so he let the mouse go free.\nA few days later, the lion was walking through the jungle again when he fell into a trap. A net set by hunters caught him, and he couldn't escape. He tried to bite and tear the ropes, but they were too strong. The lion roared loudly, hoping someone would come.\nThe mouse heard the roar and ran to help. He saw the lion trapped and quickly started to chew the ropes with his sharp teeth. After some time, the net broke, and the lion was free.\nThe lion looked at the mouse with surprise and said, \"Thank you! You really saved my life.\"\nThe mouse smiled and said, \"I told you I would help you one day.\"\nFrom that moment on, the lion and the mouse became close friends. The lion learned that even small creatures can do great things, and we all need help sometimes.\n(Source: vedanta.com/stories/the-lion-and-the-mouse)"),
        Question("rb4", "As you read the part where the lion let the mouse go, which of the following endings do you anticipate? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("The mouse forgets about the lion and never helps him", "The lion gets into trouble and no one helps him", "The lion becomes angry at all small animals", "The mouse spreads the lion's kindness to other animals", "The mouse becomes the lion's loyal assistant"), 4, "Setelah dilepaskan, tikus berjanji membalas budi. Akhir yang masuk akal adalah tikus membalas kebaikan itu: menjadi penolong setia singa dan menyebarkan kebaikannya. Akhir negatif bertentangan dengan janji tikus.", passage = "The Lion and the Mouse\n\nOnce upon a time, in a thick jungle in Africa, there lived a strong and fierce lion. Every afternoon, the lion would rest under the cool shade of a big tree after walking through the forest.\nOne day, while he was sleeping, a playful little mouse passed by. The mouse saw the lion's thick mane and was curious. He climbed up and began to jump around on the lion's head, playing in his mane.\nThe lion woke up suddenly and was not happy at all. He quickly caught the mouse in his big paw and roared, \"Who dares to wake me up?\" He was very angry and almost killed the mouse.\nScared and shaking, the mouse begged the lion, \"Please don't kill me! I didn't mean to bother you. If you let me go, I promise I'll help you one day.\"\nThe lion laughed loudly. \"You? Help me? That's funny.\" But the lion was feeling kind, so he let the mouse go free.\nA few days later, the lion was walking through the jungle again when he fell into a trap. A net set by hunters caught him, and he couldn't escape. He tried to bite and tear the ropes, but they were too strong. The lion roared loudly, hoping someone would come.\nThe mouse heard the roar and ran to help. He saw the lion trapped and quickly started to chew the ropes with his sharp teeth. After some time, the net broke, and the lion was free.\nThe lion looked at the mouse with surprise and said, \"Thank you! You really saved my life.\"\nThe mouse smiled and said, \"I told you I would help you one day.\"\nFrom that moment on, the lion and the mouse became close friends. The lion learned that even small creatures can do great things, and we all need help sometimes.\n(Source: vedanta.com/stories/the-lion-and-the-mouse)", multi = setOf(3, 4)),
        Question("rb5", "Which of the following sentences from the story help you understand the lion's character? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("\"The lion always took his afternoon nap under the shade of a big tree in the bushes.\"", "\"He caught the mouse and questioned him for interrupting his nap.\"", "\"The lion was amused at the mouse's words and decided to spare his life.\"", "\"With his sharp teeth, the mouse nibbled through the net.\"", "\"The lion thanked the mouse immensely for his help.\""), 1, "Watak singa terlihat dari tindakannya: galak saat diganggu (B), murah hati saat melepaskan tikus (C), dan tahu berterima kasih (E). Pilihan A hanya kebiasaan, D tentang tikus.", passage = "The Lion and the Mouse\n\nOnce upon a time, in a thick jungle in Africa, there lived a strong and fierce lion. Every afternoon, the lion would rest under the cool shade of a big tree after walking through the forest.\nOne day, while he was sleeping, a playful little mouse passed by. The mouse saw the lion's thick mane and was curious. He climbed up and began to jump around on the lion's head, playing in his mane.\nThe lion woke up suddenly and was not happy at all. He quickly caught the mouse in his big paw and roared, \"Who dares to wake me up?\" He was very angry and almost killed the mouse.\nScared and shaking, the mouse begged the lion, \"Please don't kill me! I didn't mean to bother you. If you let me go, I promise I'll help you one day.\"\nThe lion laughed loudly. \"You? Help me? That's funny.\" But the lion was feeling kind, so he let the mouse go free.\nA few days later, the lion was walking through the jungle again when he fell into a trap. A net set by hunters caught him, and he couldn't escape. He tried to bite and tear the ropes, but they were too strong. The lion roared loudly, hoping someone would come.\nThe mouse heard the roar and ran to help. He saw the lion trapped and quickly started to chew the ropes with his sharp teeth. After some time, the net broke, and the lion was free.\nThe lion looked at the mouse with surprise and said, \"Thank you! You really saved my life.\"\nThe mouse smiled and said, \"I told you I would help you one day.\"\nFrom that moment on, the lion and the mouse became close friends. The lion learned that even small creatures can do great things, and we all need help sometimes.\n(Source: vedanta.com/stories/the-lion-and-the-mouse)", multi = setOf(1, 2, 4)),
        Question("rb6", "Based on the information given, we can keep our mind focused and fresh by ....", listOf("knowing your learning style", "using Pomodoro Technique", "using online quizzes apps", "by reviewing materials", "by creating mind maps"), 1, "Poin 4: Pomodoro (25 menit belajar, 5 menit istirahat) \"keeps your mind fresh and focused\".", passage = "Effective Study Techniques (infographic)\n\n1. Know Your Learning Style: understand whether you learn best by reading, listening, or watching.\n2. Set a Consistent Study Schedule: study at the same time every day. Regularity helps build strong habits.\n3. Create a Comfortable Study Space: find a quiet, well-lit, and distraction-free area. Have all your materials ready.\n4. Use the Pomodoro Technique: study for 25 minutes, then take a 5-minute break. This keeps your mind fresh and focused.\n5. Take Effective Notes: write key points using methods like mind maps or tables to help remember important information.\n6. Practice and Repeat: regularly review your material and do practice questions to deepen understanding and improve retention.\n7. Join a Study Group: discuss topics with friends to gain new insights and solve problems together.\n8. Leverage Technology: use apps and websites for flashcards, video lessons, and online quizzes to support your study routine.\n9. Get Enough Sleep: aim for 7–8 hours.\n10. Be Patient and Persistent: learning takes time.", image = "soal/study_techniques.jpg"),
        Question("rb7", "Based on the infographic, determine whether each study technique is categorized as Time Management or Self Management.", listOf("Time Management", "Self Management"), 0, "Pomodoro dan jadwal tetap mengatur waktu belajar (Time Management). Sabar dan gigih adalah sikap diri (Self Management).", passage = "Effective Study Techniques (infographic)\n\n1. Know Your Learning Style: understand whether you learn best by reading, listening, or watching.\n2. Set a Consistent Study Schedule: study at the same time every day. Regularity helps build strong habits.\n3. Create a Comfortable Study Space: find a quiet, well-lit, and distraction-free area. Have all your materials ready.\n4. Use the Pomodoro Technique: study for 25 minutes, then take a 5-minute break. This keeps your mind fresh and focused.\n5. Take Effective Notes: write key points using methods like mind maps or tables to help remember important information.\n6. Practice and Repeat: regularly review your material and do practice questions to deepen understanding and improve retention.\n7. Join a Study Group: discuss topics with friends to gain new insights and solve problems together.\n8. Leverage Technology: use apps and websites for flashcards, video lessons, and online quizzes to support your study routine.\n9. Get Enough Sleep: aim for 7–8 hours.\n10. Be Patient and Persistent: learning takes time.", image = "soal/study_techniques.jpg", rows = listOf("Be patient and persistent", "Use the Pomodoro technique", "Set a consistent study schedule"), rowKeys = listOf(1, 0, 0)),
        Question("rb8", "From the options provided, choose the sequence that best reflects the information in the infographic \"Effective Study Techniques\".", listOf("Set your goal → Watch lessons videos → Sleep well → Have group chat with friends → Eat nutritious meal", "Plan study time → Join a study group → Take long breaks → Write a to do list → Write important points", "Know your learning style → Find a quiet area → Set a timetable → Use less gadgets → Be patient and persistent", "Know your study style → Plan your study time → Practice and repeat → Take a break → Watch lessons videos", "Take notes → Join a study groups → Use different medias → Play music you like → Have good meal while studying"), 3, "Semua langkah di pilihan D ada di infografik (poin 1, 2, 6, 4, 8). Pilihan C memuat \"use less gadgets\" yang bertentangan dengan poin 8 (leverage technology); pilihan lain memuat hal yang tidak disebut.", passage = "Effective Study Techniques (infographic)\n\n1. Know Your Learning Style: understand whether you learn best by reading, listening, or watching.\n2. Set a Consistent Study Schedule: study at the same time every day. Regularity helps build strong habits.\n3. Create a Comfortable Study Space: find a quiet, well-lit, and distraction-free area. Have all your materials ready.\n4. Use the Pomodoro Technique: study for 25 minutes, then take a 5-minute break. This keeps your mind fresh and focused.\n5. Take Effective Notes: write key points using methods like mind maps or tables to help remember important information.\n6. Practice and Repeat: regularly review your material and do practice questions to deepen understanding and improve retention.\n7. Join a Study Group: discuss topics with friends to gain new insights and solve problems together.\n8. Leverage Technology: use apps and websites for flashcards, video lessons, and online quizzes to support your study routine.\n9. Get Enough Sleep: aim for 7–8 hours.\n10. Be Patient and Persistent: learning takes time.", image = "soal/study_techniques.jpg"),
        Question("rb9", "Which of the following statements best reflect the author's purpose in writing the text? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("To help students find fun strategies to play after studying", "To offer students guidance on how to learn more efficiently", "To encourage students to use simple habits to improve their learning", "To explain why studying tips is difficult for most students", "To show students that they can manage their time and focus better"), 1, "Infografik berisi tips belajar: membimbing belajar efisien (B), mendorong kebiasaan sederhana (C), dan menunjukkan cara mengatur waktu dan fokus (E).", passage = "Effective Study Techniques (infographic)\n\n1. Know Your Learning Style: understand whether you learn best by reading, listening, or watching.\n2. Set a Consistent Study Schedule: study at the same time every day. Regularity helps build strong habits.\n3. Create a Comfortable Study Space: find a quiet, well-lit, and distraction-free area. Have all your materials ready.\n4. Use the Pomodoro Technique: study for 25 minutes, then take a 5-minute break. This keeps your mind fresh and focused.\n5. Take Effective Notes: write key points using methods like mind maps or tables to help remember important information.\n6. Practice and Repeat: regularly review your material and do practice questions to deepen understanding and improve retention.\n7. Join a Study Group: discuss topics with friends to gain new insights and solve problems together.\n8. Leverage Technology: use apps and websites for flashcards, video lessons, and online quizzes to support your study routine.\n9. Get Enough Sleep: aim for 7–8 hours.\n10. Be Patient and Persistent: learning takes time.", image = "soal/study_techniques.jpg", multi = setOf(1, 2, 4)),
        Question("rb10", "If you are preparing for an important exam and want to improve your study routine, which of the following techniques do you think can be implemented effectively in your personal study time? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("Only study when you are in a group discussion with others", "Use technology during all study sessions in or outside class", "Use the Pomodoro Technique to structure your study and break time", "Practice and repeat study material regularly to retain information", "Create a quiet and comfortable study space to improve focus"), 2, "C, D, E sesuai infografik dan bisa dilakukan sendiri. A (hanya belajar kelompok) dan B (teknologi di semua sesi) berlebihan dan tidak disarankan teks.", passage = "Effective Study Techniques (infographic)\n\n1. Know Your Learning Style: understand whether you learn best by reading, listening, or watching.\n2. Set a Consistent Study Schedule: study at the same time every day. Regularity helps build strong habits.\n3. Create a Comfortable Study Space: find a quiet, well-lit, and distraction-free area. Have all your materials ready.\n4. Use the Pomodoro Technique: study for 25 minutes, then take a 5-minute break. This keeps your mind fresh and focused.\n5. Take Effective Notes: write key points using methods like mind maps or tables to help remember important information.\n6. Practice and Repeat: regularly review your material and do practice questions to deepen understanding and improve retention.\n7. Join a Study Group: discuss topics with friends to gain new insights and solve problems together.\n8. Leverage Technology: use apps and websites for flashcards, video lessons, and online quizzes to support your study routine.\n9. Get Enough Sleep: aim for 7–8 hours.\n10. Be Patient and Persistent: learning takes time.", image = "soal/study_techniques.jpg", multi = setOf(2, 3, 4)),
        Question("rb11", "Which statement provides the most accurate chronological summary of the story's main events?", listOf("Shero falls into the dirt. The hyenas cause trouble at the river. Hera tells Shero that he is funny. Shero copies Hera's roar. Shero becomes the kingdom's funny helper.", "Hera is a strong lion king. Shero likes to pretend to be strong. The hyenas cause trouble near the river. Hera scares the hyenas, but Shero makes them laugh. Shero learns that making others happy is special.", "Hera and Shero are both strong leaders. The hyenas come to help the lions. Shero tells funny stories to the hyenas. Hera is angry with Shero. The lions and hyenas become friends.", "Shero is a strong lion king. Hera is jealous of Shero. The hyenas attack the lions. Shero defeats the hyenas. Shero becomes the new king.", "Shero wants to be king and fights Hera. The hyenas help Shero. Hera leaves the kingdom. Shero becomes king. Hera returns to forgive Shero."), 1, "Pilihan B mengikuti urutan cerita dari awal sampai akhir. Pilihan A urutannya acak; C, D, E tidak sesuai isi cerita.", passage = "The False Lion King\n\nOnce upon a time, in Africa, there lived two lion kings. One was named Hera and the other was Shero. Hera was very strong and handsome. All the animals loved and respected him. He was a great leader. Shero was not like Hera. He had a small mane and a funny, squeaky voice. Shero liked to pretend he was as powerful as Hera. He often copied Hera's roar, but it made the other animals laugh.\nOne day, the animals heard that some hyenas were causing trouble near the river. Hera quickly gathered his followers to stop the hyenas. Shero also wanted to come. He wanted to show everyone that he was strong too.\nWhen they reached the river, Hera roared loudly. His roar was so powerful that the hyenas got scared. Shero also tried to roar, but his voice was high and silly. The hyenas laughed at him. Their leader, Hank the Hyena, made jokes about Shero.\nHera stayed calm and smiled. Shero did not give up. He said, \"I am just as strong as Hera!\" The hyenas laughed even louder. Shero tried to show his power by jumping on a small dirt hill. But he tripped and fell into the ground. The hyenas laughed so much they cried. Even Hera laughed a little.\nAt the end of the day, the hyenas left, still laughing about Shero. Hera told Shero, \"You are not like me, but you make everyone happy with your jokes.\" Shero smiled and understood that he had his own special gift.\nFrom that day, Shero became the kingdom's jester. He and Hera ruled together — one with strength, and one with laughter. The animals learned that both power and fun are important in life.\n(Adapted from wikibedtimestories.com)", image = "soal/false_lion_king.jpg"),
        Question("rb12", "What can we learn from the story of Hera and Shero? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("Everyone has something special to give, even if they are not the leader", "Being funny and making others smile is just as important as being strong", "Good friends will support you and help you see your real strengths", "Working together is better when people use their different talents", "Trying your best to help others is more important than always being perfect"), 0, "Shero punya bakat sendiri (A); \"both power and fun are important\" (B); Hera dan Shero memerintah bersama dengan bakat berbeda (D).", passage = "The False Lion King\n\nOnce upon a time, in Africa, there lived two lion kings. One was named Hera and the other was Shero. Hera was very strong and handsome. All the animals loved and respected him. He was a great leader. Shero was not like Hera. He had a small mane and a funny, squeaky voice. Shero liked to pretend he was as powerful as Hera. He often copied Hera's roar, but it made the other animals laugh.\nOne day, the animals heard that some hyenas were causing trouble near the river. Hera quickly gathered his followers to stop the hyenas. Shero also wanted to come. He wanted to show everyone that he was strong too.\nWhen they reached the river, Hera roared loudly. His roar was so powerful that the hyenas got scared. Shero also tried to roar, but his voice was high and silly. The hyenas laughed at him. Their leader, Hank the Hyena, made jokes about Shero.\nHera stayed calm and smiled. Shero did not give up. He said, \"I am just as strong as Hera!\" The hyenas laughed even louder. Shero tried to show his power by jumping on a small dirt hill. But he tripped and fell into the ground. The hyenas laughed so much they cried. Even Hera laughed a little.\nAt the end of the day, the hyenas left, still laughing about Shero. Hera told Shero, \"You are not like me, but you make everyone happy with your jokes.\" Shero smiled and understood that he had his own special gift.\nFrom that day, Shero became the kingdom's jester. He and Hera ruled together — one with strength, and one with laughter. The animals learned that both power and fun are important in life.\n(Adapted from wikibedtimestories.com)", image = "soal/false_lion_king.jpg", multi = setOf(0, 1, 3)),
        Question("rb13", "The hyenas laugh so much when Shero tries to roar like Hera because ....", listOf("Shero tries to roar in a serious way and surprises the hyenas", "Shero's roar is funny, which the hyenas think he is joking", "Hera tells a joke about Shero to make the hyenas laugh", "Shero is acting like Hera, and it's absolutely brilliant", "Shero trips and falls when trying to show his strength"), 1, "Teks: \"Shero also tried to roar, but his voice was high and silly. The hyenas laughed at him.\" Jatuh tersandung terjadi pada bagian lain.", passage = "The False Lion King\n\nOnce upon a time, in Africa, there lived two lion kings. One was named Hera and the other was Shero. Hera was very strong and handsome. All the animals loved and respected him. He was a great leader. Shero was not like Hera. He had a small mane and a funny, squeaky voice. Shero liked to pretend he was as powerful as Hera. He often copied Hera's roar, but it made the other animals laugh.\nOne day, the animals heard that some hyenas were causing trouble near the river. Hera quickly gathered his followers to stop the hyenas. Shero also wanted to come. He wanted to show everyone that he was strong too.\nWhen they reached the river, Hera roared loudly. His roar was so powerful that the hyenas got scared. Shero also tried to roar, but his voice was high and silly. The hyenas laughed at him. Their leader, Hank the Hyena, made jokes about Shero.\nHera stayed calm and smiled. Shero did not give up. He said, \"I am just as strong as Hera!\" The hyenas laughed even louder. Shero tried to show his power by jumping on a small dirt hill. But he tripped and fell into the ground. The hyenas laughed so much they cried. Even Hera laughed a little.\nAt the end of the day, the hyenas left, still laughing about Shero. Hera told Shero, \"You are not like me, but you make everyone happy with your jokes.\" Shero smiled and understood that he had his own special gift.\nFrom that day, Shero became the kingdom's jester. He and Hera ruled together — one with strength, and one with laughter. The animals learned that both power and fun are important in life.\n(Adapted from wikibedtimestories.com)", image = "soal/false_lion_king.jpg"),
        Question("rb14", "If in the beginning of the story, Shero is a strong lion with a loud roar, just like Hera, what would happen at the end of the story? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("Shero and Hera would both scare the hyenas away together", "Shero would become the king, and Hera would leave the savannah", "Shero would get respect from the other animals for his strength", "The hyenas would still laugh at Shero because he is funny", "Shero would try to take Hera's place as the only lion king"), 0, "Kalau Shero sekuat Hera, aumannya juga menakutkan sehingga mereka mengusir hyena bersama (A) dan Shero dihormati karena kekuatannya (C), seperti Hera di awal cerita.", passage = "The False Lion King\n\nOnce upon a time, in Africa, there lived two lion kings. One was named Hera and the other was Shero. Hera was very strong and handsome. All the animals loved and respected him. He was a great leader. Shero was not like Hera. He had a small mane and a funny, squeaky voice. Shero liked to pretend he was as powerful as Hera. He often copied Hera's roar, but it made the other animals laugh.\nOne day, the animals heard that some hyenas were causing trouble near the river. Hera quickly gathered his followers to stop the hyenas. Shero also wanted to come. He wanted to show everyone that he was strong too.\nWhen they reached the river, Hera roared loudly. His roar was so powerful that the hyenas got scared. Shero also tried to roar, but his voice was high and silly. The hyenas laughed at him. Their leader, Hank the Hyena, made jokes about Shero.\nHera stayed calm and smiled. Shero did not give up. He said, \"I am just as strong as Hera!\" The hyenas laughed even louder. Shero tried to show his power by jumping on a small dirt hill. But he tripped and fell into the ground. The hyenas laughed so much they cried. Even Hera laughed a little.\nAt the end of the day, the hyenas left, still laughing about Shero. Hera told Shero, \"You are not like me, but you make everyone happy with your jokes.\" Shero smiled and understood that he had his own special gift.\nFrom that day, Shero became the kingdom's jester. He and Hera ruled together — one with strength, and one with laughter. The animals learned that both power and fun are important in life.\n(Adapted from wikibedtimestories.com)", image = "soal/false_lion_king.jpg", multi = setOf(0, 2)),
        Question("rb15", "Shero is clumsy and funny. This is shown when he .... (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("scares the hyenas away with his loud and powerful roar", "makes the other animals smile by pretending to be a great king", "tries to roar like Hera, but his voice is small and makes the hyenas laugh", "walks with Hera to confront the hyenas, acting as if he is an important king too", "tells the hyenas that he is as mighty as King Hera, even though no one believes him"), 2, "Paragraf 1: meniru auman Hera membuat hewan lain tertawa (B). Paragraf 3: suaranya melengking dan hyena tertawa (C). Paragraf 4: mengaku sekuat Hera, hyena makin tertawa (E).", passage = "The False Lion King\n\nOnce upon a time, in Africa, there lived two lion kings. One was named Hera and the other was Shero. Hera was very strong and handsome. All the animals loved and respected him. He was a great leader. Shero was not like Hera. He had a small mane and a funny, squeaky voice. Shero liked to pretend he was as powerful as Hera. He often copied Hera's roar, but it made the other animals laugh.\nOne day, the animals heard that some hyenas were causing trouble near the river. Hera quickly gathered his followers to stop the hyenas. Shero also wanted to come. He wanted to show everyone that he was strong too.\nWhen they reached the river, Hera roared loudly. His roar was so powerful that the hyenas got scared. Shero also tried to roar, but his voice was high and silly. The hyenas laughed at him. Their leader, Hank the Hyena, made jokes about Shero.\nHera stayed calm and smiled. Shero did not give up. He said, \"I am just as strong as Hera!\" The hyenas laughed even louder. Shero tried to show his power by jumping on a small dirt hill. But he tripped and fell into the ground. The hyenas laughed so much they cried. Even Hera laughed a little.\nAt the end of the day, the hyenas left, still laughing about Shero. Hera told Shero, \"You are not like me, but you make everyone happy with your jokes.\" Shero smiled and understood that he had his own special gift.\nFrom that day, Shero became the kingdom's jester. He and Hera ruled together — one with strength, and one with laughter. The animals learned that both power and fun are important in life.\n(Adapted from wikibedtimestories.com)", image = "soal/false_lion_king.jpg", multi = setOf(1, 2, 4)),
        Question("rb16", "Which of the following descriptions are mentioned clearly in the text? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("The reef was built by local communities over hundreds of years", "The reef is located in the Pacific Ocean near Australia", "The reef can help protect the coast from big waves", "The reef is home to sea turtles and dolphins", "The reef has more than 10,000 coral islands"), 1, "B (paragraf 1), C (paragraf 4), dan D (paragraf 2) tertulis jelas. A dan E tidak disebut.", passage = "The Great Barrier Reef\n\nThe Great Barrier Reef is one of the most beautiful places in the world. It is located in the Pacific Ocean, near the northeast coast of Australia. The reef is very big. It stretches over 2,000 kilometers and can even be seen from space. There are many small coral islands and clear, warm waters around the reef.\nThis reef is full of life. There are many kinds of colorful fish, sea turtles, dolphins, and even sharks. Coral of different shapes and colors grows under the water. Sea birds fly over the reef and nest on small islands. People can see this beauty by swimming, diving, or joining a boat tour.\nThe colors under the water are amazing. Coral comes in red, yellow, green, and blue. Some coral looks like trees, and some looks like big round stones. Small fish swim in and out of the coral like they are playing a game. In some places, soft coral moves with the water like grass in the wind. When the sun shines, the reef looks bright and full of light. It feels like a different world under the sea.\nThe reef is not only beautiful, but also very important. It helps protect the coast from big waves and storms. It is a home for sea animals and a place where plants can grow. Many people also get food and jobs from the sea near the reef. Without the reef, the ocean would not be the same.\n(Adapted from britannica.com/place/Great-Barrier-Reef)", multi = setOf(1, 2, 3)),
        Question("rb17", "The author mentioned \"It feels like a different world under the sea\". What does the phrase \"a different world under the sea\" most likely mean?", listOf("A safe place that has bright reef", "A peaceful place where people can live under water", "A colorful place that looks the same as the land", "A shining reef that is quiet", "A calm place that looks beautiful and unique"), 4, "Paragraf itu menggambarkan warna-warni karang dan ikan yang tenang dan indah, jadi \"dunia lain\" berarti tempat yang indah dan unik, berbeda dari daratan.", passage = "The Great Barrier Reef\n\nThe Great Barrier Reef is one of the most beautiful places in the world. It is located in the Pacific Ocean, near the northeast coast of Australia. The reef is very big. It stretches over 2,000 kilometers and can even be seen from space. There are many small coral islands and clear, warm waters around the reef.\nThis reef is full of life. There are many kinds of colorful fish, sea turtles, dolphins, and even sharks. Coral of different shapes and colors grows under the water. Sea birds fly over the reef and nest on small islands. People can see this beauty by swimming, diving, or joining a boat tour.\nThe colors under the water are amazing. Coral comes in red, yellow, green, and blue. Some coral looks like trees, and some looks like big round stones. Small fish swim in and out of the coral like they are playing a game. In some places, soft coral moves with the water like grass in the wind. When the sun shines, the reef looks bright and full of light. It feels like a different world under the sea.\nThe reef is not only beautiful, but also very important. It helps protect the coast from big waves and storms. It is a home for sea animals and a place where plants can grow. Many people also get food and jobs from the sea near the reef. Without the reef, the ocean would not be the same.\n(Adapted from britannica.com/place/Great-Barrier-Reef)"),
        Question("rb18", "Which of the following best represents the main idea implied by the text?", listOf("The reef is useful for fishing and shipping", "The reef is large, but not important to people", "The reef is a natural treasure that must be cared for", "The reef is only for scientists and researchers to explore", "The reef is a protected area that should be closed to visitors"), 2, "Teks menekankan karang itu indah sekaligus penting bagi alam dan manusia, sehingga harus dijaga.", passage = "The Great Barrier Reef\n\nThe Great Barrier Reef is one of the most beautiful places in the world. It is located in the Pacific Ocean, near the northeast coast of Australia. The reef is very big. It stretches over 2,000 kilometers and can even be seen from space. There are many small coral islands and clear, warm waters around the reef.\nThis reef is full of life. There are many kinds of colorful fish, sea turtles, dolphins, and even sharks. Coral of different shapes and colors grows under the water. Sea birds fly over the reef and nest on small islands. People can see this beauty by swimming, diving, or joining a boat tour.\nThe colors under the water are amazing. Coral comes in red, yellow, green, and blue. Some coral looks like trees, and some looks like big round stones. Small fish swim in and out of the coral like they are playing a game. In some places, soft coral moves with the water like grass in the wind. When the sun shines, the reef looks bright and full of light. It feels like a different world under the sea.\nThe reef is not only beautiful, but also very important. It helps protect the coast from big waves and storms. It is a home for sea animals and a place where plants can grow. Many people also get food and jobs from the sea near the reef. Without the reef, the ocean would not be the same.\n(Adapted from britannica.com/place/Great-Barrier-Reef)"),
        Question("rb19", "Which detail would best encourage people to visit the Great Barrier Reef?", listOf("Visitors can see an Australian national park", "Visitors can stay in hotels around the reef", "Visitors can get there by boat or short flights", "Visitors can protect the coral and the animals", "Visitors can see the coral by diving or swimming"), 4, "Teks menyebut keindahan karang bisa dinikmati dengan berenang, menyelam, atau tur perahu; detail ini paling menarik minat pengunjung.", passage = "The Great Barrier Reef\n\nThe Great Barrier Reef is one of the most beautiful places in the world. It is located in the Pacific Ocean, near the northeast coast of Australia. The reef is very big. It stretches over 2,000 kilometers and can even be seen from space. There are many small coral islands and clear, warm waters around the reef.\nThis reef is full of life. There are many kinds of colorful fish, sea turtles, dolphins, and even sharks. Coral of different shapes and colors grows under the water. Sea birds fly over the reef and nest on small islands. People can see this beauty by swimming, diving, or joining a boat tour.\nThe colors under the water are amazing. Coral comes in red, yellow, green, and blue. Some coral looks like trees, and some looks like big round stones. Small fish swim in and out of the coral like they are playing a game. In some places, soft coral moves with the water like grass in the wind. When the sun shines, the reef looks bright and full of light. It feels like a different world under the sea.\nThe reef is not only beautiful, but also very important. It helps protect the coast from big waves and storms. It is a home for sea animals and a place where plants can grow. Many people also get food and jobs from the sea near the reef. Without the reef, the ocean would not be the same.\n(Adapted from britannica.com/place/Great-Barrier-Reef)"),
        Question("rb20", "Which parts of the text best support the idea that the Great Barrier Reef is both beautiful and important? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("The reef helps protect the coast from big waves", "It is home to sea turtles, dolphins, and colorful fish", "The coral reefs grow best in cold, deep water", "Some areas of the reef are damaged by starfish and warm water", "The reef was discovered by sailors in the 1800s"), 0, "A menunjukkan pentingnya karang; B menunjukkan keindahan dan kekayaan hidupnya. C, D, E tidak ada di teks.", passage = "The Great Barrier Reef\n\nThe Great Barrier Reef is one of the most beautiful places in the world. It is located in the Pacific Ocean, near the northeast coast of Australia. The reef is very big. It stretches over 2,000 kilometers and can even be seen from space. There are many small coral islands and clear, warm waters around the reef.\nThis reef is full of life. There are many kinds of colorful fish, sea turtles, dolphins, and even sharks. Coral of different shapes and colors grows under the water. Sea birds fly over the reef and nest on small islands. People can see this beauty by swimming, diving, or joining a boat tour.\nThe colors under the water are amazing. Coral comes in red, yellow, green, and blue. Some coral looks like trees, and some looks like big round stones. Small fish swim in and out of the coral like they are playing a game. In some places, soft coral moves with the water like grass in the wind. When the sun shines, the reef looks bright and full of light. It feels like a different world under the sea.\nThe reef is not only beautiful, but also very important. It helps protect the coast from big waves and storms. It is a home for sea animals and a place where plants can grow. Many people also get food and jobs from the sea near the reef. Without the reef, the ocean would not be the same.\n(Adapted from britannica.com/place/Great-Barrier-Reef)", multi = setOf(0, 1)),
        Question("rb21", "Based on the text, choose the activity that best fits each description.", listOf("Short-term financial goal", "Long-term financial goal"), 0, "Paragraf 2: getting a new phone = short-term; saving for college dan starting a business = long-term.", passage = "Why Teenagers Should Learn to Manage Their Money\n\nMany young people today often spend money on things they like, such as snacks, clothes, or fun activities. But learning to handle money from a young age is very important. Good money habits can help students make a better future.\nHaving a clear plan for the future can show teenagers how to use their money. Students should think about short-term goals, like getting a new phone, and long-term goals, like saving for college or starting a business. Writing these goals down can help students stay motivated and focused.\nA budget helps students see where their money goes every month. It's important to list basic needs like food and travel, and also other costs like clothes or presents. A budget makes it easier to decide how much money to save, spend, or keep for unexpected problems.\nSometimes, students don't know how much they spend on small things. Keeping track of spending with notes or apps can help students understand their habits. This helps them stay within their budget and make changes if needed.\nTeenagers should also learn the difference between saving money and investing money. Saving is safer but slower, while investing has more risk but can earn more money. Knowing both can help students choose the best way for their money goals.\nTo sum up, students who learn to plan, budget, track, and understand saving choices are more ready for the future. That is why learning about money should start early and be done often.\n\nTable 1. How do students manage their money?\n• Students who save regularly — 45% — save at least 10% of allowance\n• Students who track expenses — 35% — use apps or notes\n• Students with financial education — 25% — have learned budgeting in class\n• Students who often borrow from friends — 30% — due to running out of money\n• Students who spend most on food & drinks — 50% — largest category of spending\n• Students who plan monthly budgets — 28% — usually better savers\n(Adapted from onefamily.com)", rows = listOf("Saving money for university", "Saving to buy a new phone", "Starting a business"), rowKeys = listOf(1, 0, 1)),
        Question("rb22", "According to the text, which of the following actions support smart money management for students? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("Tracking daily expenses using a notebook or app", "Spending more money than the monthly budget allows", "Setting financial goals for the short and long term", "Borrowing money whenever there is not enough left", "Dividing money into saving, spending, and emergency funds"), 0, "Teks menyarankan mencatat pengeluaran (A), menetapkan tujuan jangka pendek dan panjang (C), dan membagi uang untuk ditabung, dibelanjakan, dan cadangan masalah tak terduga (E).", passage = "Why Teenagers Should Learn to Manage Their Money\n\nMany young people today often spend money on things they like, such as snacks, clothes, or fun activities. But learning to handle money from a young age is very important. Good money habits can help students make a better future.\nHaving a clear plan for the future can show teenagers how to use their money. Students should think about short-term goals, like getting a new phone, and long-term goals, like saving for college or starting a business. Writing these goals down can help students stay motivated and focused.\nA budget helps students see where their money goes every month. It's important to list basic needs like food and travel, and also other costs like clothes or presents. A budget makes it easier to decide how much money to save, spend, or keep for unexpected problems.\nSometimes, students don't know how much they spend on small things. Keeping track of spending with notes or apps can help students understand their habits. This helps them stay within their budget and make changes if needed.\nTeenagers should also learn the difference between saving money and investing money. Saving is safer but slower, while investing has more risk but can earn more money. Knowing both can help students choose the best way for their money goals.\nTo sum up, students who learn to plan, budget, track, and understand saving choices are more ready for the future. That is why learning about money should start early and be done often.\n\nTable 1. How do students manage their money?\n• Students who save regularly — 45% — save at least 10% of allowance\n• Students who track expenses — 35% — use apps or notes\n• Students with financial education — 25% — have learned budgeting in class\n• Students who often borrow from friends — 30% — due to running out of money\n• Students who spend most on food & drinks — 50% — largest category of spending\n• Students who plan monthly budgets — 28% — usually better savers\n(Adapted from onefamily.com)", multi = setOf(0, 2, 4)),
        Question("rb23", "Who is most likely to be the target audience of this text? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("Teenagers who are learning to manage their money", "Parents looking for tips on how to control their children's spending", "Students who want to plan for their financial future", "High school readers who need to understand saving and budgeting", "Bankers and financial experts"), 0, "Teks ditujukan kepada remaja dan pelajar (A, C, D). Teks tidak memberi tips untuk orang tua atau ahli keuangan.", passage = "Why Teenagers Should Learn to Manage Their Money\n\nMany young people today often spend money on things they like, such as snacks, clothes, or fun activities. But learning to handle money from a young age is very important. Good money habits can help students make a better future.\nHaving a clear plan for the future can show teenagers how to use their money. Students should think about short-term goals, like getting a new phone, and long-term goals, like saving for college or starting a business. Writing these goals down can help students stay motivated and focused.\nA budget helps students see where their money goes every month. It's important to list basic needs like food and travel, and also other costs like clothes or presents. A budget makes it easier to decide how much money to save, spend, or keep for unexpected problems.\nSometimes, students don't know how much they spend on small things. Keeping track of spending with notes or apps can help students understand their habits. This helps them stay within their budget and make changes if needed.\nTeenagers should also learn the difference between saving money and investing money. Saving is safer but slower, while investing has more risk but can earn more money. Knowing both can help students choose the best way for their money goals.\nTo sum up, students who learn to plan, budget, track, and understand saving choices are more ready for the future. That is why learning about money should start early and be done often.\n\nTable 1. How do students manage their money?\n• Students who save regularly — 45% — save at least 10% of allowance\n• Students who track expenses — 35% — use apps or notes\n• Students with financial education — 25% — have learned budgeting in class\n• Students who often borrow from friends — 30% — due to running out of money\n• Students who spend most on food & drinks — 50% — largest category of spending\n• Students who plan monthly budgets — 28% — usually better savers\n(Adapted from onefamily.com)", multi = setOf(0, 2, 3)),
        Question("rb24", "Which information would make the text more informative about student spending habits?", listOf("A paragraph about the history of financial education in schools", "A table showing common monthly high school students expenses", "A graph comparing saving habits between teenagers and adults", "A chart listing popular entertainment choices among students", "A paragraph about students' experiences in managing budget"), 1, "Kebiasaan belanja paling jelas digambarkan dengan data pengeluaran bulanan siswa.", passage = "Why Teenagers Should Learn to Manage Their Money\n\nMany young people today often spend money on things they like, such as snacks, clothes, or fun activities. But learning to handle money from a young age is very important. Good money habits can help students make a better future.\nHaving a clear plan for the future can show teenagers how to use their money. Students should think about short-term goals, like getting a new phone, and long-term goals, like saving for college or starting a business. Writing these goals down can help students stay motivated and focused.\nA budget helps students see where their money goes every month. It's important to list basic needs like food and travel, and also other costs like clothes or presents. A budget makes it easier to decide how much money to save, spend, or keep for unexpected problems.\nSometimes, students don't know how much they spend on small things. Keeping track of spending with notes or apps can help students understand their habits. This helps them stay within their budget and make changes if needed.\nTeenagers should also learn the difference between saving money and investing money. Saving is safer but slower, while investing has more risk but can earn more money. Knowing both can help students choose the best way for their money goals.\nTo sum up, students who learn to plan, budget, track, and understand saving choices are more ready for the future. That is why learning about money should start early and be done often.\n\nTable 1. How do students manage their money?\n• Students who save regularly — 45% — save at least 10% of allowance\n• Students who track expenses — 35% — use apps or notes\n• Students with financial education — 25% — have learned budgeting in class\n• Students who often borrow from friends — 30% — due to running out of money\n• Students who spend most on food & drinks — 50% — largest category of spending\n• Students who plan monthly budgets — 28% — usually better savers\n(Adapted from onefamily.com)"),
        Question("rb25", "Which of the following statements are supported by clear data or facts in the text and table? (Pilih lebih dari satu.)", listOf("45% of students save money regularly", "Tracking expenses can help understand spending habits", "Most students do not care about money at all", "Saving 10% of allowance is a good practice", "Spending on fun activities is always better than saving"), 0, "A ada di tabel dan B dinyatakan di paragraf 4. D adalah penilaian (opini), sedangkan C dan E tidak didukung data.", passage = "Why Teenagers Should Learn to Manage Their Money\n\nMany young people today often spend money on things they like, such as snacks, clothes, or fun activities. But learning to handle money from a young age is very important. Good money habits can help students make a better future.\nHaving a clear plan for the future can show teenagers how to use their money. Students should think about short-term goals, like getting a new phone, and long-term goals, like saving for college or starting a business. Writing these goals down can help students stay motivated and focused.\nA budget helps students see where their money goes every month. It's important to list basic needs like food and travel, and also other costs like clothes or presents. A budget makes it easier to decide how much money to save, spend, or keep for unexpected problems.\nSometimes, students don't know how much they spend on small things. Keeping track of spending with notes or apps can help students understand their habits. This helps them stay within their budget and make changes if needed.\nTeenagers should also learn the difference between saving money and investing money. Saving is safer but slower, while investing has more risk but can earn more money. Knowing both can help students choose the best way for their money goals.\nTo sum up, students who learn to plan, budget, track, and understand saving choices are more ready for the future. That is why learning about money should start early and be done often.\n\nTable 1. How do students manage their money?\n• Students who save regularly — 45% — save at least 10% of allowance\n• Students who track expenses — 35% — use apps or notes\n• Students with financial education — 25% — have learned budgeting in class\n• Students who often borrow from friends — 30% — due to running out of money\n• Students who spend most on food & drinks — 50% — largest category of spending\n• Students who plan monthly budgets — 28% — usually better savers\n(Adapted from onefamily.com)", multi = setOf(0, 1)),
    )

    private fun latihanBigRaw() = listOf(
        Question("lb1", "The communicative purpose of this text is ....", listOf("To describe a particular animal", "To share an amusing incident with others", "To present two points of view about an issue", "To inform the readers about the beauty of Dolgy", "To retell events for the purpose of informing and entertaining"), 0, "Descriptive text bertujuan menggambarkan satu benda/hewan tertentu, di sini anjing bernama Dolgy.", passage = "My Pet\n\nI have a pet. It is a dog and I call it Dolgy. Dolgy is a Chinese breed. It is small, fluffy and cute. It has got thick black fur. When I cuddle it, this fur feels soft. Dolgy doesn't like bones. Every day it eats soft food like steamed rice, fish, or bread. Every morning I give him milk and bread. When I am at school, Dolgy plays with my rabbit. They get along well, and never fight maybe because Dolgy doesn't bark a lot. It treats the other animals in our house gently and never eats shoes. Dolgy is really a sweet and friendly animal."),
        Question("lb2", "What does Dolgy look like?", listOf("Big, fierce and cute", "Big, fluffy and fierce", "Small, fierce and stink", "Small, fluffy and cute", "Small, fluffy and stink"), 3, "Teks: \"It is small, fluffy and cute.\"", passage = "My Pet\n\nI have a pet. It is a dog and I call it Dolgy. Dolgy is a Chinese breed. It is small, fluffy and cute. It has got thick black fur. When I cuddle it, this fur feels soft. Dolgy doesn't like bones. Every day it eats soft food like steamed rice, fish, or bread. Every morning I give him milk and bread. When I am at school, Dolgy plays with my rabbit. They get along well, and never fight maybe because Dolgy doesn't bark a lot. It treats the other animals in our house gently and never eats shoes. Dolgy is really a sweet and friendly animal."),
        Question("lb3", "Whom does Dolgy play with when the writer goes to school?", listOf("The writer's sister", "The writer's mother", "The writer's cat", "The writer's other dog", "The writer's rabbit"), 4, "Teks: \"When I am at school, Dolgy plays with my rabbit.\"", passage = "My Pet\n\nI have a pet. It is a dog and I call it Dolgy. Dolgy is a Chinese breed. It is small, fluffy and cute. It has got thick black fur. When I cuddle it, this fur feels soft. Dolgy doesn't like bones. Every day it eats soft food like steamed rice, fish, or bread. Every morning I give him milk and bread. When I am at school, Dolgy plays with my rabbit. They get along well, and never fight maybe because Dolgy doesn't bark a lot. It treats the other animals in our house gently and never eats shoes. Dolgy is really a sweet and friendly animal."),
        Question("lb4", "What is the communicative purpose of the text?", listOf("To present two points of view about Paris", "To explain Paris, the capital city of France", "To describe Paris", "To retell Paris, the capital of France", "To persuade the readers to go to Paris"), 2, "Teks menggambarkan ciri-ciri satu kota tertentu → descriptive text, tujuannya to describe Paris.", passage = "Paris\n\nParis is the capital city of France. It is also one of the most beautiful and famous cities in the world.\nParis is called the city of light. It is also an international fashion center. What stylish women are wearing in Paris will be worn by women all over the world. Paris is also famous as a world center of education. For instance, it is the headquarters of UNESCO, the United Nations Educational, Scientific, and Cultural Organization.\nThere are many other famous places in Paris, such as the famous museum the Louvre as well as the cathedral of Notre Dame. However, the most famous landmark in this city must be the Eiffel Tower.\nParis is named after a group of people called the Parisii. They built a small village on an island in the middle of the Seine River about two thousand years ago. This island is called Île de la Cité. It is where Notre Dame is located. Today around eight million people live in the Paris area."),
        Question("lb5", "What are the famous places in Paris?", listOf("Pisa Tower and the Louvre museum", "The cathedral of Notre Dame and Pisa Tower", "The Louvre museum, Eiffel Tower, and Pisa Tower", "The Louvre museum, Eiffel Tower, and the cathedral of Notre Dame", "Pisa Tower and Eiffel Tower"), 3, "Menara Pisa ada di Italia, bukan Paris. Teks menyebut Louvre, Notre Dame, dan Menara Eiffel.", passage = "Paris\n\nParis is the capital city of France. It is also one of the most beautiful and famous cities in the world.\nParis is called the city of light. It is also an international fashion center. What stylish women are wearing in Paris will be worn by women all over the world. Paris is also famous as a world center of education. For instance, it is the headquarters of UNESCO, the United Nations Educational, Scientific, and Cultural Organization.\nThere are many other famous places in Paris, such as the famous museum the Louvre as well as the cathedral of Notre Dame. However, the most famous landmark in this city must be the Eiffel Tower.\nParis is named after a group of people called the Parisii. They built a small village on an island in the middle of the Seine River about two thousand years ago. This island is called Île de la Cité. It is where Notre Dame is located. Today around eight million people live in the Paris area."),
        Question("lb6", "How many people live in the Paris area?", listOf("Eight million people", "Seven million people", "Six million people", "Five million people", "Four million people"), 0, "Kalimat terakhir: \"Today around eight million people live in the Paris area.\"", passage = "Paris\n\nParis is the capital city of France. It is also one of the most beautiful and famous cities in the world.\nParis is called the city of light. It is also an international fashion center. What stylish women are wearing in Paris will be worn by women all over the world. Paris is also famous as a world center of education. For instance, it is the headquarters of UNESCO, the United Nations Educational, Scientific, and Cultural Organization.\nThere are many other famous places in Paris, such as the famous museum the Louvre as well as the cathedral of Notre Dame. However, the most famous landmark in this city must be the Eiffel Tower.\nParis is named after a group of people called the Parisii. They built a small village on an island in the middle of the Seine River about two thousand years ago. This island is called Île de la Cité. It is where Notre Dame is located. Today around eight million people live in the Paris area."),
        Question("lb7", "According to the passage, we know that Peter is ...", listOf("The writer's youngest brother", "The writer's elder brother", "A naughty boy", "A friendly boy"), 0, "\"Peter is the youngest in our family… four years younger than me\" → adik bungsu penulis.", passage = "Peter is the youngest in our family. He is fourteen years old and four years younger than me. He has long, straight hair, bright eyes and a friendly smile. Sometimes he is rather naughty at home, but he usually does what he is asked to do.\nPeter is interested in sports very much, and at school, he plays football and tennis. He is the best badminton player in our family."),
        Question("lb8", "The writer is ...... years old.", listOf("Fourteen", "Sixteen", "Eighteen", "Nineteen"), 2, "Peter 14 tahun dan empat tahun lebih muda dari penulis: 14 + 4 = 18.", passage = "Peter is the youngest in our family. He is fourteen years old and four years younger than me. He has long, straight hair, bright eyes and a friendly smile. Sometimes he is rather naughty at home, but he usually does what he is asked to do.\nPeter is interested in sports very much, and at school, he plays football and tennis. He is the best badminton player in our family."),
        Question("lb9", "\"Peter is interested in sports very much.\" The phrase \"is interested in sports very much\" can be replaced by ......", listOf("Dislikes sport", "Really likes sport", "Hates sport very much", "Finds sport not really entertaining"), 1, "Interested in … very much = sangat menyukai.", passage = "Peter is the youngest in our family. He is fourteen years old and four years younger than me. He has long, straight hair, bright eyes and a friendly smile. Sometimes he is rather naughty at home, but he usually does what he is asked to do.\nPeter is interested in sports very much, and at school, he plays football and tennis. He is the best badminton player in our family."),
        Question("lb10", "\"But he usually does what he is asked to do.\" The phrase means ....", listOf("He does anything he wants", "He always asks", "He is lazy", "He is diligent"), 3, "Biasanya mengerjakan apa yang diminta → rajin dan patuh (diligent).", passage = "Peter is the youngest in our family. He is fourteen years old and four years younger than me. He has long, straight hair, bright eyes and a friendly smile. Sometimes he is rather naughty at home, but he usually does what he is asked to do.\nPeter is interested in sports very much, and at school, he plays football and tennis. He is the best badminton player in our family."),
        Question("lb11", "What is the text about?", listOf("Telling about someone's hobby", "Introducing oneself", "Telling about someone's profession", "Introducing someone"), 1, "Hannah menulis surat untuk memperkenalkan dirinya kepada Alia.", passage = "Hello, Alia! Let me introduce myself. My name is Hannah.\nI know your name from my friend, Caroline. She told me that you sent her an email telling her that you would like to have more pen pals from the US. I'd really like to be your e-pal. You sound really cool!\nI guess I'd better tell you something about myself. I'm 16 years old and I attend Thomas Edison High School here in Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA. I have two brothers and two half sisters and I'm the middle child. My father died a few years ago so my mother runs the house and the family business. My father was a barista.\nI have lots of hobbies. I like music, mostly classical music and folk music, but I don't play an instrument. I like sports, especially tennis and basketball. At school I'm in the basketball team and I spend most of my extra-curricular time playing basketball. My favorite subjects at school are art and geography. I think I'd like to become a park ranger when I graduate, perhaps work for the National Park Service.\nI don't like reading but I love drawing and painting. How about you? Please drop me a line, Alia! Can't wait to hear from you!\n\nHannah"),
        Question("lb12", "What is the main idea of the third paragraph?", listOf("Kinds of activities that Hannah dislikes", "Hannah told that she knew Alia from Caroline", "Hannah has many hobbies", "Hannah told Alia about her family and herself"), 3, "Paragraf 3 berisi umur, sekolah, saudara, dan keluarga Hannah.", passage = "Hello, Alia! Let me introduce myself. My name is Hannah.\nI know your name from my friend, Caroline. She told me that you sent her an email telling her that you would like to have more pen pals from the US. I'd really like to be your e-pal. You sound really cool!\nI guess I'd better tell you something about myself. I'm 16 years old and I attend Thomas Edison High School here in Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA. I have two brothers and two half sisters and I'm the middle child. My father died a few years ago so my mother runs the house and the family business. My father was a barista.\nI have lots of hobbies. I like music, mostly classical music and folk music, but I don't play an instrument. I like sports, especially tennis and basketball. At school I'm in the basketball team and I spend most of my extra-curricular time playing basketball. My favorite subjects at school are art and geography. I think I'd like to become a park ranger when I graduate, perhaps work for the National Park Service.\nI don't like reading but I love drawing and painting. How about you? Please drop me a line, Alia! Can't wait to hear from you!\n\nHannah"),
        Question("lb13", "Which is NOT correct based on the text above?", listOf("Caroline introduces Hannah to Alia", "Thomas Edison High School is Hannah's school", "Hannah has five siblings", "Hannah doesn't like reading"), 2, "Hannah punya dua saudara laki-laki dan dua saudara tiri perempuan = empat, bukan lima.", passage = "Hello, Alia! Let me introduce myself. My name is Hannah.\nI know your name from my friend, Caroline. She told me that you sent her an email telling her that you would like to have more pen pals from the US. I'd really like to be your e-pal. You sound really cool!\nI guess I'd better tell you something about myself. I'm 16 years old and I attend Thomas Edison High School here in Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA. I have two brothers and two half sisters and I'm the middle child. My father died a few years ago so my mother runs the house and the family business. My father was a barista.\nI have lots of hobbies. I like music, mostly classical music and folk music, but I don't play an instrument. I like sports, especially tennis and basketball. At school I'm in the basketball team and I spend most of my extra-curricular time playing basketball. My favorite subjects at school are art and geography. I think I'd like to become a park ranger when I graduate, perhaps work for the National Park Service.\nI don't like reading but I love drawing and painting. How about you? Please drop me a line, Alia! Can't wait to hear from you!\n\nHannah"),
        Question("lb14", "What does Hannah want for her future?", listOf("A musician", "A basketball player", "An artist", "A park ranger"), 3, "\"I think I'd like to become a park ranger when I graduate.\"", passage = "Hello, Alia! Let me introduce myself. My name is Hannah.\nI know your name from my friend, Caroline. She told me that you sent her an email telling her that you would like to have more pen pals from the US. I'd really like to be your e-pal. You sound really cool!\nI guess I'd better tell you something about myself. I'm 16 years old and I attend Thomas Edison High School here in Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA. I have two brothers and two half sisters and I'm the middle child. My father died a few years ago so my mother runs the house and the family business. My father was a barista.\nI have lots of hobbies. I like music, mostly classical music and folk music, but I don't play an instrument. I like sports, especially tennis and basketball. At school I'm in the basketball team and I spend most of my extra-curricular time playing basketball. My favorite subjects at school are art and geography. I think I'd like to become a park ranger when I graduate, perhaps work for the National Park Service.\nI don't like reading but I love drawing and painting. How about you? Please drop me a line, Alia! Can't wait to hear from you!\n\nHannah"),
        Question("lb15", "Why was the mother very angry? Because ...", listOf("Her daughters were crying and found her", "The earth began to shake and started to erupt", "Batara Guru Sahala broke his promise", "Batara Guru Sahala was angry"), 2, "Paragraf terakhir: \"The mother was very angry. Batara Guru Sahala broke his promise.\"", passage = "The Legend of Toba Lake\n\nOnce upon a time, there was a handsome man named Batara Guru Sahala, who enjoyed fishing so much. One day, he caught a fish. He was surprised to find out that the fish could talk. The fish begged him to set it free.\nBatara Guru Sahala could not bear it. He set the fish free. As soon as it was free, the fish changed into a very beautiful woman. Batara Guru Sahala fell in love with that fish woman and wanted to marry her. Batara Guru Sahala promised to keep the secret that she had been a fish and would never tell anybody about it.\nThey were married happily. They had two daughters. One day Batara Guru Sahala got very angry with his daughters. He could not control his temper. He shouted angrily and said the word \"fish\" to his daughters. The daughters were crying. They found their mother and told her about it.\nThe mother was very angry. Batara Guru Sahala broke his promise. The mother was shouting angrily, then the earth formed a very big hole. People believed that the big hole became a lake. Today the lake is known as Toba Lake."),
        Question("lb16", "What is the main idea of the fourth paragraph?", listOf("How Toba Lake was formed", "The daughters found their mother", "Their daughters were crying", "Batara Guru Sahala had two daughters"), 0, "Paragraf 4 menceritakan terbentuknya lubang besar yang menjadi Danau Toba.", passage = "The Legend of Toba Lake\n\nOnce upon a time, there was a handsome man named Batara Guru Sahala, who enjoyed fishing so much. One day, he caught a fish. He was surprised to find out that the fish could talk. The fish begged him to set it free.\nBatara Guru Sahala could not bear it. He set the fish free. As soon as it was free, the fish changed into a very beautiful woman. Batara Guru Sahala fell in love with that fish woman and wanted to marry her. Batara Guru Sahala promised to keep the secret that she had been a fish and would never tell anybody about it.\nThey were married happily. They had two daughters. One day Batara Guru Sahala got very angry with his daughters. He could not control his temper. He shouted angrily and said the word \"fish\" to his daughters. The daughters were crying. They found their mother and told her about it.\nThe mother was very angry. Batara Guru Sahala broke his promise. The mother was shouting angrily, then the earth formed a very big hole. People believed that the big hole became a lake. Today the lake is known as Toba Lake."),
        Question("lb17", "What can you learn from the text above? We should ...", listOf("Promise to our wife", "Promise to our husband", "Break our promise", "Keep our promise"), 3, "Bencana terjadi karena Sahala melanggar janji → kita harus menepati janji.", passage = "The Legend of Toba Lake\n\nOnce upon a time, there was a handsome man named Batara Guru Sahala, who enjoyed fishing so much. One day, he caught a fish. He was surprised to find out that the fish could talk. The fish begged him to set it free.\nBatara Guru Sahala could not bear it. He set the fish free. As soon as it was free, the fish changed into a very beautiful woman. Batara Guru Sahala fell in love with that fish woman and wanted to marry her. Batara Guru Sahala promised to keep the secret that she had been a fish and would never tell anybody about it.\nThey were married happily. They had two daughters. One day Batara Guru Sahala got very angry with his daughters. He could not control his temper. He shouted angrily and said the word \"fish\" to his daughters. The daughters were crying. They found their mother and told her about it.\nThe mother was very angry. Batara Guru Sahala broke his promise. The mother was shouting angrily, then the earth formed a very big hole. People believed that the big hole became a lake. Today the lake is known as Toba Lake."),
        Question("lb18", "Why did Roro Anteng and Joko Seger have to sacrifice their youngest son?", listOf("The youngest son was a noble man", "The son could stop the eruption", "They had promised to do that", "They had 25 children already"), 2, "Doa mereka dikabulkan dengan syarat mengorbankan anak bungsu; itu janji mereka.", passage = "Once upon a time, Roro Anteng and Joko Seger lived at the foot of Mount Bromo. After six years of marriage, they had not had any children. They prayed and pleaded to the Gods for children. Their prayer was granted on one condition: they should sacrifice their youngest son to the Bromo crater.\nAfter some time, Roro Anteng gave birth to a child, and it happened every year until they had 25 children. They lived happily and forgot about the agreement. Mount Bromo erupted, signaling that the Gods asked the couple to fulfill their promise. But they didn't want their youngest son, Raden Kusuma, to be sacrificed to the crater.\nRaden Kusuma learned about the deal his parents had made. Meanwhile the lava from the crater had made the people living near the mountain suffer. Since Raden Kusuma was a kind and noble man, he didn't want his siblings and other people to suffer because of him. Therefore he went to Mount Bromo and sacrificed himself to the crater. The eruption suddenly stopped.\nAfter that day, the Tengger people have given offerings to the crater, as Raden Kusuma had sacrificed himself before."),
        Question("lb19", "What is the main idea of paragraph 3?", listOf("The eruption of the mount stopped instantly", "Raden Kusuma sacrificed himself", "The crater of Mount Bromo was dangerous", "Raden Kusuma made people angry"), 1, "Paragraf 3 berpusat pada Raden Kusuma yang mengorbankan dirinya.", passage = "Once upon a time, Roro Anteng and Joko Seger lived at the foot of Mount Bromo. After six years of marriage, they had not had any children. They prayed and pleaded to the Gods for children. Their prayer was granted on one condition: they should sacrifice their youngest son to the Bromo crater.\nAfter some time, Roro Anteng gave birth to a child, and it happened every year until they had 25 children. They lived happily and forgot about the agreement. Mount Bromo erupted, signaling that the Gods asked the couple to fulfill their promise. But they didn't want their youngest son, Raden Kusuma, to be sacrificed to the crater.\nRaden Kusuma learned about the deal his parents had made. Meanwhile the lava from the crater had made the people living near the mountain suffer. Since Raden Kusuma was a kind and noble man, he didn't want his siblings and other people to suffer because of him. Therefore he went to Mount Bromo and sacrificed himself to the crater. The eruption suddenly stopped.\nAfter that day, the Tengger people have given offerings to the crater, as Raden Kusuma had sacrificed himself before."),
        Question("lb20", "The moral of the story is ....", listOf("Keeping our promise is unnecessary", "Parents must not promise to do anything", "All parents love their children", "We have to fulfill our promise"), 3, "Letusan terjadi karena janji dilupakan → kita harus menepati janji.", passage = "Once upon a time, Roro Anteng and Joko Seger lived at the foot of Mount Bromo. After six years of marriage, they had not had any children. They prayed and pleaded to the Gods for children. Their prayer was granted on one condition: they should sacrifice their youngest son to the Bromo crater.\nAfter some time, Roro Anteng gave birth to a child, and it happened every year until they had 25 children. They lived happily and forgot about the agreement. Mount Bromo erupted, signaling that the Gods asked the couple to fulfill their promise. But they didn't want their youngest son, Raden Kusuma, to be sacrificed to the crater.\nRaden Kusuma learned about the deal his parents had made. Meanwhile the lava from the crater had made the people living near the mountain suffer. Since Raden Kusuma was a kind and noble man, he didn't want his siblings and other people to suffer because of him. Therefore he went to Mount Bromo and sacrificed himself to the crater. The eruption suddenly stopped.\nAfter that day, the Tengger people have given offerings to the crater, as Raden Kusuma had sacrificed himself before."),
    )

